  (RUNTIME-EXCEPTION.md).
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  HookIO.pcpp - the HookIO unit: `import HookIO;` lets C stdio open CustomIO
  streams by path.

  Register an IO or an IOSource and get back its prefix, `io://<n>`. A path
  that starts with that prefix then names the registered stream wherever C
  code opens a file: fopen("io://<n>/...") in the program, or inside any C /
  C++ library linked into it (raylib, stb_vorbis, ...), opens the stream
  instead of a file on disk. The hooks are HookABI link-time hooks, so they
  bind every call in the final link; a DLL / .so loaded at run time is not
  reached.

    io://<n>/<name>   a registered IO. <name> is never looked up: it is there
                      for the caller, which may pick a decoder by its
                      extension (io://3/song.ogg). `io://<n>` alone opens it
                      too. Every open gets its own handle with its own
                      position; closing a handle never closes the IO.
    io://<n>/<entry>  a registered IOSource: the entry, opened with
                      IOSourceOpen (relative, `/` separated). The handle owns
                      that IO and closes it.

  Any other path goes to the C runtime untouched, except while a path source
  is set (SetIOPathSource for the program, SetIOThreadPathSource for one
  thread, which takes the program's place on that thread): a plain path that
  source holds opens and answers as its entry, any other still goes to the
  C runtime. `io://` is matched exactly (lowercase); `<n>` is the decimal
  number RegisterIO / RegisterIOSource gave, without leading zeros. A
  leading `./` (on Windows `.\` too), once or more, before `io://` names the
  same path: a C library that joins a folder and a name writes a folder with
  no root that way (raylib does for a model's textures).

  A handle is HookIO's own object, never a C runtime FILE: it is valid only
  with the names HookIO hooks. On Linux it begins as glibc's FILE does (its
  flags and empty buffer areas), so glibc's inline getc_unlocked /
  putc_unlocked / feof_unlocked / ferror_unlocked, which read those fields
  straight, fall through to the hooked __uflow / __overflow and see the
  handle's end and error state. freopen (Linux also freopen64) reopens a
  handle in place, on a virtual path or a disk file (the handle then holds
  the disk file through CustomIO's file IOs, every fopen mode). A real FILE
  reopened onto a virtual path is the C runtime's and fails as it does
  (ENOENT): the CRT owns that object. The names HookIO hooks are the open
  family (Windows fopen, fopen_s, _wfopen; Linux fopen, fopen64), freopen,
  fclose, the
  lock-free forms (glibc's *_unlocked, ucrt's *_nolock), the stream lock
  calls (Linux flockfile, funlockfile, ftrylockfile; Windows _lock_file,
  _unlock_file: nothing on a handle) and the stream family:
  fread, fwrite, fseek, ftell, fseeko64, ftello64, rewind, feof, ferror,
  clearerr, fflush, fgetc, getc, fgets, fputc, putc, fputs, fputws, fputwc,
  putwc, ungetc, setbuf, setvbuf, fileno, fprintf; Windows also _fileno,
  _fseeki64, _ftelli64, _lock_file, _unlock_file, __stdio_common_vfprintf
  (the printf family), __stdio_common_vfscanf (the scanf family) and
  __mingw_fprintf; Linux also fwide, fseeko, ftello, vfprintf, fscanf,
  __isoc99_fscanf, vfscanf, __isoc99_vfscanf and glibc's fortified names
  (what C built with -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE calls): __fprintf_chk,
  __vfprintf_chk, __fgets_chk, __fgets_unlocked_chk, __fread_chk and
  __fread_unlocked_chk, each applying glibc's own check (the printf flag
  through glibc's __vsnprintf_chk, the buffer sizes as glibc does) before
  the handle's plain path. FileIO gives the IO behind a handle (nil for a
  real FILE).
  scripts\hookabi\gen_bindlist.py --complete checks a linked program: none
  of its imports may take a FILE*.

  The query family answers a virtual path as fopen would find it: Windows
  _access, the oldnames access, stat64i32 (mingw's stat) and
  GetFileAttributesA; Linux access, stat and stat64 (a C++ stat is stat64 by
  the headers' asm name, a C one the plain stat: both are defined). The file
  exists when an open of it can succeed (under a registered IO's prefix every
  name is that IO; a source entry when IOSourceExists says so), its size is
  the IO's, it is writable when a write open that empties nothing ("r+")
  succeeds, never executable, with no times (0); a missing one is ENOENT
  (GetFileAttributesA: ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND). Directories are not answered
  (CustomIO has no directory query): a source's root is a missing file.

  A scan (fscanf and the rest of its family) on a handle runs the C
  runtime's own scan over a stand-in FILE holding the handle's next bytes
  (Linux a fopencookie FILE, Windows a std::tmpfile, deleted on close), then
  moves the handle on by exactly what the scan used: the place and feof
  after a scan are what a real file of the same bytes gives, except in one
  case, an inherent limit of the stand-in. Windows, under a DBCS code page
  set by setlocale: when a lead byte matches a lead byte of the format's
  literal text and the byte after it does not match, ucrt's scan ungets
  both. A real FILE refuses the second unget when the lead byte was the last
  byte of a 4096-byte fill, so the lead byte stays used and the place is one
  past it; anywhere else it takes both (measured, code page 932). The
  stand-in's fills start at the scan's start, not where the handle's would,
  so in that case the place after the scan can differ from a real file's by
  that one byte.

  A handle reads through a model of the target C runtime's own FILE, its
  rules as the runtime's source states them (Windows: the Windows Kits ucrt;
  Linux: glibc 2.39 libio), so every read form, ungetc, fseek and ftell give
  what that runtime gives on a real file of the same bytes, ungot bytes and
  buffer boundaries included. Windows, every mode: ucrt's buffer (4096-byte
  fills, 512 for the first one after an fseek of a read-only stream, large
  freads straight past the buffer, an fseek inside the buffer of a read-only
  binary stream only moving in it), ungetc into that buffer (refused when
  the next byte is already the buffer's first with bytes left, as for a
  second ungetc right after an fseek, and on a stream that has not read
  unless it is an update stream that writes), ucrt's ftell (no sign check).
  Linux: glibc's buffer (4096 bytes, the size glibc gives a file whose
  st_blksize is the one this unit's stat reports), its backup area for an
  ungot byte that does not step back into the buffer, glibc's ftell (which
  counts no ungot byte before the first read and can be negative after
  several), glibc's fseek (block-aligned read-ahead, and the backup area
  dropped first only on a byte-oriented stream). Writes go through the same
  model, buffered and flushed as that runtime does it: Windows, ucrt's
  buffer filled by fputc / fwrite (a write of at least a buffer goes
  straight to the IO in whole buffers), flushed when full, by fflush,
  fseek, rewind, setvbuf and fclose, a read-to-write turn without a seek
  allowed only at the end, and ucrt's write-mode ftell; Linux, glibc's put
  area (overflow, xsputn with its line-buffered and whole-block rules, the
  descriptor stepped back over read-ahead before a write lands, write-mode
  ftell, an appending stream's ftell going to the end). printf hands its
  text over as each runtime's own does (ucrt: one fputc per byte; glibc:
  straight into the put area, else a 128-byte stage). Every open handle's
  unflushed bytes are flushed at exit, as both runtimes flush their
  streams. Where a runtime's answer to a read right after a write, or a
  write right after a read, with no fflush or fseek between (which C
  leaves undefined) is to lose, misplace or invent bytes, a handle behaves
  exactly as the runtime does when the caller makes the fflush or fseek C
  requires there. glibc's ungetc in put mode mixes its areas even after an
  fflush; there a handle reads the ungot bytes, then the file at the
  caller's place.
  feof is set by a read that stops at the IO's end (and, on Linux, ends
  every later read until cleared, as C99 wants), ferror by any other
  failure (errno EIO), a read on a write-only handle fails as the
  runtime's does (ucrt's _filbuf: ferror, errno untouched; a read straight
  from the descriptor, and glibc: EBADF; glibc's fgetc / fread hand back
  ungot bytes first, its fscanf refuses up front without ferror), fread /
  fwrite counts whose product overflows follow the
  runtime (ucrt: EINVAL and 0, no ferror; glibc: the product wraps), and
  a write on a read-only one fails as the runtime's does (EBADF; ucrt's
  fputc into bytes read ahead succeeds, replacing the next of them, and its
  fwrite there writes nothing). fseek may go past the end where the IO
  allows it, never before the start (EINVAL), and on Windows clears feof
  even when it fails, as ucrt's fseek does; ftell past what a long holds
  (32 bits on Windows) is -1 with EINVAL, as ucrt's; _ftelli64 / ftello64
  hold any place. fileno is -1 (EBADF: no descriptor). setvbuf / setbuf
  act as the target CRT's on its FILE model: the buffer's size (ucrt rounds
  it down to even; glibc ignores the size when no array is given and uses
  its own), the caller's array used as the buffer and filled as a real
  FILE fills it, unbuffered (ucrt: 2 bytes per fill, glibc: 1), the
  argument checks (ucrt: -1 with EINVAL; glibc: EOF, errno untouched), and
  what becomes of bytes read ahead or ungot: ucrt drops them where the
  descriptor is, glibc steps the descriptor back first. glibc's line or
  unbuffered stream flushes a line-buffered stdout before each fill. One
  exception: setvbuf on glibc while ungot bytes sit in its backup area
  leaves glibc reading freed memory (measured; fclose then aborts), so
  there a handle keeps the stream as the caller stands in it: the ungot
  bytes first, then the file from the caller's place. fflush on a reading
  handle does what the target CRT's does: glibc steps the descriptor back
  over the bytes read ahead (ungot ones dropped), ucrt leaves it alone.
  fflush(nil) flushes every handle too.

  Wide output (fputwc, putwc, fputws) writes what the target CRT writes on
  a real FILE of the same mode under the same locale. Windows (ucrt): a
  binary handle takes the 2 raw bytes of each wchar_t through the buffer; a
  text handle converts each one by the current locale (wctomb_s), byte by
  byte through fputc's path ("\n" becomes "\r\n"), and a character the
  locale cannot convert fails with WEOF / EOF and wctomb's errno; fwide is
  the toolchain's own (it never reads the FILE). Linux (glibc): a stream's
  orientation is set by its first call that sets one, as glibc sets it
  (fputs, fwrite, a narrow printf or scan and a narrow refill make it
  byte-oriented and refuse a wide stream; fputwc and fputws make it wide
  and refuse a byte one; fwide asks or sets it; putwc, fputc, ungetc and a
  read out of the buffer check nothing). A wide stream keeps glibc's wide
  buffer and converts it at each flush through the locale's charset, with
  transliteration, as chosen when it turned wide; ftell, fseek and fflush
  count and step through it as glibc's wide stream does.

  Modes are parsed exactly as the target CRT's fopen parses them, so a mode
  string HookIO refuses is one the C runtime refuses, with the same EINVAL.
  Windows (ucrt's rules): leading spaces, r, w or a, then any of + (once),
  b or t (one of them, once), c or n (one of them, once), S or R (one of
  them, once), T (once), D (once), N, x (only with w) and spaces, or a comma
  starting ccs=UTF-8 / UTF-16LE / UNICODE. Linux (glibc's rules): r, w or a
  first, then at most six more characters up to a comma: + and x count,
  every other character is ignored. r opens for reading, w empties or
  creates, a creates when missing and writes every byte at the end; + adds
  the other direction (r+ the file must exist, w+ empties or creates, a+
  reads anywhere and still writes at the end). ucrt starts every a / a+
  handle at 0 (its descriptor goes to the end at each write); glibc starts
  a at the end and a+ at 0. x (w on Windows, w or a on Linux) fails with
  EEXIST when the target exists, which a registered IO always does. The
  hints (c, n, S, R, T, N; glibc's m, c, e) change nothing an IO can show.
  Windows D (glibc ignores it) removes an IOSource entry when its last D
  handle closes, or at exit while one is still open (IOSourceRemove), as
  the OS deletes a delete-on-close file; on a registered IO it removes
  nothing (there is no file behind it). As ucrt's DELETE access and its
  share rules: a D open of an entry the source cannot remove (a zip) or of
  an existing entry that does not open for writing (a read-only file)
  fails with EACCES, and a D handle and a plain one on the same entry
  refuse each other (EACCES); several D handles may share one.
  Not built yet, refused with EINVAL although the CRT accepts it: a ccs=
  encoding (Linux ",ccs=").
  w / w+ empty the IO through
  IOTruncate, as the C runtime's open truncates a file (every other handle
  on it sees it emptied); an IO that cannot write refuses with EACCES, one
  that cannot be emptied with what each CRT reports for a file it cannot
  truncate (Windows EINVAL, Linux EPERM). w+ / a+ on an IOSource entry
  that is missing create it first (IOSourceOpen Write / Append), then open it
  for reading and writing.

  Text mode (Windows), as ucrt's text-mode FILE: a mode with t, or with
  neither b nor t while _get_fmode says _O_TEXT (the default). Reads deliver
  every "\r\n" as "\n" (a '\r' before anything else stays, also across the
  end of one read and the start of the next), and a Ctrl-Z (0x1A) ends the
  input; writes put "\r\n" for every "\n". ftell gives what ucrt's
  text-mode ftell gives, which is not always the IO's byte place (it
  estimates the untranslated size of the buffer), and the Ctrl-Z end lasts
  until an fseek, rewind, clearerr or ftell (ucrt's ftell moves the
  descriptor, which clears it). A text open with + drops one trailing
  Ctrl-Z from the IO, as ucrt's open does (IOTruncate; when the IO cannot
  be shortened the open still succeeds, the byte kept and errno EACCES, as
  ucrt's). On both targets a scan leaves the FILE model
  as the scan's own reads and its put-back look-ahead leave a real FILE's.
  Linux has no text mode: b and t change nothing there.

  A failed open returns nil (fopen_s: the error code) with errno set: ENOENT
  for a prefix that is not registered or an entry the source does not have,
  EACCES for an entry that exists but not in that mode, EEXIST for x on a
  target that exists, EINVAL for a refused mode, ENOMEM when out of memory.

  The registry never closes what was registered: unregister it first, close
  its handles, then close it. UnregisterIO leaves open handles as they are.
  Registering, unregistering, opening and closing are safe on several threads
  at once.

  HookIO defines fopen and the others itself, so a program that imports HookIO
  writes no hook of these names of its own.
==============================================================================*/

module unit HookIO;

import
  HookABI,
  CustomIO;

// Private: the registry and the handles, this unit's own translation unit.
// Helpers are named apart from the exported names (a body in the unit's
// namespace would find those first).
cpp source;

#include <algorithm>
#include <atomic>
#include <cctype>
#include <cerrno>
#include <climits>
#include <cstdarg>
#include <cstddef>
#include <cstdint>
#include <cstdio>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <cstring>
#include <cwchar>
#include <map>
#include <memory>
#include <mutex>
#include <new>
#include <string>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <utility>
#include <vector>

#include <sys/stat.h>
#if !defined(_WIN32)
#include <unistd.h>
// A wide stream's conversion (glibc's codecvt): iconv over the locale's
// charset, nl_langinfo(CODESET) at the time the stream turns wide
#include <iconv.h>
#include <langinfo.h>
#endif

#if defined(_WIN32)
#ifndef WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
#define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
#endif
#ifndef NOMINMAX
#define NOMINMAX
#endif
#include <windows.h>
// _get_fmode and _O_TEXT / _O_BINARY: a mode's default text mode
#include <fcntl.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
// mingw's headers make putwc a macro over fputwc; ucrt still exports
// putwc, which a call written (putwc)(...) or its address reaches, so the
// hook defines that name itself; getwc is the same over fgetwc
#undef putwc
#undef getwc
#endif

// CustomIO's own real file system work (a file IO's open, a folder source's
// queries) runs with this true on its thread (CustomIO.pcpp): HookIO's path
// source never redirects a path then, so those always mean the disk
namespace pcpp_customio_internal {
bool InFileSystemWork() noexcept;
}

namespace {

using HookIODoIO = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IO;
using HookIODoSource = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSource;
using HookIODoMode = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::FileMode;

// A registered stream: exactly one of Stream (RegisterIO) and Source
// (RegisterIOSource) is set. StreamLock (with Stream only) is the lock every
// handle on Stream shares: they share its position, so one handle's seek and
// read / write run whole.
struct HookIODoEntry
{
  HookIODoIO Stream = nullptr;
  HookIODoSource Source = nullptr;
  std::shared_ptr<std::mutex> StreamLock;
};

// An open handle, what a hooked open returns in place of a FILE*. Owned: the
// handle opened Stream itself (an IOSource entry) and closes it with the
// handle. Otherwise Stream is a registered IO that every handle on it shares.
// Position is the descriptor's place in Stream (the place after what the
// handle has taken from it, read ahead into Crt's buffer included); the
// caller's place is what the target CRT's ftell computes from Crt.
// StreamLock guards every field and every call on Stream; it is held while
// CustomIO runs, the registry lock never is.
// AtEnd / Failed are feof / ferror. Closed: fclose ran, under StreamLock (a
// call that raced it finds the handle gone). Text: opened in text mode
// (Windows only, see the unit header): Crt's reads translate, its ftell
// counts the translation. Crt: the state of the target CRT's own FILE
// (below), what every read form, ungetc, ftell and fseek run on, so that a
// handle gives what the CRT gives on a real file of the same bytes, ungot
// bytes and buffer boundaries included.

// A CRT FILE's main buffer: memory the model allocated (Owned) or the
// caller's own array handed to setvbuf / setbuf (External), which the CRT
// fills itself, so the caller sees the bytes there as a real FILE leaves
// them. The model never frees the caller's array. Copying the model copies
// the view, not the caller's bytes (HookIODoReadState keeps those itself).
struct HookIODoCrtBuffer
{
  std::vector<unsigned char> Owned;
  unsigned char* External = nullptr;
  std::int64_t Size = 0;

  unsigned char* data()
  {
    return (External != nullptr) ? External : Owned.data();
  }

  const unsigned char* data() const
  {
    return (External != nullptr) ? External : Owned.data();
  }

  unsigned char& operator[](const std::size_t AIndex)
  {
    return data()[AIndex];
  }

  const unsigned char& operator[](const std::size_t AIndex) const
  {
    return data()[AIndex];
  }

  std::int64_t size() const
  {
    return Size;
  }

  // ASize bytes of the model's own, all AValue
  void assign(const std::size_t ASize, const unsigned char AValue)
  {
    External = nullptr;
    Owned.assign(ASize, AValue);
    Size = static_cast<std::int64_t>(ASize);
  }

  // The caller's array of ASize bytes; the model's own memory is released
  void adopt(unsigned char* ABuffer, const std::int64_t ASize)
  {
    std::vector<unsigned char>().swap(Owned);
    External = ABuffer;
    Size = ASize;
  }

  void clear()
  {
    std::vector<unsigned char>().swap(Owned);
    External = nullptr;
    Size = 0;
  }
};

#if defined(_WIN32)
// Who made a ucrt FILE's buffer (corecrt_internal_stdio.h): Crt is
// _IOBUFFER_CRT (the first fill, ungetc or setvbuf with no array), User is
// _IOBUFFER_USER (the caller's array, setvbuf / setbuf), Single is
// _IOBUFFER_NONE (setvbuf _IONBF: the FILE's own 2-byte _charbuf).
enum class HookIODoUcrtBuffer
{
  Crt,
  User,
  Single
};

// The state of a ucrt FILE, text or binary (Windows Kits 10.0.26100 ucrt:
// stdio _filbuf.cpp, fread.cpp, ftell.cpp, fseek.cpp, ungetc.cpp; lowio
// read.cpp; writes: fwrite.cpp, fputc.cpp, _flsbuf.cpp, fflush.cpp, lowio
// write.cpp). The stdio side: Buffer holds the last fill (translated on a
// text handle); Ptr is the next byte in it (_ptr - _base), Count the bytes
// left (_cnt), BufferSize the size the next fill asks for (_bufsiz). While
// writing, [0, Ptr) are the bytes written and not yet flushed (untranslated:
// lowio translates them when they go) and Count is the room left;
// HasBuffer: the buffer exists (any _IOBUFFER_* bit), Kind says who made it.
// StreamRead / StreamWrite / StreamUpdate are _IOREAD / _IOWRITE /
// _IOUPDATE; StreamCtrlZ is _IOCTRLZ (a fill of a read-only stream met a
// Ctrl-Z; cleared only by setvbuf); SetvbufBuffer is _IOBUFFER_SETVBUF. The lowio
// side, over the handle's Position: LowEof is FEOFLAG (a text read met a
// Ctrl-Z; lowio reads nothing until a seek clears it), LowCrlf is FCRLF (the
// last text read began with '\n'). A binary handle never sets either.
struct HookIODoCrtModel
{
  HookIODoCrtBuffer Buffer;
  std::int64_t Ptr = 0;
  std::int64_t Count = 0;
  std::int64_t BufferSize = 0;
  bool HasBuffer = false;
  HookIODoUcrtBuffer Kind = HookIODoUcrtBuffer::Crt;
  bool StreamRead = false;
  bool StreamWrite = false;
  bool StreamUpdate = false;
  bool StreamCtrlZ = false;
  bool SetvbufBuffer = false;
  bool LowEof = false;
  bool LowCrlf = false;
};
#else
// The state of a glibc FILE (glibc 2.39 libio: fileops.c, genops.c,
// ioseekoff.c, ftello.c, iofread.c, iogetline.c), byte-oriented, no
// markers. Buffer is the main buffer (_IO_buf_base .. _IO_buf_end, made by
// the first fill, fread, fseek or setvbuf; HasBuffer); its size is
// _IO_buf_end - _IO_buf_base: 4096 made by the model, 1 for an unbuffered
// stream (_shortbuf), any size for the caller's array. Unbuffered /
// LineBuffered are _IO_UNBUFFERED / _IO_LINE_BUF. Backup is the backup area
// ungetc makes when a byte cannot go back into the get area (128 bytes,
// doubled when full; HaveBackup). The get area (_IO_read_base / _ptr /
// _end: ReadBase, ReadPtr, ReadEnd) lies in Backup while InBackup, else in
// Buffer; the save area (_IO_save_base / _end: SaveBase, SaveEnd) lies in
// the other one: while InBackup it is what is left of the main get area,
// otherwise the backup area's extent. An index 0 into a Buffer not yet made
// stands for glibc's null pointers (only differences are ever taken).
// OffsetKnown: _offset is not _IO_pos_BAD (its value is then Position).
// Orientation is _mode: -1 byte-oriented, 1 wide, 0 neither yet (a fresh
// stream; it decides whether fseek drops the backup area first).
// The put area (_IO_write_base / _ptr / _end: WriteBase, WritePtr,
// WriteEnd) lies in Buffer; [WriteBase, WritePtr) are the bytes written and
// not yet flushed. WriteArea: its pointers are not glibc's null ones yet
// (set by the first fill, seek, setbuf or write). Putting is
// _IO_CURRENTLY_PUTTING (the stream is in put mode).
// AtEnd / Failed on the handle are _IO_EOF_SEEN / _IO_ERR_SEEN.
// A wide stream (glibc's _wide_data, wfileops.c / wgenops.c): Wide is its
// buffer of wchar_t (made at the first wide write or seek; HasWide), with
// the wide get area WideReadBase / Ptr / End and the wide put area
// WideWriteBase / Ptr / End in it; WideWriteArea: those pointers are not
// glibc's null ones. Converter is the stream's codecvt, made when it turned
// wide (HookIODoCrtWideConverter); a copy of the model shares it.
// WideBackup is the wide backup area ungetwc makes (_IO_wdefault_pbackfail:
// 128 wchar_t, doubled when full; made = not empty), WideSaveBase / End and
// WideBackupBase its _IO_save_base / _end and _IO_backup_base.
// InBackup is glibc's one _IO_IN_BACKUP flag, shared by the byte and the
// wide areas (as glibc's is). glibc's areas are pointers, so a swap moves
// which buffer each one points into: ReadInBackup / SaveInBackup say
// whether the byte get / save area lies in Backup (else in Buffer), and
// WideReadInBackup / WideSaveInBackup the same for the wide areas
// (WideBackup / Wide). They differ from InBackup only where glibc's own
// code leaves one kind swapped while the flag says otherwise.
struct HookIODoCrtConverter;

struct HookIODoCrtModel
{
  HookIODoCrtBuffer Buffer;
  std::vector<unsigned char> Backup;
  std::int64_t ReadBase = 0;
  std::int64_t ReadPtr = 0;
  std::int64_t ReadEnd = 0;
  std::int64_t SaveBase = 0;
  std::int64_t SaveEnd = 0;
  std::int64_t WriteBase = 0;
  std::int64_t WritePtr = 0;
  std::int64_t WriteEnd = 0;
  bool HasBuffer = false;
  bool HaveBackup = false;
  bool InBackup = false;
  bool ReadInBackup = false;
  bool SaveInBackup = true;
  bool OffsetKnown = false;
  int Orientation = 0;
  bool Unbuffered = false;
  bool LineBuffered = false;
  bool WriteArea = false;
  bool Putting = false;
  std::vector<wchar_t> Wide;
  std::int64_t WideReadBase = 0;
  std::int64_t WideReadPtr = 0;
  std::int64_t WideReadEnd = 0;
  std::int64_t WideWriteBase = 0;
  std::int64_t WideWritePtr = 0;
  std::int64_t WideWriteEnd = 0;
  bool HasWide = false;
  bool WideWriteArea = false;
  std::vector<wchar_t> WideBackup;
  std::int64_t WideSaveBase = 0;
  std::int64_t WideSaveEnd = 0;
  std::int64_t WideBackupBase = 0;
  bool WideReadInBackup = false;
  bool WideSaveInBackup = true;
  std::shared_ptr<HookIODoCrtConverter> Converter;
};

// The head of glibc's FILE (bits/types/struct_FILE.h): _flags and the six
// area pointers, laid out as struct _IO_FILE begins. A Linux handle is known
// by this head's address (HookIODoFileOf): glibc's inline getc_unlocked /
// putc_unlocked / feof_unlocked / ferror_unlocked (bits/stdio.h, built in
// wherever C is optimized: lua's file loader) read these fields straight,
// with no call HookIO could hook. The areas stay empty (every pointer
// nullptr), so each inline read finds its get area used up and calls
// __uflow, and each inline write calls __overflow, both hooked. Flags holds
// only _IO_EOF_SEEN / _IO_ERR_SEEN, mirrored from AtEnd / Failed whenever a
// call on the handle ends (HookIODoMirrorFlags). glibc's own functions never
// see the head: every name that takes a FILE* is hooked.
struct HookIODoGlibcHead
{
  int Flags = 0;
  char* ReadPtr = nullptr;
  char* ReadEnd = nullptr;
  char* ReadBase = nullptr;
  char* WriteBase = nullptr;
  char* WritePtr = nullptr;
  char* WriteEnd = nullptr;
};

// The fields the inline forms read sit where glibc's FILE has them
static_assert(offsetof(HookIODoGlibcHead, Flags) == offsetof(FILE, _flags));
static_assert(offsetof(HookIODoGlibcHead, ReadPtr) == offsetof(FILE, _IO_read_ptr));
static_assert(offsetof(HookIODoGlibcHead, ReadEnd) == offsetof(FILE, _IO_read_end));
static_assert(offsetof(HookIODoGlibcHead, ReadBase) == offsetof(FILE, _IO_read_base));
static_assert(offsetof(HookIODoGlibcHead, WriteBase) == offsetof(FILE, _IO_write_base));
static_assert(offsetof(HookIODoGlibcHead, WritePtr) == offsetof(FILE, _IO_write_ptr));
static_assert(offsetof(HookIODoGlibcHead, WriteEnd) == offsetof(FILE, _IO_write_end));
#endif

struct HookIODoHandle
{
#if !defined(_WIN32)
  // What a caller holds as the handle's FILE* (HookIODoGlibcHead above)
  HookIODoGlibcHead GlibcHead;
#endif
  HookIODoIO Stream = nullptr;
  bool Owned = false;
  std::int64_t Position = 0;
  HookIODoMode Mode = HookIODoMode::Read;
  // Opened with a or a+: every write lands at the IO's end (O_APPEND /
  // ucrt's FAPPEND), whatever the handle's place
  bool Appending = false;
  std::shared_ptr<std::mutex> StreamLock;
  bool AtEnd = false;
  bool Failed = false;
  bool Closed = false;
  bool Text = false;
  // Windows lowio's text mode (_textmode): 0 ANSI, 1 UTF-8, 2 UTF-16LE
  // (a ccs= open, its BOM read or written); Utf8Translated is
  // _utf8translations (the last UTF-8 read's characters differ in count
  // from its bytes) and StartPos _startpos (where that read began)
  int LowText = 0;
  bool Utf8Translated = false;
  std::int64_t StartPos = 0;
  // Windows lowio's _tm_unicode: the open asked for ccs=UNICODE (_O_WTEXT,
  // open.cpp sets it whatever the BOM and the b / t letter give); the byte
  // functions refuse such a stream even while its text mode is ANSI
  bool WideText = false;
  // The IOSource entry the handle opened (Source nullptr on a registered IO,
  // and once the handle gave its entry use back) and whether it was opened
  // with ucrt's D: the entry is removed when its last D handle closes
  // (HookIODoReleaseEntry; Windows only, Temporary is never set on Linux)
  HookIODoSource Source = nullptr;
  std::string EntryName;
  bool Temporary = false;
  // A folder IOSource the handle made for itself (a freopen onto a real
  // path, HookIODoReopen): closed once the handle's entry use is given back
  HookIODoSource OwnedSource = nullptr;
  // The path the handle was opened by, as the caller gave it: glibc's
  // freopen with no path reopens that file in the new mode
  std::string OpenedPath;
  HookIODoCrtModel Crt;
};

// The FILE* a handle is known by: its glibc head on Linux (HookIODoGlibcHead),
// the object itself on Windows, where ucrt's FILE is opaque (no inline form
// reads into it)
std::FILE* HookIODoFileOf(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  return reinterpret_cast<std::FILE*>(&AHandle);
#else
  return reinterpret_cast<std::FILE*>(&AHandle.GlibcHead);
#endif
}

// The head's _IO_EOF_SEEN / _IO_ERR_SEEN set as AHandle's AtEnd / Failed
// stand, so glibc's inline feof_unlocked / ferror_unlocked read what feof /
// ferror answer. Nothing to mirror on Windows.
void HookIODoMirrorFlags(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  (void)AHandle;
#else
  int LFlags = 0;

  if (AHandle.AtEnd)
    LFlags |= _IO_EOF_SEEN;
  if (AHandle.Failed)
    LFlags |= _IO_ERR_SEEN;
  AHandle.GlibcHead.Flags = LFlags;
#endif
}

using HookIODoHandleRef = std::shared_ptr<HookIODoHandle>;

// The registry and the open handles. Function-local statics: built on first
// use, so a hook that runs before main (another library's static initializer
// opening a file) never finds them unbuilt. One lock for both, never held
// while CustomIO or the C runtime runs: a source that opens files comes back
// through these hooks.
// Never destroyed (made on the heap, never freed): a handle still open at
// exit stays usable, as a real FILE does, by every hooked call made while
// the program's statics are destroyed (a global's destructor writing to a
// FILE, the C++ streams flushing stdout); a destroyed registry would be
// locked and searched there.
std::mutex& HookIODoLock()
{
  static std::mutex* const LLock = new std::mutex();
  return *LLock;
}

std::unordered_map<std::uint64_t, HookIODoEntry>& HookIODoEntries()
{
  static auto* const LEntries = new std::unordered_map<std::uint64_t, HookIODoEntry>();
  return *LEntries;
}

// Open handles by the address a hooked open returned. The map holds a
// reference: a call that found the handle keeps it alive past an fclose.
std::unordered_map<void*, HookIODoHandleRef>& HookIODoHandles()
{
  static auto* const LHandles = new std::unordered_map<void*, HookIODoHandleRef>();
  return *LHandles;
}

// The stream lock of every registered IO that an entry or a handle still
// holds. One IO has one lock however often it is registered, also after an
// unregister while handles stay open.
std::unordered_map<HookIODoIO, std::weak_ptr<std::mutex>>& HookIODoStreamLocks()
{
  static auto* const LLocks = new std::unordered_map<HookIODoIO, std::weak_ptr<std::mutex>>();
  return *LLocks;
}

// AStream's lock, made on first use; the caller holds the registry lock.
// Locks no one holds any more are dropped on the way.
std::shared_ptr<std::mutex> HookIODoStreamLockOf(const HookIODoIO AStream)
{
  std::shared_ptr<std::mutex> LLock;

  for (auto LCursor = HookIODoStreamLocks().begin(); LCursor != HookIODoStreamLocks().end(); )
  {
    if (LCursor->second.expired())
      LCursor = HookIODoStreamLocks().erase(LCursor);
    else
      ++LCursor;
  }
  const auto LFound = HookIODoStreamLocks().find(AStream);
  if (LFound != HookIODoStreamLocks().end())
    LLock = LFound->second.lock();
  if (!LLock)
  {
    LLock = std::make_shared<std::mutex>();
    HookIODoStreamLocks()[AStream] = LLock;
  }
  return LLock;
}

#if defined(_WIN32)
// How open handles use one IOSource entry, ucrt's share rules for D (lowio
// open.cpp: a D open asks DELETE access and shares deletion, every other
// open shares reading and writing only, so a D handle and a plain one on a
// file refuse each other: a sharing violation, EACCES). Plain / Temporary
// count the handles of each kind, made under the registry lock before the
// entry is opened. When the last D handle closes the entry is removed
// (the OS deletes a FILE_FLAG_DELETE_ON_CLOSE file at its last close);
// Removing is set while that close deletes it, and an open meanwhile finds
// it gone (ENOENT), as an open just after the real close does.
struct HookIODoEntryUse
{
  std::int64_t Plain = 0;
  std::int64_t Temporary = 0;
  bool Removing = false;
};

using HookIODoEntryKey = std::pair<HookIODoSource, std::string>;

std::map<HookIODoEntryKey, HookIODoEntryUse>& HookIODoEntryUses()
{
  static auto* const LUses = new std::map<HookIODoEntryKey, HookIODoEntryUse>();
  return *LUses;
}

// Takes a use of the entry before it is opened. False with errno set:
// EACCES when the other kind holds it, ENOENT while its last D close is
// removing it, ENOMEM.
bool HookIODoReserveEntry(const HookIODoSource ASource, const std::string& AEntry,
  const bool ATemporary)
{
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
    HookIODoEntryUse& LUse = HookIODoEntryUses()[HookIODoEntryKey(ASource, AEntry)];
    if (LUse.Removing)
    {
      errno = ENOENT;
      return false;
    }
    if ((ATemporary && (LUse.Plain > 0)) || ((!ATemporary) && (LUse.Temporary > 0)))
    {
      errno = EACCES;
      return false;
    }
    if (ATemporary)
      ++LUse.Temporary;
    else
      ++LUse.Plain;
    return true;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
}

// Gives a use back. True when it was the entry's last D use and ARemove
// asks for the removal: the entry is then marked Removing and the caller
// removes it (HookIODoFinishRemove). ARemove is false when the open that
// took the use failed before its IO was opened.
bool HookIODoReleaseEntry(const HookIODoSource ASource, const std::string& AEntry,
  const bool ATemporary, const bool ARemove)
{
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
    const auto LFound = HookIODoEntryUses().find(HookIODoEntryKey(ASource, AEntry));
    if (LFound == HookIODoEntryUses().end())
      return false;
    HookIODoEntryUse& LUse = LFound->second;
    if (ATemporary)
      --LUse.Temporary;
    else
      --LUse.Plain;
    if (ATemporary && ARemove && (LUse.Temporary == 0))
    {
      LUse.Removing = true;
      return true;
    }
    if ((LUse.Plain == 0) && (LUse.Temporary == 0) && (!LUse.Removing))
      HookIODoEntryUses().erase(LFound);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    // find / erase do not throw; the lock alone can
  }
  return false;
}

// Removes an entry whose last D handle closed (the registry lock is not held:
// the source runs), then forgets it. The result is not reported: ucrt's
// fclose cannot see whether the OS deleted the file either.
void HookIODoFinishRemove(const HookIODoSource ASource, const std::string& AEntry)
{
  try
  {
    ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceRemove(ASource, AEntry);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    // The entry stays; nothing can report it
  }
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
    HookIODoEntryUses().erase(HookIODoEntryKey(ASource, AEntry));
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    // Only the lock can throw
  }
}
#endif

// Gives back the entry use a handle holds, once (Source is cleared), and
// removes the entry when that was its last D handle. ARemove: false when
// the handle never opened its IO. A no-op on a registered IO and on Linux.
void HookIODoGiveBackEntry(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const bool ARemove)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  const HookIODoSource LSource = AHandle.Source;

  if (LSource == nullptr)
    return;
  AHandle.Source = nullptr;
  if (HookIODoReleaseEntry(LSource, AHandle.EntryName, AHandle.Temporary, ARemove))
    HookIODoFinishRemove(LSource, AHandle.EntryName);
#else
  (void)AHandle;
  (void)ARemove;
#endif
}

// How many handles are open, changed under the lock. While it is 0 no
// address is a handle, so a stream call on a real FILE skips the lock.
// Constant-initialized: valid before any constructor runs.
std::atomic<std::size_t> HookIODoOpenCount{0};

// The last prefix number handed out (0 is never one), under the lock
std::uint64_t HookIODoLastId = 0;

// The scheme every virtual path starts with
constexpr char CHookIODoScheme[] = "io://";
constexpr std::size_t CHookIODoSchemeLength = sizeof(CHookIODoScheme) - 1;

// True when APath is virtual (starts with io://). AId = its prefix number,
// 0 when the number is missing, has a leading zero, overflows, or is not
// followed by the end or '/' (no prefix is 0, so the path is a missing file).
// ARest = what follows the number: "" or "/<name>".
bool HookIODoParse(const char* APath, std::uint64_t& AId, const char*& ARest)
{
  const char* LCursor;
  std::uint64_t LId = 0;
  bool LDigits = false;

  AId = 0;
  ARest = "";
  if (APath == nullptr)
    return false;
  if (std::strncmp(APath, CHookIODoScheme, CHookIODoSchemeLength) != 0)
    return false;
  LCursor = APath + CHookIODoSchemeLength;
  if (*LCursor == '0')
    return true;
  while ((*LCursor >= '0') && (*LCursor <= '9'))
  {
    const std::uint64_t LDigit = static_cast<std::uint64_t>(*LCursor - '0');
    // Past the largest number: no such prefix
    if (LId > ((UINT64_MAX - LDigit) / 10))
      return true;
    LId = (LId * 10) + LDigit;
    LDigits = true;
    ++LCursor;
  }
  if ((!LDigits) || ((*LCursor != '\0') && (*LCursor != '/')))
    return true;
  AId = LId;
  ARest = LCursor;
  return true;
}

#if defined(_WIN32)
// True when a mode with neither b nor t opens in text mode: _get_fmode's
// _O_TEXT (ucrt's default; a program linked with binmode.o has _O_BINARY)
bool HookIODoDefaultText()
{
  int LMode = _O_TEXT;

  if (_get_fmode(&LMode) != 0)
    return true;
  return (LMode & _O_BINARY) == 0;
}
#endif

// What a mode string asks for, as the target CRT's parser reads it. The
// parse only: HookIODoOpen decides which of it HookIO opens.
struct HookIODoOpenMode
{
  // The first letter: 'r', 'w' or 'a'
  char First = 'r';
  // r: Read, w: Write, a: Append; any of them with +: ReadWrite (First
  // then says whether the open empties, w, or appends, a)
  HookIODoMode Mode = HookIODoMode::Read;
  // '+' was given
  bool Plus = false;
  // Reads and writes translate (Windows text mode; always false on Linux)
  bool Text = false;
  // 'x': the open creates the file and fails EEXIST when it exists
  bool Exclusive = false;
  // ucrt 'D': the file is removed when its last handle closes
  bool Temporary = false;
  // ",ccs=...": a wide-text stream
  bool Encoded = false;
  // Windows: which ccs= name (ucrt's _O_U8TEXT 1, _O_U16TEXT 2, _O_WTEXT 3)
  int Encoding = 0;
  // Linux: the charset ",ccs=" names (glibc's gconv name)
  std::string Charset;
};

// AResult's First and Mode from the mode's first letter; false when it is
// not r, w or a (both CRTs' EINVAL)
bool HookIODoParseFirst(const char AFirst, HookIODoOpenMode& AResult)
{
  AResult.First = AFirst;
  if (AFirst == 'r')
    AResult.Mode = HookIODoMode::Read;
  else if (AFirst == 'w')
    AResult.Mode = HookIODoMode::Write;
  else if (AFirst == 'a')
    AResult.Mode = HookIODoMode::Append;
  else
    return false;
  return true;
}

#if defined(_WIN32)
// True when ACursor starts with the ACount characters of AWord, ASCII
// letters compared without case
bool HookIODoStartsNoCase(const char* ACursor, const char* AWord, const std::size_t ACount)
{
  std::size_t LI;
  char LHave;
  char LWant;

  for (LI = 0; LI < ACount; ++LI)
  {
    LHave = ACursor[LI];
    LWant = AWord[LI];
    if ((LHave >= 'a') && (LHave <= 'z'))
      LHave = static_cast<char>(LHave - 'a' + 'A');
    if ((LWant >= 'a') && (LWant <= 'z'))
      LWant = static_cast<char>(LWant - 'a' + 'A');
    if (LHave != LWant)
      return false;
  }
  return true;
}

// ucrt's encoding part after the comma: spaces, "ccs" (lower case only),
// spaces, '=', spaces, UTF-8, UTF-16LE or UNICODE (any case), spaces, the
// end. False: EINVAL. AEncoding: 1 UTF-8, 2 UTF-16LE, 3 UNICODE.
bool HookIODoParseEncoding(const char* ACursor, int& AEncoding)
{
  const char* LCursor = ACursor;

  while (*LCursor == ' ')
    ++LCursor;
  if (std::strncmp(LCursor, "ccs", 3) != 0)
    return false;
  LCursor += 3;
  while (*LCursor == ' ')
    ++LCursor;
  if (*LCursor != '=')
    return false;
  ++LCursor;
  while (*LCursor == ' ')
    ++LCursor;
  // ucrt tries the names in this order, each as a prefix of what follows
  if (HookIODoStartsNoCase(LCursor, "UTF-8", 5))
  {
    LCursor += 5;
    AEncoding = 1;
  }
  else if (HookIODoStartsNoCase(LCursor, "UTF-16LE", 8))
  {
    LCursor += 8;
    AEncoding = 2;
  }
  else if (HookIODoStartsNoCase(LCursor, "UNICODE", 7))
  {
    LCursor += 7;
    AEncoding = 3;
  }
  else
    return false;
  while (*LCursor == ' ')
    ++LCursor;
  return *LCursor == '\0';
}

// AMode as ucrt's fopen parses it (rules from corecrt_internal_stdio.h
// __acrt_stdio_parse_mode, Windows Kits 10.0.26100): leading spaces, then r,
// w or a, then any of: + (once); b or t (one of the two, once); c or n (one
// of the two, once); S or R (one of the two, once); T (once); D (once); N
// (any number); x (only when the first letter is w); spaces; or a comma,
// which starts the encoding part (HookIODoParseEncoding). Anything else, or
// any of those rules broken: false (fopen's EINVAL). Text: t, or neither b
// nor t while _get_fmode says _O_TEXT. c / n (commit on flush), S / R / T
// (caching hints) and N (not inherited) change nothing an IO can show.
bool HookIODoParseMode(const char* AMode, HookIODoOpenMode& AResult)
{
  const char* LCursor;
  char LChar;
  bool LBinary = false;
  bool LTextFlag = false;
  bool LCommit = false;
  bool LCaching = false;
  bool LShortLived = false;
  bool LComma = false;

  AResult = HookIODoOpenMode();
  if (AMode == nullptr)
    return false;
  LCursor = AMode;
  while (*LCursor == ' ')
    ++LCursor;
  if (!HookIODoParseFirst(*LCursor, AResult))
    return false;
  ++LCursor;
  while ((!LComma) && (*LCursor != '\0'))
  {
    LChar = *LCursor;
    if (LChar == '+')
    {
      if (AResult.Plus)
        return false;
      AResult.Plus = true;
    }
    else if ((LChar == 'b') || (LChar == 't'))
    {
      if (LBinary || LTextFlag)
        return false;
      LBinary = LChar == 'b';
      LTextFlag = LChar == 't';
    }
    else if ((LChar == 'c') || (LChar == 'n'))
    {
      if (LCommit)
        return false;
      LCommit = true;
    }
    else if ((LChar == 'S') || (LChar == 'R'))
    {
      if (LCaching)
        return false;
      LCaching = true;
    }
    else if (LChar == 'T')
    {
      if (LShortLived)
        return false;
      LShortLived = true;
    }
    else if (LChar == 'D')
    {
      if (AResult.Temporary)
        return false;
      AResult.Temporary = true;
    }
    else if (LChar == 'x')
    {
      // ucrt allows x only with the truncating open, w
      if (AResult.First != 'w')
        return false;
      AResult.Exclusive = true;
    }
    else if (LChar == ',')
      LComma = true;
    else if ((LChar != 'N') && (LChar != ' '))
      return false;
    ++LCursor;
  }
  if (LComma)
  {
    if (!HookIODoParseEncoding(LCursor, AResult.Encoding))
      return false;
    AResult.Encoded = true;
  }
  // ucrt: + gives _O_RDWR and _IOUPDATE whatever the first letter
  if (AResult.Plus)
    AResult.Mode = HookIODoMode::ReadWrite;
  AResult.Text = (!LBinary) && (LTextFlag || HookIODoDefaultText());
  return true;
}
#else
// AMode as glibc's fopen parses it (rules from glibc 2.39 libio/fileops.c
// _IO_new_file_fopen): r, w or a first (nothing may come before it); then at
// most six more characters, stopping at the end or at a comma: + reads and
// writes, x is O_EXCL, every other character (b, t, m, c, e or anything
// else) changes nothing an IO can show. ",ccs=" anywhere after the last +,
// x or b asks for a wide-text stream. False: EINVAL (only a wrong first
// letter). No text mode.
bool HookIODoParseMode(const char* AMode, HookIODoOpenMode& AResult)
{
  const char* LLastRecognized;
  int LI;
  char LChar;

  AResult = HookIODoOpenMode();
  if ((AMode == nullptr) || (!HookIODoParseFirst(AMode[0], AResult)))
    return false;
  LLastRecognized = AMode;
  for (LI = 1; LI < 7; ++LI)
  {
    LChar = AMode[LI];
    if ((LChar == '\0') || (LChar == ','))
      break;
    if (LChar == '+')
    {
      AResult.Plus = true;
      LLastRecognized = AMode + LI;
    }
    else if (LChar == 'x')
    {
      AResult.Exclusive = true;
      LLastRecognized = AMode + LI;
    }
    else if (LChar == 'b')
      LLastRecognized = AMode + LI;
  }
  // ",ccs=NAME": the name runs to the next comma or the end (glibc's
  // strchrnul), spaces trimmed
  const char* LCcs = std::strstr(LLastRecognized + 1, ",ccs=");
  AResult.Encoded = LCcs != nullptr;
  if (LCcs != nullptr)
  {
    const char* LStart = LCcs + 5;
    const char* LEnd = std::strchr(LStart, ',');
    if (LEnd == nullptr)
      LEnd = LStart + std::strlen(LStart);
    while ((LStart < LEnd) && (*LStart == ' '))
      ++LStart;
    while ((LEnd > LStart) && (LEnd[-1] == ' '))
      --LEnd;
    try
    {
      AResult.Charset.assign(LStart, LEnd);
    }
    catch (...)
    {
      return false;
    }
  }
  // glibc: + gives O_RDWR whatever the first letter (a+ keeps appending)
  if (AResult.Plus)
    AResult.Mode = HookIODoMode::ReadWrite;
  return true;
}
#endif

// True when the parsed mode asks for something HookIO does not open; the
// open is refused with EINVAL. Every mode either CRT accepts is opened
// today: none.
bool HookIODoModeNotBuilt(const HookIODoOpenMode& AMode)
{
  (void)AMode;
  return false;
}

// True when the open must fail with EEXIST because the target exists: x
// with a creating open (w; on Linux also a). glibc passes O_EXCL with r
// too, where Linux's open ignores it without O_CREAT.
bool HookIODoExclusive(const HookIODoOpenMode& AMode)
{
  return AMode.Exclusive && (AMode.First != 'r');
}

// The registered entry of AId, copied out under the lock; false when none
bool HookIODoFind(const std::uint64_t AId, HookIODoEntry& AEntry)
{
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
    const auto LFound = HookIODoEntries().find(AId);
    if (LFound == HookIODoEntries().end())
      return false;
    AEntry = LFound->second;
    return true;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    return false;
  }
}

// The prefix number of the IOSource SetIOPathSource set (0: none). It is a
// registered entry like any other, so a lookup copies it out under the lock
// (HookIODoFind) and a source unset meanwhile is simply not found.
// Constant-initialized: valid before any constructor runs.
std::atomic<std::uint64_t> HookIODoPathSourceId{0};

// The prefix number of this thread's own path source (SetIOThreadPathSource;
// 0: none). While it is set, this thread's plain paths are looked up in it
// instead of HookIODoPathSourceId's source; other threads never see it.
// Trivially destructible: registers no thread exit work.
thread_local std::uint64_t HookIODoThreadPathSourceId = 0;

// The prefix number a plain path on this thread is looked up in: the
// thread's own path source when one is set, else the program's (0: none)
std::uint64_t HookIODoActivePathSourceId()
{
  if (HookIODoThreadPathSourceId != 0)
    return HookIODoThreadPathSourceId;
  return HookIODoPathSourceId.load();
}

// How deep this thread is inside HookIO's own path work (a hooked open or
// query, the path source lookup). While it is above 0 a plain path is never
// looked up in the path source: the source's own opens (a folder source
// opening its real files, a zip source reading its archive) reach the real
// file system, and the lookup cannot recurse into itself. Trivially
// destructible: registers no thread exit work.
thread_local int HookIODoPathDepth = 0;

// Raises HookIODoPathDepth for its scope
struct HookIODoPathGuard
{
  HookIODoPathGuard()
  {
    ++HookIODoPathDepth;
  }

  ~HookIODoPathGuard()
  {
    --HookIODoPathDepth;
  }

  HookIODoPathGuard(const HookIODoPathGuard&) = delete;
  HookIODoPathGuard& operator=(const HookIODoPathGuard&) = delete;
};

// True when a plain path may be looked up in the path source: one is set
// (this thread's own or the program's) and this thread is inside neither
// HookIO's own path work nor CustomIO's real file system work
bool HookIODoPathSourceActive()
{
  return (HookIODoPathDepth == 0) && (HookIODoActivePathSourceId() != 0) &&
    (!::pcpp_customio_internal::InFileSystemWork());
}

// A plain path as an entry name of the path source: '\' turned to '/', and
// every leading "./" or '/' dropped (a source's names are relative), as
// raylib_ext's file callbacks name them. "" when nothing is left.
std::string HookIODoPathEntryName(const char* APath)
{
  std::string LName(APath);

  for (char& LChar : LName)
  {
    if (LChar == '\\')
      LChar = '/';
  }
  for (;;)
  {
    if (LName.rfind("./", 0) == 0)
      LName.erase(0, 2);
    else if ((!LName.empty()) && (LName[0] == '/'))
      LName.erase(0, 1);
    else
      break;
  }
  return LName;
}

// APath past every leading "./" (on Windows ".\" too) when an io:// path
// follows them, else APath itself. A C library that joins a folder and a
// name writes a folder with no root as "./<folder>" (raylib's
// GetDirectoryPath does), so "./io://3/model/tex.png" names the same path
// as "io://3/model/tex.png".
const char* HookIODoSkipCurrentFolder(const char* APath)
{
  const char* LCursor = APath;

  if (APath == nullptr)
    return APath;
  while ((LCursor[0] == '.') && ((LCursor[1] == '/')
#if defined(_WIN32)
    || (LCursor[1] == '\\')
#endif
    ))
    LCursor += 2;
  if ((LCursor != APath) &&
    (std::strncmp(LCursor, CHookIODoScheme, CHookIODoSchemeLength) == 0))
    return LCursor;
  return APath;
}

// As HookIODoParse (after HookIODoSkipCurrentFolder), and a plain path the
// path source holds (this thread's own when set, else the program's): then
// AId is that path source's prefix number and ARest
// "/<entry>" (kept in AStorage). A plain path the source lacks (or any path
// while no source is set, inside HookIO's own path work, or out of memory)
// is false: the C runtime gets it.
bool HookIODoResolve(const char* APath, std::uint64_t& AId, const char*& ARest,
  std::string& AStorage)
{
  std::uint64_t LSourceId;
  HookIODoEntry LEntry;
  bool LExists;

  if (HookIODoParse(HookIODoSkipCurrentFolder(APath), AId, ARest))
    return true;
  if ((APath == nullptr) || (*APath == '\0') || (!HookIODoPathSourceActive()))
    return false;
  LSourceId = HookIODoActivePathSourceId();
  if ((LSourceId == 0) || (!HookIODoFind(LSourceId, LEntry)) || (LEntry.Source == nullptr))
    return false;
  try
  {
    HookIODoPathGuard LPathGuard;
    const std::string LName(HookIODoPathEntryName(APath));
    if (LName.empty())
      return false;
    LExists = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceExists(LEntry.Source, LName);
    if (!LExists)
      return false;
    AStorage = "/" + LName;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    return false;
  }
  AId = LSourceId;
  ARest = AStorage.c_str();
  return true;
}

// The exit flush of open handles' written bytes, defined below
void HookIODoArmExitFlush();

// Records AHandle as open; false (out of memory) leaves it unrecorded. The
// exit flush is armed after the registry exists (it is then destroyed
// first, while the registry still lives).
bool HookIODoAddHandle(const HookIODoHandleRef& AHandle)
{
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
    HookIODoHandles().emplace(HookIODoFileOf(*AHandle), AHandle);
    HookIODoOpenCount.fetch_add(1);
    HookIODoArmExitFlush();
    return true;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    return false;
  }
}

// The handle behind AFile, or empty when AFile is not one (a real FILE, nil)
HookIODoHandleRef HookIODoFindHandle(std::FILE* AFile)
{
  if ((AFile == nullptr) || (HookIODoOpenCount.load() == 0))
    return HookIODoHandleRef();
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
    const auto LFound = HookIODoHandles().find(AFile);
    if (LFound == HookIODoHandles().end())
      return HookIODoHandleRef();
    return LFound->second;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    return HookIODoHandleRef();
  }
}

// The byte that ends a text-mode read on Windows
constexpr unsigned char CHookIODoCtrlZ = 0x1A;

#if defined(_WIN32)
// ucrt's open of a text-mode file for reading and writing (any "+") drops
// one trailing Ctrl-Z so that appending works (rules from ucrt
// lowio\open.cpp truncate_ctrl_z_if_present): nothing for an empty IO or
// one that cannot seek to its end (ucrt skips devices and pipes, the
// descriptors that cannot seek); when the last byte is 0x1A the IO is
// shortened by one. A shorten that fails does not fail the open: ucrt
// compares _chsize_nolock's errno_t with -1, so its open goes on with the
// byte kept and errno left at EACCES (measured on a mapped file,
// tests\probe\hookabi\trunc_refuse.c). The handle starts at 0 either way
// (its Position; the IO itself is moved back by HookIODoSyncLocked before
// any access). False (ENOMEM) when the stream lock could not be taken.
bool HookIODoDropCtrlZ(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  std::int64_t LEnd;
  unsigned char LLast = 0;

  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(*AHandle.StreamLock);
    LEnd = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSize(AHandle.Stream);
    // An IO with no size may still know its end
    if (LEnd < 0)
      LEnd = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, 0, ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromEnd);
    // An empty file: ucrt's seek to -1 from the end fails (SetFilePointerEx
    // ERROR_NEGATIVE_SEEK, mapped to EINVAL); the open goes on, errno is
    // left at EINVAL (measured, tests\probe\hookabi\ccs_real.c "w+,ccs=")
    if (LEnd == 0)
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return true;
    }
    if (LEnd < 0)
      return true;
    if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, LEnd - 1,
      ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromStart) != (LEnd - 1))
      return true;
    // A failed read of the last byte is not an error (ucrt reads 0 bytes)
    if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IORead(AHandle.Stream, &LLast, 1) != 1)
      return true;
    if (LLast != CHookIODoCtrlZ)
      return true;
    if (!::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOTruncate(AHandle.Stream, LEnd - 1))
      errno = EACCES;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
  AHandle.Position = 0;
  return true;
}
#endif

// "w" / "w+" empty the handle's IO, as the C runtime's open truncates the
// file (on a registered IO every other handle sees it emptied, as other
// descriptors of a real file do). An IO that cannot write refuses the open
// with EACCES (a read-only file); one that cannot be emptied (no Truncate,
// or a failed one) with what each CRT reports for a file it cannot truncate
// (measured, tests\probe\hookabi\trunc_refuse.c: ucrt EINVAL for a mapped
// file, glibc EPERM for an append-only one). False with errno set; the
// handle starts at 0. ENOMEM when the stream lock could not be taken.
bool HookIODoEmptyIO(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  bool LEmptied;
  bool LReadOnly = false;

  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(*AHandle.StreamLock);
    LEmptied = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOTruncate(AHandle.Stream, 0);
    if (!LEmptied)
      LReadOnly = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOStatus(AHandle.Stream) == ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOState::ReadOnly;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
  if (!LEmptied)
  {
    if (LReadOnly)
      errno = EACCES;
    else
    {
#if defined(_WIN32)
      errno = EINVAL;
#else
      errno = EPERM;
#endif
    }
    return false;
  }
  AHandle.Position = 0;
  return true;
}

// Where a write-only append handle ("a") starts, as the target CRT opens
// it: ucrt's open leaves its descriptor at 0 (lowio moves it to the end at
// each write, so ftell before the first write is 0, measured); glibc's
// fopen seeks to the end (_IO_file_open, only when the stream appends and
// does not read). "a+" starts at 0 on both, so this is not called for it.
// The IO's end, under its stream lock; false (ENOMEM) when the lock could
// not be taken.
bool HookIODoAppendStart(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  AHandle.Position = 0;
#else
  std::int64_t LEnd;

  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(*AHandle.StreamLock);
    LEnd = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSize(AHandle.Stream);
    if (LEnd < 0)
      LEnd = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, 0, ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromEnd);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
  AHandle.Position = (LEnd > 0) ? LEnd : 0;
#endif
  return true;
}

// A handle on a registered IO, sharing the entry's stream lock. w / w+
// empty the IO (HookIODoEmptyIO). a starts where the target CRT's does
// (HookIODoAppendStart); a+ at 0.
bool HookIODoOpenShared(const HookIODoEntry& AEntry, const HookIODoOpenMode& AParsed,
  HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  AHandle.Stream = AEntry.Stream;
  AHandle.StreamLock = AEntry.StreamLock;
  AHandle.Owned = false;
  AHandle.Position = 0;
  if (AParsed.First == 'w')
    return HookIODoEmptyIO(AHandle);
  if (AParsed.Mode == HookIODoMode::Append)
    return HookIODoAppendStart(AHandle);
  return true;
}

// The entry name in a path's rest after the prefix: "/<entry>" -> "<entry>"
std::string HookIODoEntryName(const char* ARest)
{
  return std::string((*ARest == '/') ? (ARest + 1) : ARest);
}

// AExists = the open's target exists: always for a registered IO (every
// name under its prefix is that IO), IOSourceExists for a source entry.
// False: out of memory (errno ENOMEM).
bool HookIODoExists(const HookIODoEntry& AEntry, const char* ARest, bool& AExists)
{
  AExists = true;
  if (AEntry.Stream != nullptr)
    return true;
  try
  {
    AExists = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceExists(AEntry.Source, HookIODoEntryName(ARest));
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
  return true;
}

// w+ / a+ on an IOSource entry: CustomIO has no mode that creates AND
// reads, so a missing entry is created first by IOSourceOpen in Write (w+)
// or Append (a+) and closed at once; the handle then opens it ReadWrite.
// False with errno set: ENOENT when the source would not create it (as a
// plain w / a on that source), EIO when closing the new entry failed.
bool HookIODoCreateEntry(const HookIODoSource ASource, const std::string& AEntry,
  const HookIODoOpenMode& AParsed)
{
  HookIODoIO LCreated;

  if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceExists(ASource, AEntry))
    return true;
  LCreated = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceOpen(ASource, AEntry,
    (AParsed.First == 'w') ? HookIODoMode::Write : HookIODoMode::Append);
  if (LCreated == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOENT;
    return false;
  }
  if (!::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOClose(LCreated))
  {
    errno = EIO;
    return false;
  }
  return true;
}

// A handle's IO on an IOSource entry: ARest is "/<entry>". The handle owns
// the IO. w+ / a+ open it ReadWrite (HookIODoCreateEntry first), w+ then
// empties it (HookIODoEmptyIO). A failed open sets errno: EACCES when the
// entry exists (the source does not offer that mode), ENOENT otherwise
// (missing, or a path IOSourceOpen refuses).
bool HookIODoOpenEntryIO(const HookIODoSource ASource, const char* ARest,
  const HookIODoOpenMode& AParsed, HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  const bool LCreating = AParsed.Plus && (AParsed.First != 'r');

  try
  {
    const std::string LEntry(HookIODoEntryName(ARest));
    if (LCreating && (!HookIODoCreateEntry(ASource, LEntry, AParsed)))
      return false;
    const HookIODoIO LStream = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceOpen(ASource, LEntry, AParsed.Mode);
    if (LStream == nullptr)
    {
      if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceExists(ASource, LEntry))
        errno = EACCES;
      else
        errno = ENOENT;
      return false;
    }
    AHandle.Stream = LStream;
    AHandle.Owned = true;
    AHandle.Position = 0;
    try
    {
      // The entry's IO is this handle's alone: its own stream lock
      AHandle.StreamLock = std::make_shared<std::mutex>();
    }
    catch (...)
    {
      ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOClose(LStream);
      AHandle.Stream = nullptr;
      throw;
    }
    // errno is set by the step that fails; the close must not change it
    if (((AParsed.Mode == HookIODoMode::Append) && (!HookIODoAppendStart(AHandle)))
      || (LCreating && (AParsed.First == 'w') && (!HookIODoEmptyIO(AHandle))))
    {
      const int LError = errno;
      ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOClose(LStream);
      AHandle.Stream = nullptr;
      errno = LError;
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
}

#if defined(_WIN32)
// ucrt's D open asks DELETE access (lowio open.cpp), which a file that cannot
// be deleted refuses with EACCES before anything is opened. For an entry: a
// source that cannot remove entries (a zip), or an existing entry that does
// not open for writing (a read-only file). A missing entry opened with r is
// left to the open's own ENOENT. False with errno set.
bool HookIODoTemporaryAllowed(const HookIODoSource ASource, const std::string& AEntry,
  const HookIODoOpenMode& AParsed)
{
  bool LExists;
  HookIODoIO LProbe;

  try
  {
    LExists = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceExists(ASource, AEntry);
    if ((!LExists) && (AParsed.First == 'r'))
      return true;
    if (!::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceCanRemove(ASource))
    {
      errno = EACCES;
      return false;
    }
    if (!LExists)
      return true;
    LProbe = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceOpen(ASource, AEntry, HookIODoMode::ReadWrite);
    if (LProbe == nullptr)
    {
      errno = EACCES;
      return false;
    }
    ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOClose(LProbe);
    return true;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
}
#endif

// A handle on an IOSource entry (HookIODoOpenEntryIO). On Windows the
// handle takes a use of the entry first (ucrt's share rules for D,
// HookIODoReserveEntry) and a D open checks the entry can be removed
// (HookIODoTemporaryAllowed); the handle keeps the entry and gives the use
// back at its close (HookIODoGiveBackEntry).
bool HookIODoOpenEntry(const HookIODoSource ASource, const char* ARest,
  const HookIODoOpenMode& AParsed, HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  std::string LEntry;

  try
  {
    LEntry = HookIODoEntryName(ARest);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
  if (AParsed.Temporary && (!HookIODoTemporaryAllowed(ASource, LEntry, AParsed)))
    return false;
  if (!HookIODoReserveEntry(ASource, LEntry, AParsed.Temporary))
    return false;
  if (!HookIODoOpenEntryIO(ASource, ARest, AParsed, AHandle))
  {
    const int LError = errno;
    HookIODoReleaseEntry(ASource, LEntry, AParsed.Temporary, false);
    errno = LError;
    return false;
  }
  AHandle.Source = ASource;
  AHandle.EntryName = std::move(LEntry);
  AHandle.Temporary = AParsed.Temporary;
  return true;
#else
  return HookIODoOpenEntryIO(ASource, ARest, AParsed, AHandle);
#endif
}

// Closes the folder source a handle made for itself (HookIODoReopen), once
// its entry use is given back. False when closing the source failed.
bool HookIODoCloseOwnedSource(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  bool LOk = true;

  if (AHandle.OwnedSource == nullptr)
    return true;
  try
  {
    LOk = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceClose(AHandle.OwnedSource);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    LOk = false;
  }
  AHandle.OwnedSource = nullptr;
  return LOk;
}

// Undoes an open that succeeded but cannot be handed out: closes the
// handle's own IO and gives its entry use back (a D entry goes, as the OS
// deletes the file when the failed open's handle closes). errno is kept.
void HookIODoAbandon(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  const int LError = errno;

  if (AHandle.Owned)
    ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOClose(AHandle.Stream);
  AHandle.Stream = nullptr;
  HookIODoGiveBackEntry(AHandle, true);
  HookIODoCloseOwnedSource(AHandle);
  errno = LError;
}

// A hooked open of APath. False: not a virtual path, the caller passes it to
// the C runtime. True: handled; AResult is the new handle, or nullptr with
// errno set (see the unit header).
// The ccs= part of an open, defined with each CRT's FILE model below
#if defined(_WIN32)
bool HookIODoConfigureTextMode(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const HookIODoOpenMode& AParsed);
#else
bool HookIODoNamedWide(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::string& ACharset);
#endif

// The open once a path has named its target. AEntry: the registered IO or
// IOSource the path names (nullptr: nothing is registered under it, ENOENT
// once the mode is read); ARest: the entry's name in an IOSource; APath: the
// path as the caller gave it (kept for glibc's freopen with no path);
// ACallerErrno: errno as the caller left it. AResult: the new handle, or
// nullptr with errno set (see the unit header). HookIODoOpen calls it for a
// virtual path, HookIODoReopen for a real one (a folder source's entry).
void HookIODoOpenOn(const HookIODoEntry* AEntry, const char* ARest, const char* APath,
  const char* AMode, const int ACallerErrno, std::FILE*& AResult);

bool HookIODoOpen(const char* APath, const char* AMode, std::FILE*& AResult)
{
  std::uint64_t LId;
  const char* LRest;
  HookIODoEntry LEntry;
  std::string LMapped;
  bool LFound;
  // errno as the caller left it: a successful open leaves it so (neither
  // CRT clears or sets it on success), except where a CRT's own open sets
  // it on the way (ucrt's Ctrl-Z step, below); what the source's work set
  // (a missing entry's ENOENT before it is created) never leaks out
  const int LCallerErrno = errno;

  AResult = nullptr;
  if (!HookIODoResolve(APath, LId, LRest, LMapped))
    return false;
  // The open's own work (the source's real files) never maps a plain path
  HookIODoPathGuard LPathGuard;
  LFound = (LId != 0) && HookIODoFind(LId, LEntry);
  errno = LCallerErrno;
  // LRest points into LMapped or APath: both live until the open returns
  HookIODoOpenOn(LFound ? &LEntry : nullptr, LRest, APath, AMode, LCallerErrno, AResult);
  return true;
}

void HookIODoOpenOn(const HookIODoEntry* AEntry, const char* ARest, const char* APath,
  const char* AMode, const int ACallerErrno, std::FILE*& AResult)
{
  HookIODoOpenMode LParsed;
  HookIODoMode LMode;
  HookIODoHandleRef LHandle;
  bool LOpened;
  bool LText;
  bool LExists;
  const int LCallerErrno = ACallerErrno;
  int LOpenErrno = LCallerErrno;

  AResult = nullptr;
  // Both CRTs read the mode before they touch the file
  if ((!HookIODoParseMode(AMode, LParsed)) || HookIODoModeNotBuilt(LParsed))
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return;
  }
  LMode = LParsed.Mode;
  LText = LParsed.Text;
  if (AEntry == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOENT;
    return;
  }
  // x: the creating open fails when its target exists
  if (HookIODoExclusive(LParsed))
  {
    if (!HookIODoExists(*AEntry, ARest, LExists))
      return;
    if (LExists)
    {
      errno = EEXIST;
      return;
    }
  }
  try
  {
    LHandle = std::make_shared<HookIODoHandle>();
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return;
  }
  LHandle->Mode = LMode;
  LHandle->Appending = LParsed.First == 'a';
  LHandle->Text = LText;
  try
  {
    LHandle->OpenedPath = APath;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return;
  }
#if defined(_WIN32)
  // ucrt's open: 'r' sets _IOREAD, 'w' / 'a' _IOWRITE, '+' _IOUPDATE and
  // neither of the other two
  LHandle->Crt.StreamUpdate = LMode == HookIODoMode::ReadWrite;
  LHandle->Crt.StreamRead = LMode == HookIODoMode::Read;
  LHandle->Crt.StreamWrite = (LMode == HookIODoMode::Write) || (LMode == HookIODoMode::Append);
#endif
  // errno is set by the open that fails
  if (AEntry->Stream != nullptr)
    LOpened = HookIODoOpenShared(*AEntry, LParsed, *LHandle);
  else
    LOpened = HookIODoOpenEntry(AEntry->Source, ARest, LParsed, *LHandle);
  if (!LOpened)
    return;
  errno = LCallerErrno;
#if defined(_WIN32)
  // A text open for reading and writing drops a trailing Ctrl-Z, as ucrt's
  if (LText && (LMode == HookIODoMode::ReadWrite) && (!HookIODoDropCtrlZ(*LHandle)))
  {
    HookIODoAbandon(*LHandle);
    return;
  }
  LOpenErrno = errno;
  // Then the text mode a ccs= open asks for (its BOM read or written)
  if (!HookIODoConfigureTextMode(*LHandle, LParsed))
  {
    HookIODoAbandon(*LHandle);
    return;
  }
#else
  // ",ccs=NAME": the stream is wide from its open, converting through the
  // named charset; one glibc cannot load fails the open with EINVAL
  if (LParsed.Encoded && (!HookIODoNamedWide(*LHandle, LParsed.Charset)))
  {
    HookIODoAbandon(*LHandle);
    errno = EINVAL;
    return;
  }
#endif
  if (!HookIODoAddHandle(LHandle))
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    HookIODoAbandon(*LHandle);
    return;
  }
  errno = LOpenErrno;
  AResult = HookIODoFileOf(*LHandle);
}

// The CRT flushes fclose runs, defined with each CRT's FILE model below
#if defined(_WIN32)
int HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle);
#else
int HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle);
#endif

// What fclose does to a handle once it is out of the open list: the CRT's
// flush of written bytes, its own IO closed, its entry use given back. False
// when the flush or closing the IO failed (the handle still closes).
bool HookIODoShutHandle(const HookIODoHandleRef& AHandle);

// A hooked fclose. False: not a HookIO handle, the caller passes it to the C
// runtime. True: closed; AResult 0, or EOF when the CRT's flush of written
// bytes or closing its own IO failed.
// The object is freed when the last call holding it returns.
bool HookIODoClose(std::FILE* AFile, int& AResult)
{
  HookIODoHandleRef LHandle;

  AResult = 0;
  if ((AFile == nullptr) || (HookIODoOpenCount.load() == 0))
    return false;
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
    const auto LFound = HookIODoHandles().find(AFile);
    if (LFound == HookIODoHandles().end())
      return false;
    LHandle = LFound->second;
    HookIODoHandles().erase(LFound);
    HookIODoOpenCount.fetch_sub(1);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    return false;
  }
  if (!HookIODoShutHandle(LHandle))
    AResult = EOF;
  return true;
}

bool HookIODoShutHandle(const HookIODoHandleRef& AHandle)
{
  const HookIODoHandleRef LHandle = AHandle;
  bool LOk = true;

  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(*LHandle->StreamLock);
    // A D handle the exit already closed (HookIODoExitFlush) has nothing left
    if (!LHandle->Closed)
    {
      // The CRT's flush of written bytes first (ucrt's fclose flushes; glibc's
      // _IO_new_file_close_it flushes a stream in put mode); a failure makes
      // the close EOF, the handle still closes
#if defined(_WIN32)
      if (HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(*LHandle) != 0)
        LOk = false;
#else
      // Put mode is only ever entered by a handle that writes (overflow)
      if (LHandle->Crt.Putting && (HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(*LHandle) != 0))
        LOk = false;
#endif
      LHandle->Closed = true;
      if (LHandle->Owned && (!::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOClose(LHandle->Stream)))
        LOk = false;
      LHandle->Stream = nullptr;
    }
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    LOk = false;
  }
  // The entry use goes back once the IO is closed: a D entry's last handle
  // removes it, as the OS deletes the file at the last close
  HookIODoGiveBackEntry(*LHandle, true);
  if (!HookIODoCloseOwnedSource(*LHandle))
    LOk = false;
  return LOk;
}

// Takes AFile out of the open list (freopen's failure leaves the stream
// closed); the handle object lives on while a call still holds it
void HookIODoForgetHandle(std::FILE* AFile)
{
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
    const auto LFound = HookIODoHandles().find(AFile);
    if (LFound == HookIODoHandles().end())
      return;
    HookIODoHandles().erase(LFound);
    HookIODoOpenCount.fetch_sub(1);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    // erase and find do not allocate: nothing to report
  }
}

// A freopen onto a path that is not a virtual one: the file opens as an
// entry of a folder IOSource over its folder (CustomIO's file IOs take every
// fopen mode; create / truncate / append / x and the CRT model are a virtual
// open's, HookIODoOpenOn), and the source is handed back for the handle to
// own (HookIODoCloseOwnedSource). AResult: the new handle, or nullptr with
// errno set (ENOENT when the folder does not exist); ASource nullptr then.
void HookIODoOpenReal(const std::string& APath, const char* AMode, const int ACallerErrno,
  std::FILE*& AResult, HookIODoSource& ASource)
{
  std::string LFolder;
  std::string LName;
  std::size_t LCut;
  HookIODoEntry LEntry;
  int LError;

  AResult = nullptr;
  ASource = nullptr;
  // The source's own file opens never map a plain path
  HookIODoPathGuard LPathGuard;
  try
  {
#if defined(_WIN32)
    LCut = APath.find_last_of("/\\");
#else
    LCut = APath.find_last_of('/');
#endif
    if (LCut == std::string::npos)
    {
      // A bare name is the current folder's, as fopen's
      LFolder = ".";
      LName = APath;
    }
    else
    {
      // "/name" keeps the root as its folder (and "C:\name" its drive root)
      LFolder = APath.substr(0, LCut);
      if (LFolder.empty() || (LFolder.back() == ':'))
        LFolder.push_back(APath[LCut]);
      LName = APath.substr(LCut + 1);
    }
    ASource = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::CreateFolderIOSource(LFolder);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return;
  }
  if (ASource == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOENT;
    return;
  }
  LEntry.Source = ASource;
  errno = ACallerErrno;
  HookIODoOpenOn(&LEntry, LName.c_str(), APath.c_str(), AMode, ACallerErrno, AResult);
  if (AResult != nullptr)
    return;
  // The open failed: its errno stands, the source goes
  LError = errno;
  try
  {
    ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceClose(ASource);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    // Closing a folder source frees its record only: nothing to report
  }
  ASource = nullptr;
  errno = LError;
}

// A hooked freopen. False: AFile is not a HookIO handle (a real FILE, or
// nil): the caller passes the call to the C runtime, whatever the path.
// True: answered; AResult is AFile, reopened in place, or nullptr (errno
// set) when the reopen failed.
// C's order: the old stream is closed first (its flush or close failing is
// ignored), then APath opened in AMode, and the stream keeps its address:
// the new handle's state moves into the object AFile names and the new
// handle's own entry is dropped. A path that is not a virtual one opens as
// an entry of a folder source over its folder (HookIODoOpenReal; a real
// FILE is the C runtime's object, so the stream stays a HookIO handle over
// the disk file, which owns that source). No path: ucrt refuses
// it before touching the stream (EINVAL, the stream stays open); glibc
// reopens the file the stream was opened by.
bool HookIODoReopen(const char* APath, const char* AMode, std::FILE* AFile, std::FILE*& AResult)
{
  const HookIODoHandleRef LOld = HookIODoFindHandle(AFile);
  HookIODoHandleRef LNew;
  std::string LPath;
  std::FILE* LNewFile = nullptr;
  HookIODoSource LSource = nullptr;
  const int LCallerErrno = errno;

  AResult = nullptr;
  if (!LOld)
    return false;
  try
  {
    if (APath != nullptr)
      LPath = APath;
    else
    {
#if defined(_WIN32)
      errno = EINVAL;
      return true;
#else
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(*LOld->StreamLock);
      LPath = LOld->OpenedPath;
#endif
    }
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return true;
  }
  // Closed first; the open list keeps AFile so the address stays ours
  HookIODoShutHandle(LOld);
  if (!HookIODoOpen(LPath.c_str(), AMode, LNewFile))
  {
    // A real path: the disk file opens as a folder source's entry, the
    // source the handle's own from here on
    errno = LCallerErrno;
    HookIODoOpenReal(LPath, AMode, LCallerErrno, LNewFile, LSource);
  }
  if (LNewFile == nullptr)
  {
    // The open failed (errno is its own): the stream stays closed
    HookIODoForgetHandle(AFile);
    return true;
  }
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
    const auto LFound = HookIODoHandles().find(LNewFile);
    if (LFound != HookIODoHandles().end())
    {
      LNew = LFound->second;
      HookIODoHandles().erase(LFound);
      HookIODoOpenCount.fetch_sub(1);
    }
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    // find and erase do not allocate: LNew stays empty
  }
  if (!LNew)
  {
    HookIODoForgetHandle(AFile);
    if (LSource != nullptr)
      ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceClose(LSource);
    errno = EBADF;
    return true;
  }
  // The new state at the old address; the moved-from handle is only dropped
  // (it owns nothing now: no close of its own). A real path's folder source
  // is the stream's from here (closed with it, HookIODoShutHandle)
  *LOld = std::move(*LNew);
  LOld->OwnedSource = LSource;
  HookIODoMirrorFlags(*LOld);
  AResult = AFile;
  return true;
}

// The IO behind a HookIO handle; nullptr for anything else
HookIODoIO HookIODoStream(std::FILE* AFile)
{
  const HookIODoHandleRef LHandle = HookIODoFindHandle(AFile);

  if (!LHandle)
    return nullptr;
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(*LHandle->StreamLock);
    return LHandle->Stream;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    return nullptr;
  }
}

// The stream family. Every HookIODoXxx below that takes a FILE* returns
// false when it is not a HookIO handle (the hook then calls the C runtime),
// true when it answered; its result follows the C function's contract.
// The *Locked helpers run with the handle's stream lock held.

// ucrt's _VALIDATE_STREAM_ANSI: the byte functions (fgetc, fgets, fputc,
// fputs, ungetc) refuse with EINVAL (no error flag) a stream whose text mode
// is not ANSI (ccs=UTF-8 / UTF-16LE, or UNICODE after a BOM) or that was
// opened ccs=UNICODE at all (_tm_unicode, corecrt_internal.h); always true
// on Linux
bool HookIODoAnsiStream(const HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  if ((AHandle.Text && (AHandle.LowText != 0)) || AHandle.WideText)
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return false;
  }
#else
  (void)AHandle;
#endif
  return true;
}

bool HookIODoCanRead(const HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  return (AHandle.Mode == HookIODoMode::Read) || (AHandle.Mode == HookIODoMode::ReadWrite);
}

bool HookIODoCanWrite(const HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  return AHandle.Mode != HookIODoMode::Read;
}

// Moves the IO to the handle's Position. Another handle on the same IO, or a
// seek that only tried a target, may have left it elsewhere.
bool HookIODoSyncLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOTell(AHandle.Stream) == AHandle.Position)
    return true;
  return ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, AHandle.Position,
    ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromStart) == AHandle.Position;
}

// The descriptor's write (ucrt lowio _write, glibc _IO_SYSWRITE): ASize
// bytes of the IO itself at the handle's Position. Append mode writes at
// the IO's end: ucrt's lowio seeks there first and ignores a failed seek
// (its lseek also clears the Ctrl-Z end); glibc's O_APPEND always lands
// there (a seek that fails here is a failed write) and its offset is then
// unknown. A handle opened without write access writes nothing: -1 with
// EBADF (ucrt maps the OS refusal to EBADF; glibc's stdio never gets here,
// its _IO_NO_WRITES check comes first). A short write is a failure: Failed
// is set and errno is EIO (ucrt, nothing written: ENOSPC and -1). Returns
// the count written or -1.
std::int64_t HookIODoWriteIOLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  std::int64_t LEnd;
  std::int64_t LGot;

  if (!HookIODoCanWrite(AHandle))
  {
    errno = EBADF;
    return -1;
  }
  if (AHandle.Appending)
  {
    LEnd = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, 0, ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromEnd);
#if defined(_WIN32)
    if (LEnd >= 0)
      AHandle.Position = LEnd;
    AHandle.Crt.LowEof = false;
#else
    if (LEnd < 0)
    {
      AHandle.Failed = true;
      errno = EIO;
      return -1;
    }
    AHandle.Position = LEnd;
    AHandle.Crt.OffsetKnown = false;
#endif
  }
  if (!HookIODoSyncLocked(AHandle))
  {
    AHandle.Failed = true;
    errno = EIO;
    return -1;
  }
  // IOWrite takes a plain ptr; it only reads the bytes
  LGot = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOWrite(AHandle.Stream, const_cast<unsigned char*>(ABuffer), ASize);
  if (LGot < 0)
    LGot = 0;
  AHandle.Position += LGot;
  if (LGot < ASize)
  {
    AHandle.Failed = true;
#if defined(_WIN32)
    if (LGot == 0)
    {
      errno = ENOSPC;
      return -1;
    }
#endif
    errno = EIO;
  }
  return LGot;
}

#if defined(_WIN32)
// lowio's text-mode _write (Windows): every '\n' of ABuffer goes to the IO
// as "\r\n". Returns the count of ABuffer's bytes written (after a short
// IO write only those whose whole translation landed), or -1 when nothing
// was written.
std::int64_t HookIODoWriteTextLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  std::string LRaw;
  std::int64_t LGot;
  std::int64_t LUsed = 0;
  std::int64_t LCount = 0;

  // Out of memory here is HookIODoWith's ENOMEM: nothing is written
  LRaw.reserve(static_cast<std::size_t>(ASize));
  for (std::int64_t LI = 0; LI < ASize; ++LI)
  {
    if (ABuffer[LI] == '\n')
      LRaw.push_back('\r');
    LRaw.push_back(static_cast<char>(ABuffer[LI]));
  }
  LGot = HookIODoWriteIOLocked(AHandle, reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char*>(LRaw.data()),
    static_cast<std::int64_t>(LRaw.size()));
  if (LGot < 0)
    return -1;
  if (LGot == static_cast<std::int64_t>(LRaw.size()))
    return ASize;
  // Walk the source: each byte took 1 raw byte, a '\n' took 2
  while (LCount < ASize)
  {
    const std::int64_t LTakes = (ABuffer[LCount] == '\n') ? 2 : 1;
    if ((LUsed + LTakes) > LGot)
      break;
    LUsed += LTakes;
    ++LCount;
  }
  return LCount;
}

// lowio's UTF-16LE text write (write.cpp write_text_utf16le_nolock): each
// L'\n' as L"\r\n". Returns what ucrt's _write_nolock returns: the bytes
// written less 2 per L'\n' of the source (the source's bytes when all
// landed), or -1 when nothing was written.
std::int64_t HookIODoWriteUtf16Locked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wchar_t* AData,
  const std::int64_t ACount)
{
  std::wstring LRaw;
  std::int64_t LNewlines = 0;
  std::int64_t LGot;

  LRaw.reserve(static_cast<std::size_t>(ACount));
  for (std::int64_t LI = 0; LI < ACount; ++LI)
  {
    if (AData[LI] == L'\n')
    {
      LRaw.push_back(L'\r');
      ++LNewlines;
    }
    LRaw.push_back(AData[LI]);
  }
  LGot = HookIODoWriteIOLocked(AHandle, reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char*>(LRaw.data()),
    static_cast<std::int64_t>(LRaw.size() * sizeof(wchar_t)));
  if (LGot < 0)
    return -1;
  return LGot - 2 * LNewlines;
}

// lowio's UTF-8 text write (write.cpp write_text_utf8_nolock): the UTF-16
// source, each L'\n' as L"\r\n", converted to UTF-8 (WideCharToMultiByte,
// flags 0) and written whole. Returns the source bytes taken, or -1 when
// nothing was written (errno from the conversion or the write).
std::int64_t HookIODoWriteUtf8Locked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wchar_t* AData,
  const std::int64_t ACount)
{
  std::wstring LWide;
  std::string LBytes;
  std::int64_t LGot;
  int LSize;

  if (ACount == 0)
    return 0;
  LWide.reserve(static_cast<std::size_t>(ACount));
  for (std::int64_t LI = 0; LI < ACount; ++LI)
  {
    if (AData[LI] == L'\n')
      LWide.push_back(L'\r');
    LWide.push_back(AData[LI]);
  }
  LSize = WideCharToMultiByte(CP_UTF8, 0, LWide.data(), static_cast<int>(LWide.size()), nullptr,
    0, nullptr, nullptr);
  if (LSize == 0)
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  LBytes.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(LSize), '\0');
  WideCharToMultiByte(CP_UTF8, 0, LWide.data(), static_cast<int>(LWide.size()), LBytes.data(),
    LSize, nullptr, nullptr);
  LGot = HookIODoWriteIOLocked(AHandle, reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char*>(LBytes.data()),
    static_cast<std::int64_t>(LBytes.size()));
  if (LGot < static_cast<std::int64_t>(LBytes.size()))
    return (LGot <= 0) ? -1 : 0;
  return ACount * static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t));
}

// lowio's _write: a text handle's bytes translated (ANSI, UTF-8 or
// UTF-16LE), a binary handle's as they are (HookIODoWriteIOLocked's rules)
std::int64_t HookIODoLowWriteLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  if (AHandle.Text && (AHandle.LowText != 0))
  {
    // A Unicode text mode writes whole UTF-16 characters: an odd count
    // EINVAL
    if ((ASize % 2) != 0)
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return -1;
    }
    if (AHandle.LowText == 1)
      return HookIODoWriteUtf8Locked(AHandle, reinterpret_cast<const wchar_t*>(ABuffer),
        ASize / static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t)));
    return HookIODoWriteUtf16Locked(AHandle, reinterpret_cast<const wchar_t*>(ABuffer),
      ASize / static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t)));
  }
  if (AHandle.Text)
    return HookIODoWriteTextLocked(AHandle, ABuffer, ASize);
  return HookIODoWriteIOLocked(AHandle, ABuffer, ASize);
}

// fseek's rule, defined below; a write after reads on an update stream
// takes the fseek C requires there (HookIODoCrtPutLocked)
int HookIODoSeekLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t AOffset, const int AOrigin);

// ucrt's stdio buffer sizes (corecrt_internal_lowio.h _INTERNAL_BUFSIZ,
// _SMALL_BUFSIZ): a fill asks for the big size, the first fill after an
// fseek of a read-only stream for the small one
constexpr std::int64_t CHookIODoBufferSize = 4096;
constexpr std::int64_t CHookIODoSmallBufferSize = 512;

// lowio's read of the descriptor itself: up to ASize bytes of the IO at the
// handle's Position. -1: the read failed (errno EIO); a short count is the
// end. No stdio flag changes here: lowio has none.
std::int64_t HookIODoLowRawLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  std::int64_t LGot;

  // A descriptor opened without read access: the OS refuses (lowio EBADF)
  if (!HookIODoCanRead(AHandle))
  {
    errno = EBADF;
    return -1;
  }
  if (!HookIODoSyncLocked(AHandle))
  {
    errno = EIO;
    return -1;
  }
  LGot = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IORead(AHandle.Stream, ABuffer, ASize);
  if (LGot < 0)
    LGot = 0;
  AHandle.Position += LGot;
  if ((LGot == 0) && (ASize > 0) &&
    (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOStatus(AHandle.Stream) != ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOState::Eof))
  {
    errno = EIO;
    return -1;
  }
  return LGot;
}

// lowio's text translation of the ACount raw bytes just read into ABuffer,
// in place (ucrt translate_text_mode_nolock, a seekable file): "\r\n" is
// '\n', any other '\r' stays. LowCrlf records whether the raw bytes began
// with '\n'. A Ctrl-Z sets LowEof and ends the bytes delivered; Position
// stays at the end of the raw read. A '\r' that is the last raw byte reads
// one more: no byte keeps the '\r'; a '\n' that would be the only byte
// delivered is taken; otherwise the descriptor steps back onto it and the
// '\r' is kept only when it was not a '\n' (the next read starts with that
// '\n', a lone one). Returns the count delivered.
std::int64_t HookIODoLowTranslateLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ACount)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LFrom = 0;
  std::int64_t LTo = 0;
  unsigned char LPeek = 0;
  std::int64_t LPeekGot;
  int LErrno;

  LModel.LowCrlf = (ACount != 0) && (ABuffer[0] == '\n');
  while (LFrom < ACount)
  {
    if (ABuffer[LFrom] == CHookIODoCtrlZ)
    {
      LModel.LowEof = true;
      break;
    }
    if (ABuffer[LFrom] != '\r')
    {
      ABuffer[LTo] = ABuffer[LFrom];
      ++LTo;
      ++LFrom;
      continue;
    }
    if ((LFrom + 1) < ACount)
    {
      if (ABuffer[LFrom + 1] == '\n')
      {
        ABuffer[LTo] = '\n';
        LFrom += 2;
      }
      else
      {
        ABuffer[LTo] = '\r';
        ++LFrom;
      }
      ++LTo;
      continue;
    }
    // The '\r' is the last raw byte: look at the next one. A failed look
    // is no byte (ucrt's ReadFile failure leaves errno alone)
    ++LFrom;
    LErrno = errno;
    LPeekGot = HookIODoLowRawLocked(AHandle, &LPeek, 1);
    errno = LErrno;
    if (LPeekGot != 1)
    {
      ABuffer[LTo] = '\r';
      ++LTo;
      continue;
    }
    if ((LPeek == '\n') && (LTo == 0))
    {
      ABuffer[LTo] = '\n';
      ++LTo;
      continue;
    }
    // A seek back (lowio's lseek clears LowEof, which is not set here)
    AHandle.Position -= 1;
    LModel.LowEof = false;
    if (LPeek != '\n')
    {
      ABuffer[LTo] = '\r';
      ++LTo;
    }
  }
  return LTo;
}

// The UTF-16LE form of HookIODoLowTranslateLocked (ucrt
// translate_text_mode_nolock<wchar_t>): the same rules on ACount wide
// characters in place, the peek and the step back one wide character (2
// bytes). Returns the bytes delivered.
std::int64_t HookIODoLowTranslateWideLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, wchar_t* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ACount)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LFrom = 0;
  std::int64_t LTo = 0;
  wchar_t LPeek = 0;
  std::int64_t LPeekGot;
  int LErrno;

  LModel.LowCrlf = (ACount != 0) && (ABuffer[0] == L'\n');
  while (LFrom < ACount)
  {
    if (ABuffer[LFrom] == static_cast<wchar_t>(CHookIODoCtrlZ))
    {
      LModel.LowEof = true;
      break;
    }
    if (ABuffer[LFrom] != L'\r')
    {
      ABuffer[LTo++] = ABuffer[LFrom++];
      continue;
    }
    if ((LFrom + 1) < ACount)
    {
      if (ABuffer[LFrom + 1] == L'\n')
      {
        ABuffer[LTo++] = L'\n';
        LFrom += 2;
      }
      else
        ABuffer[LTo++] = ABuffer[LFrom++];
      continue;
    }
    ++LFrom;
    LErrno = errno;
    LPeekGot = HookIODoLowRawLocked(AHandle, reinterpret_cast<unsigned char*>(&LPeek),
      static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(LPeek)));
    errno = LErrno;
    if (LPeekGot <= 0)
    {
      ABuffer[LTo++] = L'\r';
      continue;
    }
    if ((LPeek == L'\n') && (LTo == 0))
    {
      ABuffer[LTo++] = L'\n';
      continue;
    }
    // ucrt steps back one wide character whatever the peek read
    AHandle.Position -= static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t));
    LModel.LowEof = false;
    if (LPeek != L'\n')
      ABuffer[LTo++] = L'\r';
  }
  return LTo * static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t));
}

// ucrt's _lookuptrailbytes: the trail bytes a UTF-8 lead byte announces (0
// for an ASCII byte, a trail byte or an invalid one)
int HookIODoUtf8Trail(const unsigned char AByte)
{
  if ((AByte >= 0xC0) && (AByte <= 0xDF))
    return 1;
  if ((AByte >= 0xE0) && (AByte <= 0xEF))
    return 2;
  if ((AByte >= 0xF0) && (AByte <= 0xF7))
    return 3;
  return 0;
}

// lowio's UTF-8 read (read.cpp _read_nolock + translate_ansi_or_utf8_nolock):
// ASize (even) bytes of UTF-16 asked for; half as many raw bytes (at least
// 4) read from StartPos, text-translated as ANSI bytes; an incomplete last
// character steps the descriptor back over it; the rest converted from
// UTF-8 to UTF-16 into ABuffer (MultiByteToWideChar, flags 0). A lead byte
// with no character is EILSEQ (-1). Returns the UTF-16 bytes.
std::int64_t HookIODoLowReadUtf8Locked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  std::vector<unsigned char> LRaw;
  std::int64_t LWant = ASize / 2;
  std::int64_t LGot;
  std::int64_t LEnd;
  std::int64_t LCounter;
  int LTrail;
  int LChars;

  if (LWant < 4)
    LWant = 4;
  LRaw.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(LWant), 0);
  AHandle.StartPos = AHandle.Position;
  LGot = HookIODoLowRawLocked(AHandle, LRaw.data(), LWant);
  if (LGot < 0)
    return -1;
  LGot = HookIODoLowTranslateLocked(AHandle, LRaw.data(), LGot);
  if (LGot == 0)
    return 0;
  LEnd = LGot - 1;
  if ((LRaw[static_cast<std::size_t>(LEnd)] & 0x80) == 0)
    LEnd = LGot;
  else
  {
    LCounter = 1;
    while ((HookIODoUtf8Trail(LRaw[static_cast<std::size_t>(LEnd)]) == 0) && (LCounter <= 4) &&
      (LEnd > 0))
    {
      --LEnd;
      ++LCounter;
    }
    LTrail = HookIODoUtf8Trail(LRaw[static_cast<std::size_t>(LEnd)]);
    if (LTrail == 0)
    {
      errno = EILSEQ;
      return -1;
    }
    if ((LTrail + 1) == LCounter)
      LEnd += LCounter;
    else
    {
      // The partial character is read again by the next read (lowio's
      // lseek back, which clears FEOFLAG)
      AHandle.Position -= LCounter;
      AHandle.Crt.LowEof = false;
    }
  }
  if (LEnd == 0)
  {
    AHandle.Utf8Translated = false;
    return 0;
  }
  LChars = MultiByteToWideChar(CP_UTF8, 0, reinterpret_cast<const char*>(LRaw.data()),
    static_cast<int>(LEnd), reinterpret_cast<wchar_t*>(ABuffer),
    static_cast<int>(ASize / static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t))));
  if (LChars == 0)
  {
    errno = (GetLastError() == ERROR_NO_UNICODE_TRANSLATION) ? EILSEQ : EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  AHandle.Utf8Translated = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LChars) != LEnd;
  return static_cast<std::int64_t>(LChars) * static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t));
}

// lowio's _read: 0 at the end (a text handle: also after a Ctrl-Z,
// LowEof), -1 on a failure (errno EIO), else the count (a text handle's
// translated; a Unicode text mode's in UTF-16 bytes)
std::int64_t HookIODoLowReadLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  std::int64_t LGot;

  if ((ASize == 0) || AHandle.Crt.LowEof)
    return 0;
  // A Unicode text mode reads whole UTF-16 characters: an odd count EINVAL
  if (AHandle.Text && (AHandle.LowText != 0) && ((ASize % 2) != 0))
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  if (AHandle.Text && (AHandle.LowText == 1))
    return HookIODoLowReadUtf8Locked(AHandle, ABuffer, ASize);
  LGot = HookIODoLowRawLocked(AHandle, ABuffer, ASize);
  if (LGot < 0)
    return -1;
  if (!AHandle.Text)
    return LGot;
  if (AHandle.LowText == 2)
    return HookIODoLowTranslateWideLocked(AHandle, reinterpret_cast<wchar_t*>(ABuffer),
      LGot / static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t)));
  return HookIODoLowTranslateLocked(AHandle, ABuffer, LGot);
}

// ucrt's open text mode (open.cpp configure_text_mode) for a ccs= open: a
// binary open stays ANSI; UTF-8 / UTF-16LE as named; UNICODE is UTF-16LE
// only for "w" (write-only, created, truncated), else ANSI until a BOM says
// more. The BOM: a read-only open ("r") reads it; a writing open of an
// existing IO ("r+", "a", "a+": OPEN_EXISTING / OPEN_ALWAYS) reads it when
// the IO is not empty (an "a" open asks for read access too) and writes it
// when it is; a truncating open ("w", "w+") writes it. The read takes 3
// bytes as lowio does at that point (ANSI text): EF BB BF is UTF-8 (the
// place stays after it); else its first two FE FF are UTF-16BE (EINVAL, the
// open fails), FF FE UTF-16LE (the place 2); else the place goes back to
// 0. The BOM written is FF FE (UTF-16LE) or EF BB BF (UTF-8), none in ANSI.
// An IO that cannot be read where an "a" open would read the BOM keeps the
// default mode (ucrt's write-only retry). False: errno set, the open fails.
bool HookIODoConfigureTextMode(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const HookIODoOpenMode& AParsed)
{
  unsigned char LBom[3] = {0, 0, 0};
  std::int64_t LGot;
  std::int64_t LSize;
  bool LCheck = false;
  bool LWrite = false;
  int LMode = 0;
  // lowio's place moves (its lseek clears FEOFLAG); a failed move EINVAL
  auto LSeekTo = [&](const std::int64_t APlace) -> bool
  {
    if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, APlace,
      ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromStart) != APlace)
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return false;
    }
    AHandle.Position = APlace;
    AHandle.Crt.LowEof = false;
    return true;
  };
  // The BOM read: the IO's bytes at the place, as ANSI text (lowio reads
  // with GENERIC_READ even for "a", so the handle's own mode is not asked)
  auto LReadBom = [&]() -> std::int64_t
  {
    std::int64_t LRead;
    // An "a" open of an IOSource entry holds a write-only IO: the BOM is
    // read through a read view of the same entry, as lowio's own open
    // asks GENERIC_READ for it (open.cpp decode_access_flags); none = the
    // write-only retry, the default mode
    if ((AParsed.First == 'a') && (!AParsed.Plus) && (AHandle.Source != nullptr))
    {
      HookIODoIO LView = nullptr;
      try
      {
        LView = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceOpen(AHandle.Source, AHandle.EntryName,
          HookIODoMode::Read);
      }
      catch (...)
      {
        LView = nullptr;
      }
      if (LView == nullptr)
        return -1;
      LRead = -1;
      if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(LView, AHandle.Position,
        ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromStart) == AHandle.Position)
        LRead = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IORead(LView, LBom, 3);
      ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOClose(LView);
      if (LRead < 0)
        return -1;
      AHandle.Position += LRead;
      return HookIODoLowTranslateLocked(AHandle, LBom, LRead);
    }
    if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, AHandle.Position,
      ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromStart) != AHandle.Position)
      return -1;
    LRead = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IORead(AHandle.Stream, LBom, 3);
    if (LRead < 0)
      return -1;
    AHandle.Position += LRead;
    return HookIODoLowTranslateLocked(AHandle, LBom, LRead);
  };

  AHandle.LowText = 0;
  // _tm_unicode = (oflag & _O_WTEXT): ccs=UNICODE, binary or text
  AHandle.WideText = AParsed.Encoded && (AParsed.Encoding == 3);
  if ((!AParsed.Encoded) || (!AHandle.Text))
    return true;
  if (AParsed.Encoding == 1)
    LMode = 1;
  else if (AParsed.Encoding == 2)
    LMode = 2;
  else if ((AParsed.First == 'w') && (!AParsed.Plus))
    LMode = 2;
  if (AParsed.First == 'w')
    LWrite = true;
  else if ((AParsed.First == 'r') && (!AParsed.Plus))
    LCheck = true;
  else
  {
    LSize = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSize(AHandle.Stream);
    if (LSize != 0)
    {
      if (!LSeekTo(0))
        return false;
      LCheck = true;
    }
    else
      LWrite = true;
  }
  if (LCheck)
  {
    LGot = LReadBom();
    // An "a" open's IO that refuses a read keeps the default mode (ucrt's
    // write-only retry assumes it)
    if ((LGot < 0) && (AParsed.First == 'a') && (!AParsed.Plus))
      LGot = 0;
    if (LGot < 0)
    {
      errno = EIO;
      return false;
    }
    if ((LGot == 3) && (LBom[0] == 0xEF) && (LBom[1] == 0xBB) && (LBom[2] == 0xBF))
      LMode = 1;
    else if ((LGot >= 2) && (LBom[0] == 0xFE) && (LBom[1] == 0xFF))
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return false;
    }
    else if ((LGot >= 2) && (LBom[0] == 0xFF) && (LBom[1] == 0xFE))
    {
      if (!LSeekTo(2))
        return false;
      LMode = 2;
    }
    else if (!LSeekTo(0))
      return false;
  }
  if (LWrite && (LMode != 0))
  {
    const unsigned char LUtf16[2] = {0xFF, 0xFE};
    const unsigned char LUtf8[3] = {0xEF, 0xBB, 0xBF};
    const bool LIsUtf16 = LMode == 2;
    const std::int64_t LLength = LIsUtf16 ? 2 : 3;
    if (HookIODoWriteIOLocked(AHandle, LIsUtf16 ? LUtf16 : LUtf8, LLength) != LLength)
      return false;
  }
  // An "a" open asked GENERIC_READ only for the BOM: lowio closes that
  // descriptor and opens the file again write-only (open.cpp, after the
  // text mode), so its place starts again at 0 (each write then goes to the
  // end, FAPPEND): measured, tests\probe\hookabi\ccs_real.c ftell 0
  if ((AParsed.First == 'a') && (!AParsed.Plus))
  {
    AHandle.Position = 0;
    AHandle.Crt.LowEof = false;
  }
  AHandle.LowText = LMode;
  return true;
}

// ucrt's buffer allocation (_getbuf.cpp __acrt_stdio_allocate_buffer_nolock),
// once: the big size, empty (Ptr and Count 0). Out of memory here is
// HookIODoWith's ENOMEM.
void HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (LModel.HasBuffer)
    return;
  LModel.Buffer.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(CHookIODoBufferSize), 0);
  LModel.BufferSize = CHookIODoBufferSize;
  LModel.HasBuffer = true;
  LModel.Kind = HookIODoUcrtBuffer::Crt;
  LModel.Ptr = 0;
  LModel.Count = 0;
}

// The small fill size after an fseek, and ftell's estimate of a short
// fill, apply only to a buffer ucrt made itself on its own
// (has_crt_buffer() && !_IOBUFFER_SETVBUF)
bool HookIODoCrtOwnBuffer(const HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  return AModel.HasBuffer && (AModel.Kind == HookIODoUcrtBuffer::Crt) && (!AModel.SetvbufBuffer);
}

// ucrt's has_big_buffer(): a buffer ucrt or the caller made, not _IONBF's
// 2-byte _charbuf
bool HookIODoCrtBigBuffer(const HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  return AModel.HasBuffer && (AModel.Kind != HookIODoUcrtBuffer::Single);
}

// ucrt's buffer flush (fflush.cpp __acrt_stdio_flush_nolock): only a
// stream that writes and does not read, with a big buffer, flushes. The
// buffer empties (Ptr, Count 0), then its [0, Ptr) bytes go to lowio; a
// short write sets Failed and is EOF. An update stream that wrote bytes
// stops writing; one that had none to write keeps writing (ucrt returns
// before that step). Returns 0 or EOF.
int HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LBytes;

  if (LModel.StreamRead || (!LModel.StreamWrite) || (!HookIODoCrtBigBuffer(LModel)))
    return 0;
  LBytes = LModel.Ptr;
  LModel.Ptr = 0;
  LModel.Count = 0;
  if (LBytes <= 0)
    return 0;
  if (HookIODoLowWriteLocked(AHandle, LModel.Buffer.data(), LBytes) != LBytes)
  {
    AHandle.Failed = true;
    return EOF;
  }
  if (LModel.StreamUpdate)
    LModel.StreamWrite = false;
  return 0;
}

// A read form on an update stream that holds written bytes, where ucrt's
// read would take the buffer's stale bytes past them (fgetc, fread, a scan,
// while the buffer has room left) or read past them straight from lowio
// (ADirect: fread's direct path is next), after which no flush ever
// writes them. C requires an fflush between a write and a read; the read
// takes it here (HookIODoCrtFlushLocked), so the written bytes land and
// the read starts at the caller's place. Where ucrt itself refuses the
// read (_filbuf on a writing stream) nothing is flushed. False: the flush
// failed (Failed is set; the read reads nothing).
// A write-only stream ("w", "a") holding written bytes would hand back the
// buffer's stale bytes the same way; it is refused as ucrt's _filbuf
// refuses a writing stream (Failed, errno untouched, false).
bool HookIODoCrtLeaveWriteLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const bool ADirect)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if ((!LModel.StreamUpdate) && LModel.StreamWrite && (!LModel.StreamRead) && (LModel.Count > 0))
  {
    AHandle.Failed = true;
    return false;
  }
  if ((!LModel.StreamUpdate) || (!LModel.StreamWrite) || LModel.StreamRead || (LModel.Ptr == 0))
    return true;
  if ((LModel.Count <= 0) && (!ADirect))
    return true;
  return HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(AHandle) == 0;
}

// ucrt's refill (_filbuf.cpp common_refill_and_read_nolock): the buffer is
// made on the first fill, filled with up to BufferSize translated bytes and
// its first byte returned. Nothing read: EOF with AtEnd (the end) or Failed
// (a failure). A read-only stream whose fill met a Ctrl-Z sets StreamCtrlZ;
// a fill at the small size puts the big size back for the next one. A
// stream that writes is refused: Failed, EOF, errno untouched.
int HookIODoCrtRefillLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LGot;

  if (LModel.StreamWrite)
  {
    AHandle.Failed = true;
    return EOF;
  }
  LModel.StreamRead = true;
  HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
  LModel.Ptr = 0;
  LGot = HookIODoLowReadLocked(AHandle, LModel.Buffer.data(), LModel.BufferSize);
  if (LGot <= 0)
  {
    if (LGot < 0)
      AHandle.Failed = true;
    else
      AHandle.AtEnd = true;
    LModel.Count = 0;
    return EOF;
  }
  LModel.Count = LGot;
  if ((!LModel.StreamWrite) && (!LModel.StreamUpdate) && LModel.LowEof)
    LModel.StreamCtrlZ = true;
  if ((LModel.BufferSize == CHookIODoSmallBufferSize) && HookIODoCrtOwnBuffer(LModel))
    LModel.BufferSize = CHookIODoBufferSize;
  --LModel.Count;
  return static_cast<int>(LModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.Ptr++)]);
}

// A read of up to ASize bytes, as ucrt's fread (fread.cpp
// _fread_nolock_s): the buffer's bytes first; with the buffer empty, a
// request of at least one buffer's size reads the largest whole multiple of
// it straight from lowio, bypassing the buffer; a smaller one refills. A
// short count at the end sets AtEnd, after a failure Failed. fgetc / getc /
// fgets (one byte at a time) take the same path, as ucrt's do. Written
// bytes still in the buffer are flushed first where ucrt would read past
// them (HookIODoCrtLeaveWriteLocked).
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtReadLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LDone = 0;
  std::int64_t LStreamBufferSize;
  std::int64_t LRemaining;
  std::int64_t LTake;
  std::int64_t LLimit;
  std::int64_t LGot;
  int LByte;

  LStreamBufferSize = LModel.HasBuffer ? LModel.BufferSize : CHookIODoBufferSize;
  if (!HookIODoCrtLeaveWriteLocked(AHandle, ASize >= LStreamBufferSize))
    return 0;
  while (LDone < ASize)
  {
    LRemaining = ASize - LDone;
    if (LModel.HasBuffer && (LModel.Count != 0))
    {
      LTake = (LRemaining < LModel.Count) ? LRemaining : LModel.Count;
      std::memcpy(ABuffer + LDone, LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.Ptr,
        static_cast<std::size_t>(LTake));
      LModel.Count -= LTake;
      LModel.Ptr += LTake;
      LDone += LTake;
    }
    else if (LRemaining >= LStreamBufferSize)
    {
      // lowio reads at most INT_MAX bytes at a time
      LLimit = (LRemaining > static_cast<std::int64_t>(INT_MAX))
        ? static_cast<std::int64_t>(INT_MAX) : LRemaining;
      LTake = LLimit - (LLimit % LStreamBufferSize);
      // The buffer no longer holds what precedes the place
      LModel.Ptr = 0;
      LModel.Count = 0;
      LGot = HookIODoLowReadLocked(AHandle, ABuffer + LDone, LTake);
      if (LGot == 0)
      {
        AHandle.AtEnd = true;
        break;
      }
      if (LGot < 0)
      {
        AHandle.Failed = true;
        break;
      }
      LDone += LGot;
    }
    else
    {
      LByte = HookIODoCrtRefillLocked(AHandle);
      if (LByte == EOF)
        break;
      ABuffer[LDone] = static_cast<unsigned char>(LByte);
      ++LDone;
      LStreamBufferSize = LModel.BufferSize;
    }
  }
  return LDone;
}

// The '\n' bytes in [AFirst, ALast) of the buffer
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtNewlines(const HookIODoCrtModel& AModel, const std::int64_t AFirst,
  const std::int64_t ALast)
{
  std::int64_t LCount = 0;

  for (std::int64_t LI = AFirst; LI < ALast; ++LI)
    if (AModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LI)] == '\n')
      ++LCount;
  return LCount;
}

// The newlines in the buffer's bytes [AFirst, ALast): AWide counts L'\n'
// wide characters (a Unicode text mode's UTF-16 buffer), else '\n' bytes
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtNewlinesSized(const HookIODoCrtModel& AModel, const std::int64_t AFirst,
  const std::int64_t ALast, const bool AWide)
{
  std::int64_t LCount = 0;
  wchar_t LChar;

  if (!AWide)
    return HookIODoCrtNewlines(AModel, AFirst, ALast);
  for (std::int64_t LI = AFirst; (LI + 1) < ALast; LI += 2)
  {
    std::memcpy(&LChar, AModel.Buffer.data() + LI, sizeof(LChar));
    if (LChar == L'\n')
      ++LCount;
  }
  return LCount;
}

// ucrt's ftell of a UTF-8 text stream whose last read changed the
// character count (ftell.cpp common_ftell_translated_utf8_nolock): with
// nothing left in the buffer the descriptor's place; otherwise the raw
// bytes from StartPos (one big buffer's worth) are read again, the
// descriptor put back, and walked one character per UTF-16 character
// before Ptr ("\r\n" one, a lead byte with its trail bytes one); -1 when a
// move or the read fails, or the raw bytes are fewer than the characters.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtTellUtf8Locked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t ALow)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::vector<unsigned char> LRaw;
  const std::int64_t LCurrent = LModel.Ptr / static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t));
  std::int64_t LGot;
  std::int64_t LIt = 0;

  if (LModel.Count == 0)
    return ALow;
  LRaw.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(CHookIODoBufferSize), 0);
  if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, AHandle.StartPos,
    ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromStart) != AHandle.StartPos)
    return -1;
  LGot = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IORead(AHandle.Stream, LRaw.data(), CHookIODoBufferSize);
  if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, ALow, ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromStart)
    != ALow)
    return -1;
  if (LGot < 0)
    return -1;
  if (LCurrent > LGot)
    return -1;
  for (std::int64_t LI = 0; (LI != LCurrent) && (LIt < LGot); ++LI, ++LIt)
  {
    if (LRaw[static_cast<std::size_t>(LIt)] == '\r')
    {
      if ((LIt < (LGot - 1)) && (LRaw[static_cast<std::size_t>(LIt + 1)] == '\n'))
        ++LIt;
    }
    else
      LIt += HookIODoUtf8Trail(LRaw[static_cast<std::size_t>(LIt)]);
  }
  return AHandle.StartPos + LIt;
}

// ucrt's ftell (ftell.cpp common_ftell_nolock and
// common_ftell_read_mode_nolock), ungot bytes in the buffer counted as the
// buffer's own. ucrt finds the descriptor's place with an lseek, and
// lowio's lseek clears FEOFLAG: so does this (a read that met a Ctrl-Z goes
// on past it). A binary stream in read mode is the place minus the bytes
// left. A text stream counts each newline before Ptr twice and, in read
// mode with bytes left in the buffer, estimates the buffer's raw size as
// ucrt does: at the end of the IO its bytes plus one per newline (plus the
// Ctrl-Z of StreamCtrlZ), elsewhere the small size for a fill of at most
// that many bytes, else BufferSize, plus one when LowCrlf. A Unicode text
// mode (ccs=) counts in UTF-16 (a newline or the Ctrl-Z 2 bytes), and a
// UTF-8 one halves the buffer's sizes (or walks the raw bytes when its
// read changed the character count). -1 with EINVAL for a stream that
// neither reads, writes nor updates. No sign check (ucrt has none): an
// ungot '\n' at the front can make a text place negative.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtTellLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  const std::int64_t LLow = AHandle.Position;
  std::int64_t LOffset;
  std::int64_t LBytes;
  std::int64_t LEnd;

  // A Unicode text mode's buffer holds UTF-16: newlines are wide ones (2
  // bytes each), a UTF-8 file's bytes are counted at half (ftell.cpp
  // translation_factor), every other character size 1
  const bool LWideBuffer = AHandle.Text && (AHandle.LowText != 0);
  const std::int64_t LCharSize = LWideBuffer ? 2 : 1;
  const std::int64_t LFactor = (AHandle.Text && (AHandle.LowText == 1)) ? 2 : 1;

  // ucrt's ftell first sets a negative count to 0 (ftell.cpp): a putc
  // refused by _flsbuf (a read-only stream) leaves the count at -1
  if (LModel.Count < 0)
    LModel.Count = 0;
  LModel.LowEof = false;
  // No buffer, or the _IONBF one (not a "big" buffer): text mode too
  if ((!LModel.HasBuffer) || (LModel.Kind == HookIODoUcrtBuffer::Single))
    return LLow - LModel.Count;
  LOffset = LModel.Ptr;
  if (LModel.StreamRead || LModel.StreamWrite)
  {
    // A UTF-8 read whose characters differ in count from its bytes: the
    // place is found again from the raw bytes (common_ftell_translated_utf8)
    if (AHandle.Text && (AHandle.LowText == 1) && AHandle.Utf8Translated)
      return HookIODoCrtTellUtf8Locked(AHandle, LLow);
    if (AHandle.Text)
      LOffset += HookIODoCrtNewlinesSized(LModel, 0, LModel.Ptr, LWideBuffer) * LCharSize;
  }
  else if (!LModel.StreamUpdate)
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  if (LLow == 0)
    return LOffset;
  if (!LModel.StreamRead)
    return LLow + (LOffset / LFactor);
  if (LModel.Count == 0)
    return LLow;
  LBytes = LModel.Count + LModel.Ptr;
  // Binary: lowio - (Count + Ptr) + Ptr
  if (!AHandle.Text)
    return LLow - LModel.Count;
  // An IO with no size is never "at the end" (ucrt's lseek to the end
  // failed)
  LEnd = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSize(AHandle.Stream);
  if (LEnd == LLow)
  {
    LBytes += HookIODoCrtNewlinesSized(LModel, 0, LBytes, LWideBuffer) * LCharSize;
    if (LModel.StreamCtrlZ)
      LBytes += LCharSize;
  }
  else
  {
    if ((LBytes <= CHookIODoSmallBufferSize) && HookIODoCrtOwnBuffer(LModel))
      LBytes = CHookIODoSmallBufferSize;
    else
      LBytes = LModel.BufferSize;
    if (LModel.LowCrlf)
      LBytes += LCharSize;
  }
  return LLow - (LBytes / LFactor) + (LOffset / LFactor);
}

// ucrt's buffer drop on fseek / rewind (__acrt_stdio_reset_buffer and the
// flag rules after it): the buffer empties (ungetc's bytes with it); an
// update stream forgets whether it read or wrote; a read-only stream's next
// fill asks for the small size after an fseek (ASmallBuffer), not after a
// rewind.
void HookIODoCrtResetLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const bool ASmallBuffer)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  LModel.Ptr = 0;
  LModel.Count = 0;
  if (LModel.StreamUpdate)
  {
    LModel.StreamRead = false;
    LModel.StreamWrite = false;
  }
  else if (ASmallBuffer && LModel.StreamRead && HookIODoCrtOwnBuffer(LModel))
    LModel.BufferSize = CHookIODoSmallBufferSize;
}

// ucrt's fseek fast track for a read-only binary stream
// (fseek.cpp common_fseek_binary_mode_read_only_fast_track_nolock): a
// target from the start or the caller's place that lies within the buffer
// (back to its start, on to its last byte read ahead) only moves Ptr; the
// buffer, the descriptor and the next fill's size stay. The start's place
// is taken as the descriptor's place minus the bytes left. True: done.
bool HookIODoCrtSeekInBufferLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t AOffset,
  const int AOrigin)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LMove = AOffset;

  if (AOrigin == SEEK_END)
    return false;
  if ((!LModel.HasBuffer) || LModel.StreamWrite || LModel.StreamUpdate)
    return false;
  if (LModel.Count <= 0)
    return false;
  if (AHandle.Text)
    return false;
  if (AOrigin == SEEK_SET)
  {
    // ucrt refuses the fast track when the difference overflows
    const std::int64_t LHere = AHandle.Position - LModel.Count;
    if (((LHere < 0) && (AOffset > (INT64_MAX + LHere)))
      || ((LHere > 0) && (AOffset < (INT64_MIN + LHere))))
      return false;
    LMove = AOffset - LHere;
  }
  if ((LMove < -LModel.Ptr) || (LMove > LModel.Count))
    return false;
  LModel.Ptr += LMove;
  LModel.Count -= LMove;
  return true;
}

// One byte as ucrt's _fgetc_nolock reads it: the buffer's next byte, a
// refill when the buffer is empty (EOF as the refill gives it). Written
// bytes in the buffer are flushed first (HookIODoCrtLeaveWriteLocked).
int HookIODoCrtGetLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (!HookIODoCrtLeaveWriteLocked(AHandle, false))
    return EOF;
  if (LModel.HasBuffer && (LModel.Count != 0))
  {
    --LModel.Count;
    return static_cast<int>(LModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.Ptr++)]);
  }
  return HookIODoCrtRefillLocked(AHandle);
}

// ACount bytes read as that many HookIODoCrtGetLocked calls would read
// them (never fread's direct path, which a scan's getc does not take): the
// buffer's bytes in bulk, a refill each time it is empty. Returns the count
// read; short only at the end or a failure (the refill's flags).
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtSkipLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t ACount)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LDone = 0;
  std::int64_t LTake;

  if ((ACount > 0) && (!HookIODoCrtLeaveWriteLocked(AHandle, false)))
    return 0;
  while (LDone < ACount)
  {
    if (LModel.HasBuffer && (LModel.Count != 0))
    {
      LTake = ACount - LDone;
      if (LTake > LModel.Count)
        LTake = LModel.Count;
      LModel.Count -= LTake;
      LModel.Ptr += LTake;
      LDone += LTake;
    }
    else if (HookIODoCrtRefillLocked(AHandle) == EOF)
      break;
    else
      ++LDone;
  }
  return LDone;
}

// ucrt's ungetc (ungetc.cpp _ungetc_nolock, a file-backed stream, text or
// binary alike): AChar goes into the buffer in front of the next byte. Refused
// (EOF) for EOF itself, for a stream that has not read unless it is an
// update stream that writes, and when the next byte is already the
// buffer's first while bytes are left (one ungot byte at the front, no room
// for another). A stream with no buffer gets one first; at the front of an
// empty buffer the byte takes its first slot. AtEnd is cleared, the stream
// counts as reading. Returns the byte (0..255) or EOF.
// On an update stream holding written bytes ucrt puts the byte over the
// last one written, and the stream then reads, so no flush writes the rest
// (they are lost). Here the ungetc behaves as after the fflush C requires
// before a read: the written bytes land, the stream no longer writes, and
// ucrt's rule then refuses the byte (EOF).
int HookIODoCrtUngetLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const int AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (AChar == EOF)
    return EOF;
  if (LModel.StreamUpdate && (!LModel.StreamRead) && (LModel.Ptr != 0)
    && (HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
    return EOF;
  if ((!LModel.StreamRead) && (!(LModel.StreamUpdate && LModel.StreamWrite)))
    return EOF;
  HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
  if (LModel.Ptr == 0)
  {
    if (LModel.Count != 0)
      return EOF;
    LModel.Ptr = 1;
  }
  --LModel.Ptr;
  LModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.Ptr)] = static_cast<unsigned char>(AChar);
  ++LModel.Count;
  AHandle.AtEnd = false;
  LModel.StreamRead = true;
  return AChar & 0xFF;
}

// ucrt's wide refill (_filbuf.cpp common_refill_and_read_nolock<wchar_t>):
// the narrow refill's rules, plus a character split over the fill: one byte
// left before the fill is the low byte, the fill's first the high byte. A
// fill of 0 or 1 byte is no character: 0 sets AtEnd, 1 (and a failure)
// Failed, as ucrt's validity test does. Returns the character or WEOF.
wint_t HookIODoCrtRefillWideLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LGot;
  bool LSplit = false;
  unsigned char LLow = 0;
  wchar_t LChar;

  if (LModel.StreamWrite)
  {
    AHandle.Failed = true;
    return WEOF;
  }
  LModel.StreamRead = true;
  HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
  if (LModel.Count == 1)
  {
    LSplit = true;
    LLow = LModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.Ptr)];
  }
  LModel.Ptr = 0;
  LGot = HookIODoLowReadLocked(AHandle, LModel.Buffer.data(), LModel.BufferSize);
  if ((LGot == 0) || (LGot == 1) || (LGot < 0))
  {
    if (LGot != 0)
      AHandle.Failed = true;
    else
      AHandle.AtEnd = true;
    LModel.Count = 0;
    return WEOF;
  }
  LModel.Count = LGot;
  if ((!LModel.StreamWrite) && (!LModel.StreamUpdate) && LModel.LowEof)
    LModel.StreamCtrlZ = true;
  if ((LModel.BufferSize == CHookIODoSmallBufferSize) && HookIODoCrtOwnBuffer(LModel))
    LModel.BufferSize = CHookIODoBufferSize;
  if (LSplit)
  {
    LChar = static_cast<wchar_t>((static_cast<unsigned int>(LModel.Buffer[0]) << 8) | LLow);
    --LModel.Count;
    ++LModel.Ptr;
    return static_cast<wint_t>(LChar);
  }
  std::memcpy(&LChar, LModel.Buffer.data(), sizeof(LChar));
  LModel.Count -= 2;
  LModel.Ptr += 2;
  return static_cast<wint_t>(LChar);
}

// ucrt's _fgetwc_nolock on a file stream. Text (ANSI) mode: one byte by
// getc, a second when the current locale calls it a lead byte (the end
// there puts the first back with ungetc, as ucrt's does: WEOF), then
// mbtowc (-1: errno EILSEQ, WEOF). Binary: two bytes from the buffer, else
// the wide refill. Written bytes are settled as getc settles them.
wint_t HookIODoCrtGetWideLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  char LBytes[4] = {0, 0, 0, 0};
  int LSize = 1;
  int LByte;
  wchar_t LChar = 0;

  // A Unicode text mode (ccs=): two bytes by getc (lowio delivers UTF-16
  // for both UTF-8 and UTF-16LE files); the end on either is WEOF
  if (AHandle.Text && (AHandle.LowText != 0))
  {
    unsigned char LPair[2];
    for (int LI = 0; LI < 2; ++LI)
    {
      LByte = HookIODoCrtGetLocked(AHandle);
      if (LByte == EOF)
        return WEOF;
      LPair[LI] = static_cast<unsigned char>(LByte);
    }
    std::memcpy(&LChar, LPair, sizeof(LChar));
    return static_cast<wint_t>(LChar);
  }
  if (AHandle.Text)
  {
    LByte = HookIODoCrtGetLocked(AHandle);
    if (LByte == EOF)
      return WEOF;
    LBytes[0] = static_cast<char>(LByte);
    if (isleadbyte(static_cast<unsigned char>(LBytes[0])))
    {
      LByte = HookIODoCrtGetLocked(AHandle);
      if (LByte == EOF)
      {
        HookIODoCrtUngetLocked(AHandle, static_cast<int>(LBytes[0]));
        return WEOF;
      }
      LBytes[1] = static_cast<char>(LByte);
      LSize = 2;
    }
    if (std::mbtowc(&LChar, LBytes, static_cast<std::size_t>(LSize)) == -1)
    {
      errno = EILSEQ;
      return WEOF;
    }
    return static_cast<wint_t>(LChar);
  }
  if (!HookIODoCrtLeaveWriteLocked(AHandle, false))
    return WEOF;
  if (LModel.HasBuffer && (LModel.Count >= static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t))))
  {
    std::memcpy(&LChar, LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.Ptr, sizeof(LChar));
    LModel.Count -= 2;
    LModel.Ptr += 2;
    return static_cast<wint_t>(LChar);
  }
  return HookIODoCrtRefillWideLocked(AHandle);
}

// ucrt's ungetwc (ungetwc.cpp _ungetwc_nolock, a file stream): WEOF refused;
// refused for a stream that neither reads nor is an update stream that is
// not writing (an update stream holding written bytes makes C's fflush
// first: they land and it no longer writes). A stream with no buffer gets
// one. Text (ANSI) mode: the character as wctomb_s makes it in the current
// locale (its failure: WEOF, its errno); binary: its 2 raw bytes. With no
// room before Ptr: refused while bytes are left, or when the buffer is
// smaller than the bytes; else Ptr moves to just past them. The bytes go in
// front, AtEnd cleared, the stream reads. Returns the character (text:
// masked to 16 bits) or WEOF.
wint_t HookIODoCrtUngetWideLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wint_t AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  char LBytes[MB_LEN_MAX] = {0};
  int LCount = 0;
  const wchar_t LWide = static_cast<wchar_t>(AChar);

  if (AChar == WEOF)
    return WEOF;
  if (LModel.StreamUpdate && LModel.StreamWrite && (!LModel.StreamRead)
    && (HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
    return WEOF;
  if ((!LModel.StreamRead) && (!(LModel.StreamUpdate && (!LModel.StreamWrite))))
    return WEOF;
  HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
  // ANSI text: converted by the locale; a Unicode text mode (ccs=) keeps
  // the 2 raw bytes (lowio converted them on the way in)
  if (AHandle.Text && (AHandle.LowText == 0))
  {
    if (wctomb_s(&LCount, LBytes, MB_LEN_MAX, LWide) != 0)
      return WEOF;
  }
  else
  {
    std::memcpy(LBytes, &LWide, sizeof(LWide));
    LCount = 2;
  }
  if (LModel.Ptr < LCount)
  {
    if (LModel.Count != 0)
      return WEOF;
    if (LCount > LModel.BufferSize)
      return WEOF;
    LModel.Ptr = LCount;
  }
  for (int LI = LCount - 1; LI >= 0; --LI)
  {
    --LModel.Ptr;
    LModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.Ptr)] = static_cast<unsigned char>(LBytes[LI]);
  }
  LModel.Count += LCount;
  AHandle.AtEnd = false;
  LModel.StreamRead = true;
  if (AHandle.Text)
    return static_cast<wint_t>(0xFFFF & AChar);
  return static_cast<wint_t>(LWide);
}

// ucrt's setvbuf (setvbuf.cpp _setvbuf_internal, setbuf.cpp): AMode must
// be _IOFBF, _IOLBF or _IONBF and, buffering, ASize 2 .. INT_MAX, else -1
// with EINVAL (what ucrt's parameter check returns under the MinGW handler,
// measured). The FILE's buffer is then dropped as is: bytes read ahead or
// ungot are lost, the descriptor does not move (measured). _IOCTRLZ and
// every buffer bit are cleared. _IONBF: the 2-byte _charbuf; _IOLBF is
// _IOFBF; with no array a buffer of ASize rounded down to even, else the
// caller's array at that size (ucrt fills it itself). Bytes written and not
// yet flushed are flushed before the buffer goes (its result is not
// checked, as ucrt's is not). Returns 0 or -1; out of memory is
// HookIODoWith's ENOMEM.
int HookIODoCrtSetvbufLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, char* ABuffer, const int AMode,
  const std::size_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::size_t LUsable;

  if ((AMode != _IONBF) && (AMode != _IOFBF) && (AMode != _IOLBF))
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  if ((AMode != _IONBF) && ((ASize < 2) || (ASize > static_cast<std::size_t>(INT_MAX))))
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  LUsable = ASize & ~static_cast<std::size_t>(1);
  HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(AHandle);
  LModel.Buffer.clear();
  LModel.HasBuffer = false;
  LModel.SetvbufBuffer = false;
  LModel.StreamCtrlZ = false;
  LModel.Ptr = 0;
  LModel.Count = 0;
  if (AMode == _IONBF)
  {
    LModel.Buffer.assign(2, 0);
    LModel.BufferSize = 2;
    LModel.Kind = HookIODoUcrtBuffer::Single;
  }
  else if (ABuffer == nullptr)
  {
    LModel.Buffer.assign(LUsable, 0);
    LModel.BufferSize = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LUsable);
    LModel.Kind = HookIODoUcrtBuffer::Crt;
    LModel.SetvbufBuffer = true;
  }
  else
  {
    LModel.Buffer.adopt(reinterpret_cast<unsigned char*>(ABuffer),
      static_cast<std::int64_t>(LUsable));
    LModel.BufferSize = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LUsable);
    LModel.Kind = HookIODoUcrtBuffer::User;
    LModel.SetvbufBuffer = true;
  }
  LModel.HasBuffer = true;
  return 0;
}

// ucrt's setbuf: no array is _IONBF, an array is _IOFBF at BUFSIZ (512)
void HookIODoCrtSetbufLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, char* ABuffer)
{
  if (ABuffer == nullptr)
    HookIODoCrtSetvbufLocked(AHandle, nullptr, _IONBF, 0);
  else
    HookIODoCrtSetvbufLocked(AHandle, ABuffer, _IOFBF, BUFSIZ);
}

// _flsbuf.cpp stream_is_at_end_of_file_nolock: feof is set; else not when
// a big buffer's Ptr is at its start; else the descriptor's place is the
// IO's size (an IO with no size is not at the end, as a failed query is not)
bool HookIODoCrtAtEndLocked(const HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  std::int64_t LSize;

  if (AHandle.AtEnd)
    return true;
  if (HookIODoCrtBigBuffer(AHandle.Crt) && (AHandle.Crt.Ptr == 0))
    return false;
  LSize = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSize(AHandle.Stream);
  if (LSize < 0)
    return false;
  return AHandle.Position == LSize;
}

// _flsbuf.cpp write_buffer_nolock: with a big buffer its written bytes go
// to lowio (none: an append stream's descriptor goes to the IO's end, a
// failed seek is Failed and false), the buffer then holds the character's
// ASize bytes alone (1 for char, 2 for wchar_t: Ptr ASize, Count the
// rest); without one the character goes to lowio by itself. True when
// every byte asked was written.
bool HookIODoCrtWriteBufferLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* AChar,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LToWrite;
  std::int64_t LWritten = 0;
  std::int64_t LEnd;

  if (!HookIODoCrtBigBuffer(LModel))
    return HookIODoLowWriteLocked(AHandle, AChar, ASize) == ASize;
  LToWrite = LModel.Ptr;
  LModel.Ptr = ASize;
  LModel.Count = LModel.BufferSize - ASize;
  if (LToWrite > 0)
    LWritten = HookIODoLowWriteLocked(AHandle, LModel.Buffer.data(), LToWrite);
  else if (AHandle.Appending)
  {
    LEnd = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, 0, ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromEnd);
    if (LEnd < 0)
    {
      // ucrt returns its EOF from this bool function here, which is true:
      // the stream is flagged, the character is not stored, and its caller
      // reports success
      AHandle.Failed = true;
      return true;
    }
    // lowio's lseek clears the Ctrl-Z end
    AHandle.Position = LEnd;
    LModel.LowEof = false;
  }
  std::memcpy(LModel.Buffer.data(), AChar, static_cast<std::size_t>(ASize));
  return LWritten == LToWrite;
}

// ucrt's flush-and-write (_flsbuf.cpp common_flush_and_write_nolock) of a
// character of ASize bytes (1: char, 2: wchar_t): a stream that neither
// writes nor updates fails (EBADF, Failed). A reading stream may turn to
// writing only at the end (HookIODoCrtAtEndLocked); its buffer is dropped
// either way, and elsewhere it fails (Failed). The stream then writes,
// AtEnd is cleared, a stream with no buffer gets ucrt's, and the character
// goes through HookIODoCrtWriteBufferLocked (a short write: Failed).
// False: the character failed (the caller's EOF / WEOF).
bool HookIODoCrtFlushAndWriteCharLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* AChar,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  bool LSwitch;

  if ((!LModel.StreamWrite) && (!LModel.StreamUpdate))
  {
    errno = EBADF;
    AHandle.Failed = true;
    return false;
  }
  if (LModel.StreamRead)
  {
    LSwitch = HookIODoCrtAtEndLocked(AHandle);
    LModel.Count = 0;
    if (!LSwitch)
    {
      AHandle.Failed = true;
      return false;
    }
    LModel.Ptr = 0;
    LModel.StreamRead = false;
  }
  LModel.StreamWrite = true;
  AHandle.AtEnd = false;
  LModel.Count = 0;
  HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
  if (!HookIODoCrtWriteBufferLocked(AHandle, AChar, ASize))
  {
    AHandle.Failed = true;
    return false;
  }
  return true;
}

// __acrt_stdio_flush_and_write_narrow_nolock: the byte (0..255) or EOF
int HookIODoCrtFlushAndWriteLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const int AChar)
{
  const unsigned char LByte = static_cast<unsigned char>(AChar);

  if (!HookIODoCrtFlushAndWriteCharLocked(AHandle, &LByte, 1))
    return EOF;
  return AChar & 0xFF;
}

int HookIODoCrtPutLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const int AChar);

// One wide character as ucrt's _fputwc_nolock writes it. A binary handle
// (fputwc_binary_nolock): its 2 raw bytes into the buffer while it has room
// (_cnt -= 2 >= 0), else __acrt_stdio_flush_and_write_wide_nolock; an
// update stream holding bytes read ahead takes the fseek(SEEK_CUR, 0) C
// requires first, as HookIODoCrtPutLocked does. A text handle (ANSI):
// converted by the current locale (wctomb_s, as ucrt's _wctomb_internal;
// a failure is WEOF with its errno), each byte through
// HookIODoCrtPutLocked ("\n" becomes "\r\n" in lowio). Returns the
// character or WEOF.
wint_t HookIODoCrtPutWideLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wchar_t AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  char LBytes[MB_LEN_MAX];
  int LSize = 0;

  // A Unicode text mode (ccs=) writes the raw character too: lowio
  // converts it (fputwc.cpp)
  if ((!AHandle.Text) || (AHandle.LowText != 0))
  {
    if (LModel.StreamUpdate && LModel.StreamRead && (LModel.Count > 0))
      HookIODoSeekLocked(AHandle, 0, SEEK_CUR);
    LModel.Count -= static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t));
    if (LModel.Count < 0)
    {
      if (!HookIODoCrtFlushAndWriteCharLocked(AHandle,
        reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char*>(&AChar), sizeof(wchar_t)))
        return WEOF;
      return static_cast<wint_t>(AChar);
    }
    std::memcpy(LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.Ptr, &AChar, sizeof(wchar_t));
    LModel.Ptr += static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t));
    return static_cast<wint_t>(AChar);
  }
  if (wctomb_s(&LSize, LBytes, MB_LEN_MAX, AChar) != 0)
    return WEOF;
  for (int LI = 0; LI < LSize; ++LI)
  {
    if (HookIODoCrtPutLocked(AHandle, static_cast<unsigned char>(LBytes[LI])) == EOF)
      return WEOF;
  }
  return static_cast<wint_t>(AChar);
}

// One byte as ucrt's _fputc_nolock writes it: into the buffer while it has
// room (--_cnt >= 0), else HookIODoCrtFlushAndWriteLocked. Returns the byte
// (0..255) or EOF.
// ucrt's fast path also stores into a buffer holding bytes read ahead. On
// an update stream the byte is then lost (a reading buffer is never
// flushed): here the write takes the fseek(SEEK_CUR, 0) C requires between
// a read and a write first, so the byte lands at the caller's place. A
// read-only stream keeps ucrt's rule (the byte replaces the next byte read
// ahead and fputc succeeds): nothing could have been written there.
int HookIODoCrtPutLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const int AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (LModel.StreamUpdate && LModel.StreamRead && (LModel.Count > 0))
    HookIODoSeekLocked(AHandle, 0, SEEK_CUR);
  --LModel.Count;
  if (LModel.Count < 0)
    return HookIODoCrtFlushAndWriteLocked(AHandle, AChar);
  LModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.Ptr)] = static_cast<unsigned char>(AChar);
  ++LModel.Ptr;
  return AChar & 0xFF;
}

// A write of ASize bytes, as ucrt's fwrite (fwrite.cpp
// _fwrite_nolock_internal): while a big buffer has room the bytes are
// copied in (a reading stream with bytes read ahead stops there, nothing
// flagged); with no room, at least one buffer's size goes first through a
// flush and then straight to lowio as the largest whole multiple of that
// size (lowio takes at most UINT_MAX - 1 bytes at a time); less goes one
// byte through HookIODoCrtFlushAndWriteLocked, after which the buffer's own
// size counts. A failure stops the write (Failed). Returns the count
// written.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtWriteLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* AData,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LBufferSize;
  std::int64_t LRemaining = ASize;
  std::int64_t LTake;
  std::int64_t LGot;
  const unsigned char* LData = AData;

  if (ASize <= 0)
    return 0;
  LBufferSize = LModel.HasBuffer ? LModel.BufferSize : CHookIODoBufferSize;
  while (LRemaining != 0)
  {
    if (HookIODoCrtBigBuffer(LModel) && (LModel.Count != 0))
    {
      if (LModel.Count < 0)
      {
        AHandle.Failed = true;
        break;
      }
      if (LModel.StreamRead)
        break;
      LTake = (LRemaining < LModel.Count) ? LRemaining : LModel.Count;
      std::memcpy(LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.Ptr, LData, static_cast<std::size_t>(LTake));
      LRemaining -= LTake;
      LModel.Count -= LTake;
      LModel.Ptr += LTake;
      LData += LTake;
    }
    else if (LRemaining >= LBufferSize)
    {
      if (HookIODoCrtBigBuffer(LModel) && (HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(AHandle) != 0))
        break;
      LTake = (LBufferSize > 0) ? (LRemaining - (LRemaining % LBufferSize)) : LRemaining;
      if (LTake > (static_cast<std::int64_t>(UINT_MAX) - 1))
        LTake = static_cast<std::int64_t>(UINT_MAX) - 1;
      LGot = HookIODoLowWriteLocked(AHandle, LData, LTake);
      if (LGot < 0)
      {
        AHandle.Failed = true;
        break;
      }
      if (LGot > LTake)
        LGot = LTake;
      LRemaining -= LGot;
      LData += LGot;
      if (LGot < LTake)
      {
        AHandle.Failed = true;
        break;
      }
    }
    else
    {
      if (HookIODoCrtFlushAndWriteLocked(AHandle, *LData) == EOF)
        break;
      ++LData;
      --LRemaining;
      LBufferSize = (LModel.BufferSize > 0) ? LModel.BufferSize : 1;
    }
  }
  return ASize - LRemaining;
}

// The caller's place: ucrt's ftell
std::int64_t HookIODoPlaceLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  return HookIODoCrtTellLocked(AHandle);
}
#else
// The st_blksize HookIO's stat gives a virtual file
constexpr std::int64_t CHookIODoBlockSize = 4096;

// glibc's buffer size for a handle: _IO_file_doallocate's rule
// (filedoalloc.c) for a regular file whose st_blksize is the one HookIO's
// stat reports, BUFSIZ unless st_blksize is smaller. Measured: a real file
// beside the test program (WSL, glibc 2.39) gets the same 4096
// (tests\probe\hookabi\glibc_bufsize.c).
constexpr std::int64_t CHookIODoBufferSize =
  ((CHookIODoBlockSize > 0) && (CHookIODoBlockSize < BUFSIZ)) ? CHookIODoBlockSize : BUFSIZ;

// The size of _IO_default_pbackfail's first backup area
constexpr std::int64_t CHookIODoBackupSize = 128;

// The descriptor's read (_IO_SYSREAD): up to ASize bytes of the IO at the
// handle's Position. -1: the read failed (errno EIO); 0: the end. No stdio
// flag changes here.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtRawLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  std::int64_t LGot;

  // A descriptor opened without read access: read(2) fails with EBADF
  if (!HookIODoCanRead(AHandle))
  {
    errno = EBADF;
    return -1;
  }
  if (!HookIODoSyncLocked(AHandle))
  {
    errno = EIO;
    return -1;
  }
  LGot = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IORead(AHandle.Stream, ABuffer, ASize);
  if (LGot < 0)
    LGot = 0;
  AHandle.Position += LGot;
  if ((LGot == 0) && (ASize > 0) &&
    (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOStatus(AHandle.Stream) != ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOState::Eof))
  {
    errno = EIO;
    return -1;
  }
  return LGot;
}

// The descriptor's seek (_IO_SYSSEEK): AOffset from the start, the
// descriptor's place or the IO's end. The target must be reachable in the
// IO (past the end when the IO allows it); before the start or out of
// reach it fails with EINVAL and the place stays. Returns the new place or
// -1.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtSysSeekLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t AOffset,
  const int AOrigin)
{
  std::int64_t LBase = 0;
  std::int64_t LTarget;

  if (AOrigin == SEEK_CUR)
    LBase = AHandle.Position;
  else if (AOrigin == SEEK_END)
  {
    LBase = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSize(AHandle.Stream);
    // An IO with no size may still know its end
    if (LBase < 0)
      LBase = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, 0, ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromEnd);
    if (LBase < 0)
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return -1;
    }
  }
  // LBase is never negative here; the sum is checked before it is formed
  if ((AOffset > 0) && (LBase > (INT64_MAX - AOffset)))
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  LTarget = LBase + AOffset;
  if (LTarget < 0)
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, LTarget, ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromStart) != LTarget)
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  AHandle.Position = LTarget;
  return LTarget;
}

// The byte get area's buffer (Backup when the get area points into it,
// else Buffer)
unsigned char* HookIODoCrtArea(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  return AModel.ReadInBackup ? AModel.Backup.data() : AModel.Buffer.data();
}

// The wide get area's buffer (WideBackup when the wide get area points into
// it, else Wide)
wchar_t* HookIODoCrtWideArea(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  return AModel.WideReadInBackup ? AModel.WideBackup.data() : AModel.Wide.data();
}

// The second half of _IO_wfile_doallocate (wfiledoalloc.c): the wide buffer
// sized from the main one, as many wchar_t as it has bytes, or for the
// caller's array (_IO_USER_BUF) its size in wchar_t rounded up. The wide
// areas are not touched (glibc's _IO_wsetb only sets the buffer).
void HookIODoCrtWideFromNarrow(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  std::int64_t LSize = AModel.Buffer.size();

  if (AModel.Buffer.External != nullptr)
    LSize = (LSize + static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t)) - 1) /
      static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(wchar_t));
  AModel.Wide.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(LSize), L'\0');
  AModel.HasWide = true;
}

// _IO_doallocbuf: the main buffer, once (the get area is not touched):
// _IO_file_doallocate's size, or the 1-byte _shortbuf on an unbuffered
// stream. A wide stream's allocation is _IO_wfile_doallocate's, even
// unbuffered: the main buffer at _IO_file_doallocate's size, then the wide
// buffer made anew from it. Out of memory here is HookIODoWith's ENOMEM.
void HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (LModel.HasBuffer)
    return;
  if (LModel.Unbuffered && (LModel.Orientation <= 0))
    LModel.Buffer.assign(1, 0);
  else
    LModel.Buffer.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(CHookIODoBufferSize), 0);
  LModel.HasBuffer = true;
  if (LModel.Orientation > 0)
    HookIODoCrtWideFromNarrow(LModel);
}

// _IO_new_file_underflow's stdout rule for a line-buffered or unbuffered
// stream: stdout is flushed first when it is line-buffered and open
// (glibc libio.h: _IO_LINKED 0x80, _IO_NO_WRITES 0x08, _IO_LINE_BUF 0x200;
// stdout is never a HookIO handle)
void HookIODoCrtFlushStdout(const HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  constexpr int CLinked = 0x0080;
  constexpr int CNoWrites = 0x0008;
  constexpr int CLineBuf = 0x0200;

  if ((!AModel.LineBuffered) && (!AModel.Unbuffered))
    return;
  if ((stdout->_flags & (CLinked | CNoWrites | CLineBuf)) == (CLinked | CLineBuf))
    std::fflush(stdout);
}

// _IO_switch_to_main_get_area: the get area and the save area trade
// places; reading goes on at the main area's saved base
void HookIODoCrtToMain(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  AModel.InBackup = false;
  std::swap(AModel.ReadEnd, AModel.SaveEnd);
  std::swap(AModel.ReadBase, AModel.SaveBase);
  std::swap(AModel.ReadInBackup, AModel.SaveInBackup);
  AModel.ReadPtr = AModel.ReadBase;
}

// _IO_switch_to_backup_area: the trade the other way; the backup area is
// read from its end (its bytes are put in front of ReadPtr)
void HookIODoCrtToBackup(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  AModel.InBackup = true;
  std::swap(AModel.ReadEnd, AModel.SaveEnd);
  std::swap(AModel.ReadBase, AModel.SaveBase);
  std::swap(AModel.ReadInBackup, AModel.SaveInBackup);
  AModel.ReadPtr = AModel.ReadEnd;
}

// _IO_free_backup_area: back to the main area, the backup area gone. Where
// a wide switch cleared the shared flag while the byte get area still lies
// in Backup (glibc then frees the buffer under it), the get area is left
// empty at the main buffer's start, the one state that reads nothing freed.
void HookIODoCrtDropBackup(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  if (AModel.InBackup)
    HookIODoCrtToMain(AModel);
  if (AModel.ReadInBackup)
  {
    AModel.ReadBase = 0;
    AModel.ReadPtr = 0;
    AModel.ReadEnd = 0;
    AModel.ReadInBackup = false;
  }
  AModel.Backup.clear();
  AModel.HaveBackup = false;
  AModel.SaveBase = 0;
  AModel.SaveEnd = 0;
  AModel.SaveInBackup = true;
}

// _IO_switch_to_main_wget_area (wgenops.c): the wide get and save areas
// trade places; reading goes on at the main area's saved base
void HookIODoCrtWideToMain(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  AModel.InBackup = false;
  std::swap(AModel.WideReadEnd, AModel.WideSaveEnd);
  std::swap(AModel.WideReadBase, AModel.WideSaveBase);
  std::swap(AModel.WideReadInBackup, AModel.WideSaveInBackup);
  AModel.WideReadPtr = AModel.WideReadBase;
}

// _IO_switch_to_wbackup_area: the trade the other way; the wide backup
// area is read from its end
void HookIODoCrtWideToBackup(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  AModel.InBackup = true;
  std::swap(AModel.WideReadEnd, AModel.WideSaveEnd);
  std::swap(AModel.WideReadBase, AModel.WideSaveBase);
  std::swap(AModel.WideReadInBackup, AModel.WideSaveInBackup);
  AModel.WideReadPtr = AModel.WideReadEnd;
}

// _IO_free_wbackup_area (wgenops.c): back to the main wide area (the shared
// flag decides, as glibc's), the wide backup area gone. A wide get area
// still in WideBackup (the flag cleared by a byte switch) is left empty at
// the wide buffer's start.
void HookIODoCrtWideDropBackup(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  if (AModel.InBackup)
    HookIODoCrtWideToMain(AModel);
  if (AModel.WideReadInBackup)
  {
    AModel.WideReadBase = 0;
    AModel.WideReadPtr = 0;
    AModel.WideReadEnd = 0;
    AModel.WideReadInBackup = false;
  }
  AModel.WideBackup.clear();
  AModel.WideSaveBase = 0;
  AModel.WideSaveEnd = 0;
  AModel.WideBackupBase = 0;
  AModel.WideSaveInBackup = true;
}

// _IO_setp (buf_base, buf_base): an empty put area at the buffer's start
void HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  AModel.WriteBase = 0;
  AModel.WritePtr = 0;
  AModel.WriteEnd = 0;
  AModel.WriteArea = true;
}

// glibc's new_do_write (fileops.c): ASize bytes of AData to the descriptor.
// An appending stream's offset becomes unknown (O_APPEND writes at the
// end); otherwise a get area that does not end where the put area starts
// (bytes read ahead, or a write begun inside them) first moves the
// descriptor by WriteBase - ReadEnd, the offset known there (a failed move
// writes nothing: 0, no flag). Then the get and put areas restart at the
// buffer's start; the put area ends there on a line-buffered or unbuffered
// stream (each byte then goes through overflow), else at the buffer's end.
// Returns the count written.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtNewDoWriteLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* AData,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LGot;

  if (AHandle.Appending)
    LModel.OffsetKnown = false;
  else if (LModel.ReadEnd != LModel.WriteBase)
  {
    if (HookIODoCrtSysSeekLocked(AHandle, LModel.WriteBase - LModel.ReadEnd, SEEK_CUR) < 0)
      return 0;
    LModel.OffsetKnown = true;
  }
  LGot = HookIODoWriteIOLocked(AHandle, AData, ASize);
  if (LGot < 0)
    LGot = 0;
  LModel.ReadBase = 0;
  LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
  LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
  HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
  if ((!LModel.LineBuffered) && (!LModel.Unbuffered))
    LModel.WriteEnd = LModel.Buffer.size();
  return LGot;
}

// _IO_new_do_write: 0 when all ASize bytes were written (or there were
// none), else EOF
int HookIODoCrtDoWriteLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* AData,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  if (ASize == 0)
    return 0;
  return (HookIODoCrtNewDoWriteLocked(AHandle, AData, ASize) == ASize) ? 0 : EOF;
}

// A wide stream's codecvt (glibc iofwide.c: _IO_fwide clones the locale's
// wcsmbs conversion when the stream turns wide; its output step converts
// with transliteration). Here iconv over the same conversion: Out =
// wchar_t to the charset with //TRANSLIT, In = the charset to wchar_t;
// Count and CountOut are second ones of each for ftell / fseek's counts,
// so counting never disturbs the stream's own state (glibc counts from a
// copy of the saved state). Clen is __libio_codecvt_encoding: -1 for a
// stateful charset, else the bytes of every character when that is fixed,
// else 0. For glibc's charsets: fixed exactly when MB_CUR_MAX is 1.
struct HookIODoCrtConverter
{
  iconv_t Out = reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1);
  iconv_t In = reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1);
  iconv_t Count = reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1);
  iconv_t CountOut = reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1);
  int Clen = 0;

  ~HookIODoCrtConverter()
  {
    const int LSaved = errno;

    if (Out != reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1))
      iconv_close(Out);
    if (In != reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1))
      iconv_close(In);
    if (Count != reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1))
      iconv_close(Count);
    if (CountOut != reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1))
      iconv_close(CountOut);
    errno = LSaved;
  }
};

// One iconv step (defined below)
enum class HookIODoCrtConvert;
HookIODoCrtConvert HookIODoCrtIconv(iconv_t ACd, const void* AFrom, const std::size_t AFromSize,
  std::size_t& AFromUsed, void* ATo, const std::size_t AToSize, std::size_t& AToUsed);

// The codecvt over ACharset (a ccs= name); nullptr when iconv knows no such
// charset (glibc's __wcsmbs_named_conv failing). Clen as glibc's
// __libio_codecvt_encoding gives it: -1 for a stateful charset (UTF-7,
// ISO-2022-*), else the bytes every character takes when that is fixed
// (measured over characters of 1, 2, 3 and 4 UTF-8 bytes), else 0. errno
// is kept.
std::shared_ptr<HookIODoCrtConverter> HookIODoCrtNamedConverter(const std::string& ACharset)
{
  const int LSaved = errno;
  const std::string LTranslit = ACharset + "//TRANSLIT";
  std::shared_ptr<HookIODoCrtConverter> LConverter = std::make_shared<HookIODoCrtConverter>();
  const wchar_t LProbe[4] = {L'A', static_cast<wchar_t>(0xE9), static_cast<wchar_t>(0x20AC),
    static_cast<wchar_t>(0x1F600)};
  char LOut[64];
  std::size_t LTaken;
  std::size_t LMade;
  std::size_t LWidth = 0;
  bool LFixed = true;
  std::string LUpper;

  LConverter->Out = iconv_open(LTranslit.c_str(), "WCHAR_T");
  LConverter->In = iconv_open("WCHAR_T", ACharset.c_str());
  LConverter->Count = iconv_open("WCHAR_T", ACharset.c_str());
  LConverter->CountOut = iconv_open(LTranslit.c_str(), "WCHAR_T");
  errno = LSaved;
  if ((LConverter->Out == reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1)) ||
    (LConverter->In == reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1)) ||
    (LConverter->Count == reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1)) ||
    (LConverter->CountOut == reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1)))
    return nullptr;
  for (const char LChar : ACharset)
    LUpper.push_back(static_cast<char>(std::toupper(static_cast<unsigned char>(LChar))));
  if ((LUpper.rfind("UTF-7", 0) == 0) || (LUpper.rfind("UTF7", 0) == 0) ||
    (LUpper.rfind("ISO-2022", 0) == 0) || (LUpper.rfind("ISO2022", 0) == 0))
  {
    LConverter->Clen = -1;
    return LConverter;
  }
  for (const wchar_t LWide : LProbe)
  {
    iconv(LConverter->CountOut, nullptr, nullptr, nullptr, nullptr);
    HookIODoCrtIconv(LConverter->CountOut, &LWide, sizeof(LWide), LTaken, LOut, sizeof(LOut),
      LMade);
    iconv(LConverter->CountOut, nullptr, nullptr, nullptr, nullptr);
    if (LTaken != sizeof(LWide))
      continue;
    if (LWidth == 0)
      LWidth = LMade;
    else if (LWidth != LMade)
      LFixed = false;
  }
  LConverter->Clen = (LFixed && (LWidth != 0)) ? static_cast<int>(LWidth) : 0;
  errno = LSaved;
  return LConverter;
}

// A ",ccs=NAME" open (glibc fileops.c _IO_new_file_fopen): the stream's
// codecvt is NAME's, both wide areas empty, and the stream wide from the
// start. False when the charset cannot be loaded.
bool HookIODoNamedWide(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::string& ACharset)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::shared_ptr<HookIODoCrtConverter> LConverter;

  try
  {
    LConverter = HookIODoCrtNamedConverter(ACharset);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    return false;
  }
  if (LConverter == nullptr)
    return false;
  LModel.Converter = LConverter;
  LModel.WideReadPtr = LModel.WideReadEnd;
  LModel.WideWritePtr = LModel.WideWriteBase;
  LModel.Orientation = 1;
  return true;
}

// The codecvt for the current LC_CTYPE (what _IO_fwide clones). glibc's
// clone cannot fail; an iconv that cannot open is out of memory here
// (HookIODoWith's ENOMEM). errno is kept.
std::shared_ptr<HookIODoCrtConverter> HookIODoCrtWideConverter()
{
  const int LSaved = errno;
  const std::string LCharset = nl_langinfo(CODESET);
  const std::string LTranslit = LCharset + "//TRANSLIT";
  std::shared_ptr<HookIODoCrtConverter> LConverter = std::make_shared<HookIODoCrtConverter>();

  LConverter->Out = iconv_open(LTranslit.c_str(), "WCHAR_T");
  LConverter->In = iconv_open("WCHAR_T", LCharset.c_str());
  LConverter->Count = iconv_open("WCHAR_T", LCharset.c_str());
  LConverter->CountOut = iconv_open(LTranslit.c_str(), "WCHAR_T");
  errno = LSaved;
  if ((LConverter->Out == reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1)) ||
    (LConverter->In == reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1)) ||
    (LConverter->Count == reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1)) ||
    (LConverter->CountOut == reinterpret_cast<iconv_t>(-1)))
    throw std::bad_alloc();
  // mblen(nil) says whether the charset keeps a shift state (it resets only
  // mblen's own state, which no glibc locale charset has)
  if (std::mblen(nullptr, 0) != 0)
    LConverter->Clen = -1;
  else if (MB_CUR_MAX == 1)
    LConverter->Clen = 1;
  else
    LConverter->Clen = 0;
  errno = LSaved;
  return LConverter;
}

// __codecvt_result of a conversion step
enum class HookIODoCrtConvert
{
  Ok,
  Partial,
  Error
};

// One iconv step from [AFrom, AFrom + AFromSize) bytes into [ATo, ATo +
// AToSize) bytes; AFromUsed / AToUsed get what it took and made. Ok: all
// taken; Partial: the output is full (E2BIG) or the input ends inside a
// character (EINVAL); Error: an input it cannot convert (EILSEQ). errno is
// kept: glibc's codecvt sets none.
HookIODoCrtConvert HookIODoCrtIconv(iconv_t ACd, const void* AFrom, const std::size_t AFromSize,
  std::size_t& AFromUsed, void* ATo, const std::size_t AToSize, std::size_t& AToUsed)
{
  const int LSaved = errno;
  char* LIn = const_cast<char*>(static_cast<const char*>(AFrom));
  char* LOut = static_cast<char*>(ATo);
  std::size_t LInLeft = AFromSize;
  std::size_t LOutLeft = AToSize;
  HookIODoCrtConvert LResult = HookIODoCrtConvert::Ok;

  if (iconv(ACd, &LIn, &LInLeft, &LOut, &LOutLeft) == static_cast<std::size_t>(-1))
  {
    if ((errno == E2BIG) || (errno == EINVAL))
      LResult = HookIODoCrtConvert::Partial;
    else
      LResult = HookIODoCrtConvert::Error;
  }
  AFromUsed = AFromSize - LInLeft;
  AToUsed = AToSize - LOutLeft;
  errno = LSaved;
  return LResult;
}

// __libio_codecvt_length: how many bytes of [AFrom, AFrom + ASize) make at
// most AMax wide characters, counted from the initial state (glibc counts
// from the saved state, which a stream that only writes never leaves)
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtWideLength(HookIODoCrtConverter& AConverter, const unsigned char* AFrom,
  const std::int64_t ASize, const std::int64_t AMax)
{
  std::vector<wchar_t> LTo(static_cast<std::size_t>((AMax > 0) ? AMax : 1));
  std::size_t LTaken = 0;
  std::size_t LMade = 0;
  const int LSaved = errno;

  if ((AMax <= 0) || (ASize <= 0))
    return 0;
  iconv(AConverter.Count, nullptr, nullptr, nullptr, nullptr);
  errno = LSaved;
  HookIODoCrtIconv(AConverter.Count, AFrom, static_cast<std::size_t>(ASize), LTaken,
    LTo.data(), static_cast<std::size_t>(AMax) * sizeof(wchar_t), LMade);
  return static_cast<std::int64_t>(LTaken);
}

// glibc's _IO_wdo_write (wfileops.c) of the wide put area [WideWriteBase,
// WideWritePtr): bytes the main put area holds when it is full are written
// first; then the wide characters are converted into the main buffer at
// WritePtr (into a MB_LEN_MAX scratch when less room is left there) and
// each part goes out through _IO_new_do_write, until all are converted or a
// conversion fails (what it converted still goes out; the rest is dropped).
// Then the wide areas restart at the buffer's start, the wide put area
// empty on a line-buffered or unbuffered stream. 0, or WEOF as int (-1).
int HookIODoCrtWideDoWriteLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  // glibc's MB_LEN_MAX
  constexpr std::int64_t CMbLenMax = 16;

  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  const wchar_t* LData = LModel.Wide.data() + LModel.WideWriteBase;
  std::int64_t LToDo = LModel.WideWritePtr - LModel.WideWriteBase;
  unsigned char LScratch[CMbLenMax];
  unsigned char* LWriteBase;
  unsigned char* LWritePtr;
  std::int64_t LRoom;
  std::size_t LTaken;
  std::size_t LMade;
  HookIODoCrtConvert LResult;

  if (LToDo > 0)
  {
    if ((LModel.WriteEnd == LModel.WritePtr) && (LModel.WriteEnd != LModel.WriteBase))
    {
      if (HookIODoCrtDoWriteLocked(AHandle, LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.WriteBase,
        LModel.WritePtr - LModel.WriteBase) == EOF)
        return static_cast<int>(WEOF);
    }
    do
    {
      if ((LModel.Buffer.size() - LModel.WritePtr) < CMbLenMax)
      {
        LWriteBase = LScratch;
        LWritePtr = LScratch;
        LRoom = CMbLenMax;
      }
      else
      {
        LWriteBase = LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.WriteBase;
        LWritePtr = LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.WritePtr;
        LRoom = LModel.Buffer.size() - LModel.WritePtr;
      }
      LResult = HookIODoCrtIconv(LModel.Converter->Out, LData,
        static_cast<std::size_t>(LToDo) * sizeof(wchar_t), LTaken, LWritePtr,
        static_cast<std::size_t>(LRoom), LMade);
      LWritePtr += LMade;
      if (HookIODoCrtDoWriteLocked(AHandle, LWriteBase, LWritePtr - LWriteBase) == EOF)
        return static_cast<int>(WEOF);
      LToDo -= static_cast<std::int64_t>(LTaken / sizeof(wchar_t));
      if ((LResult != HookIODoCrtConvert::Ok) &&
        ((LResult != HookIODoCrtConvert::Partial) || (LTaken == 0)))
        break;
      LData += LTaken / sizeof(wchar_t);
    }
    while (LToDo > 0);
  }
  LModel.WideReadBase = 0;
  LModel.WideReadPtr = 0;
  LModel.WideReadEnd = 0;
  LModel.WideWriteBase = 0;
  LModel.WideWritePtr = 0;
  LModel.WideWriteEnd = (LModel.LineBuffered || LModel.Unbuffered) ? 0 :
    static_cast<std::int64_t>(LModel.Wide.size());
  LModel.WideWriteArea = LModel.HasWide;
  return (LToDo == 0) ? 0 : static_cast<int>(WEOF);
}

// _IO_do_flush (libioP.h): the put area's unflushed bytes through
// _IO_new_do_write, on a wide stream the wide put area through
// _IO_wdo_write
int HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (LModel.Orientation > 0)
    return HookIODoCrtWideDoWriteLocked(AHandle);
  return HookIODoCrtDoWriteLocked(AHandle, LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.WriteBase,
    LModel.WritePtr - LModel.WriteBase);
}

// _IO_fwide (iofwide.c): AMode normalized; a stream already oriented, or a
// mode of 0, gives its orientation as it is. Turning wide: the wide get
// area is empty at its pointer, the wide put area empty at its base, and
// the codecvt is taken from the current locale. Returns the orientation.
int HookIODoCrtFwideLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const int AMode)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  const int LMode = (AMode < 0) ? -1 : ((AMode == 0) ? 0 : 1);

  if ((LModel.Orientation != 0) || (LMode == 0))
    return LModel.Orientation;
  if (LMode > 0)
  {
    LModel.Converter = HookIODoCrtWideConverter();
    LModel.WideReadPtr = LModel.WideReadEnd;
    LModel.WideWritePtr = LModel.WideWriteBase;
  }
  LModel.Orientation = LMode;
  return LMode;
}

// _IO_fwide (fp, -1) == -1: the check every narrow call that refuses a
// wide stream makes (fputs, fwrite, the narrow printf and scan, __uflow /
// __underflow); a fresh stream turns byte-oriented
bool HookIODoCrtNarrowLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  return HookIODoCrtFwideLocked(AHandle, -1) == -1;
}

// _IO_wdoallocbuf (wgenops.c): the wide buffer, once: _IO_wfile_doallocate
// (the main buffer first when there is none, then the wide one from it), or
// the 1-wchar_t _shortbuf on an unbuffered stream
void HookIODoCrtWideAllocateLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (LModel.HasWide)
    return;
  if (LModel.Unbuffered)
  {
    LModel.Wide.assign(1, L'\0');
    LModel.HasWide = true;
    return;
  }
  if (!LModel.HasBuffer)
  {
    LModel.Buffer.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(CHookIODoBufferSize), 0);
    LModel.HasBuffer = true;
  }
  HookIODoCrtWideFromNarrow(LModel);
}

// glibc's _IO_wfile_overflow: AChar (or WEOF: only flush) into the wide put
// area. A handle opened without write access fails (Failed, EBADF). Not yet
// in put mode, or with no wide put area: with none, the wide buffer is made
// and the wide get area emptied at its start (the main buffer made too when
// the main put area has none, its get area emptied); otherwise a wide get
// area read to its buffer's very end restarts both get areas at their
// starts. Both put areas then begin where reading stood and both get areas
// end there; put mode; a line-buffered or unbuffered stream's wide put area
// is empty. WEOF flushes (_IO_do_flush). A full wide buffer is flushed
// first; the character is stored and, on an unbuffered stream or a
// line-buffered one at L'\n', flushed. Returns the character or WEOF.
// A write that starts while ungot wide characters are pending (InBackup) is
// C's undefined input -> output turn (C11 7.21.5.3: an fseek must come
// between); glibc then writes into the backup area's memory. Here the
// handle makes that fseek first (glibc's own wide seek, 0 from the
// caller's place: it drops the backup area), so the write lands where that
// fseek leaves the stream; its failure fails the write (WEOF).
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtWideSeekLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t AOffset,
  const int AOrigin);

wint_t HookIODoCrtWideOverflowLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wint_t AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (!HookIODoCanWrite(AHandle))
  {
    AHandle.Failed = true;
    errno = EBADF;
    return WEOF;
  }
  if ((!LModel.Putting) && LModel.InBackup && LModel.WideReadInBackup &&
    (HookIODoCrtWideSeekLocked(AHandle, 0, SEEK_CUR) < 0))
    return WEOF;
  if ((!LModel.Putting) || (!LModel.WideWriteArea))
  {
    if (!LModel.WideWriteArea)
    {
      HookIODoCrtWideAllocateLocked(AHandle);
      HookIODoCrtWideDropBackup(LModel);
      LModel.WideReadBase = 0;
      LModel.WideReadPtr = 0;
      LModel.WideReadEnd = 0;
      if (!LModel.WriteArea)
      {
        HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
        LModel.ReadBase = 0;
        LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
        LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
      }
    }
    else if (LModel.WideReadPtr == static_cast<std::int64_t>(LModel.Wide.size()))
    {
      LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
      LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
      LModel.WideReadEnd = 0;
      LModel.WideReadPtr = 0;
    }
    LModel.WideWritePtr = LModel.WideReadPtr;
    LModel.WideWriteBase = LModel.WideWritePtr;
    LModel.WideWriteEnd = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LModel.Wide.size());
    LModel.WideReadBase = LModel.WideReadEnd;
    LModel.WideReadPtr = LModel.WideReadEnd;
    LModel.WideWriteArea = true;
    LModel.WritePtr = LModel.ReadPtr;
    LModel.WriteBase = LModel.WritePtr;
    LModel.WriteEnd = LModel.Buffer.size();
    LModel.ReadBase = LModel.ReadEnd;
    LModel.ReadPtr = LModel.ReadEnd;
    LModel.WriteArea = true;
    LModel.Putting = true;
    if (LModel.LineBuffered || LModel.Unbuffered)
      LModel.WideWriteEnd = LModel.WideWritePtr;
  }
  if (AChar == WEOF)
    return static_cast<wint_t>(HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(AHandle));
  if ((LModel.WideWritePtr == static_cast<std::int64_t>(LModel.Wide.size())) &&
    (HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
    return WEOF;
  LModel.Wide[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.WideWritePtr)] = static_cast<wchar_t>(AChar);
  ++LModel.WideWritePtr;
  if (LModel.Unbuffered || (LModel.LineBuffered && (static_cast<wchar_t>(AChar) == L'\n')))
  {
    if (HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(AHandle) == EOF)
      return WEOF;
  }
  return AChar;
}

// glibc's _IO_new_file_overflow: AChar (or EOF: only flush) into the put
// area. A handle opened without write access fails (Failed, EBADF). Not yet
// in put mode, or with no put area: the buffer is made when there is none
// (the get area emptied at its start); a backup area in use is dropped, the
// get area's start moved back by its unread bytes (as far as the buffer's
// start); a get area read to the buffer's very end restarts at its start;
// the put area then begins where reading stood and the get area ends there
// (its read-ahead stays the descriptor's own); put mode; a line-buffered or
// unbuffered stream's put area is empty. EOF flushes [WriteBase, WritePtr).
// A full buffer is flushed first; the byte is stored and, on an unbuffered
// stream or a line-buffered one at '\n', the put area flushed. Returns the
// byte (0..255) or EOF.
// This is the stream's _IO_OVERFLOW: on a wide stream its table holds
// _IO_wfile_overflow, which takes AChar as a wide character (EOF as WEOF).
int HookIODoCrtOverflowLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const int AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LUnread;
  std::int64_t LBack;
  unsigned char LByte;

  if (LModel.Orientation > 0)
    return static_cast<int>(HookIODoCrtWideOverflowLocked(AHandle, static_cast<wint_t>(AChar)));
  if (!HookIODoCanWrite(AHandle))
  {
    AHandle.Failed = true;
    errno = EBADF;
    return EOF;
  }
  if ((!LModel.Putting) || (!LModel.WriteArea))
  {
    if (!LModel.WriteArea)
    {
      HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
      LModel.ReadBase = 0;
      LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
      LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
    }
    if (LModel.InBackup)
    {
      LUnread = LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr;
      HookIODoCrtDropBackup(LModel);
      LBack = (LUnread < LModel.ReadBase) ? LUnread : LModel.ReadBase;
      LModel.ReadBase -= LBack;
      LModel.ReadPtr = LModel.ReadBase;
    }
    if (LModel.ReadPtr == LModel.Buffer.size())
    {
      LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
      LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
    }
    LModel.WritePtr = LModel.ReadPtr;
    LModel.WriteBase = LModel.WritePtr;
    LModel.WriteEnd = LModel.Buffer.size();
    LModel.WriteArea = true;
    LModel.ReadBase = LModel.ReadEnd;
    LModel.ReadPtr = LModel.ReadEnd;
    LModel.Putting = true;
    if (LModel.LineBuffered || LModel.Unbuffered)
      LModel.WriteEnd = LModel.WritePtr;
  }
  if (AChar == EOF)
    return HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(AHandle);
  if ((LModel.WritePtr == LModel.Buffer.size()) && (HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
    return EOF;
  LByte = static_cast<unsigned char>(AChar);
  LModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.WritePtr)] = LByte;
  ++LModel.WritePtr;
  if (LModel.Unbuffered || (LModel.LineBuffered && (LByte == '\n')))
  {
    if (HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(AHandle) == EOF)
      return EOF;
  }
  return LByte;
}

// _IO_switch_to_get_mode (genops.c): unflushed bytes are flushed first
// (overflow, EOF on its failure); the get area starts at the buffer's (the
// backup area's while InBackup) and, outside the backup area, ends no
// earlier than WritePtr; reading goes on at WritePtr, the put area is empty
// there and put mode ends. Returns 0 or EOF.
int HookIODoCrtSwitchToGetLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if ((LModel.WritePtr > LModel.WriteBase) && (HookIODoCrtOverflowLocked(AHandle, EOF) == EOF))
    return EOF;
  LModel.ReadBase = 0;
  if ((!LModel.InBackup) && (LModel.WritePtr > LModel.ReadEnd))
    LModel.ReadEnd = LModel.WritePtr;
  LModel.ReadPtr = LModel.WritePtr;
  LModel.WriteBase = LModel.ReadPtr;
  LModel.WritePtr = LModel.ReadPtr;
  LModel.WriteEnd = LModel.ReadPtr;
  LModel.Putting = false;
  return 0;
}

// _IO_default_xsputn (genops.c): the put area's room filled, each further
// byte through overflow until all are taken or one fails. Returns the count
// taken.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtDefaultPutnLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* AData,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LMore = ASize;
  std::int64_t LCount;
  const unsigned char* LData = AData;

  if (LMore <= 0)
    return 0;
  for (;;)
  {
    if (LModel.WritePtr < LModel.WriteEnd)
    {
      LCount = LModel.WriteEnd - LModel.WritePtr;
      if (LCount > LMore)
        LCount = LMore;
      std::memcpy(LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.WritePtr, LData, static_cast<std::size_t>(LCount));
      LModel.WritePtr += LCount;
      LData += LCount;
      LMore -= LCount;
    }
    if (LMore == 0)
      break;
    if (HookIODoCrtOverflowLocked(AHandle, *LData) == EOF)
      break;
    ++LData;
    --LMore;
  }
  return ASize - LMore;
}

// glibc's _IO_new_file_xsputn (_IO_sputn): the room in the put area first
// (a line-buffered stream in put mode: the room to the buffer's end, and
// when it holds every byte, only up to the last '\n', which forces a
// flush); what is left (or the forced flush) goes through overflow(EOF) (on
// failure: EOF when every byte was taken, else the count), then the largest
// whole multiple of the buffer's size straight to the descriptor (all of it
// for a buffer under 128 bytes), and the rest through _IO_default_xsputn.
// Returns the count written, or -1 for glibc's EOF.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtPutnLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* AData,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  const unsigned char* LData = AData;
  std::int64_t LToDo = ASize;
  std::int64_t LCount = 0;
  std::int64_t LBlock;
  std::int64_t LDirect;
  bool LMustFlush = false;

  if (ASize <= 0)
    return 0;
  if (LModel.LineBuffered && LModel.Putting)
  {
    LCount = LModel.Buffer.size() - LModel.WritePtr;
    if (LCount >= ASize)
    {
      for (std::int64_t LI = ASize; LI > 0; --LI)
      {
        if (AData[LI - 1] == '\n')
        {
          LCount = LI;
          LMustFlush = true;
          break;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  else if (LModel.WriteEnd > LModel.WritePtr)
    LCount = LModel.WriteEnd - LModel.WritePtr;
  if (LCount > 0)
  {
    if (LCount > LToDo)
      LCount = LToDo;
    std::memcpy(LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.WritePtr, LData, static_cast<std::size_t>(LCount));
    LModel.WritePtr += LCount;
    LData += LCount;
    LToDo -= LCount;
  }
  if ((LToDo > 0) || LMustFlush)
  {
    if (HookIODoCrtOverflowLocked(AHandle, EOF) == EOF)
      return (LToDo == 0) ? -1 : (ASize - LToDo);
    LBlock = LModel.Buffer.size();
    LDirect = LToDo;
    if (LBlock >= 128)
      LDirect -= LToDo % LBlock;
    if (LDirect > 0)
    {
      LCount = HookIODoCrtNewDoWriteLocked(AHandle, LData, LDirect);
      LToDo -= LCount;
      if (LCount < LDirect)
        return ASize - LToDo;
    }
    if (LToDo > 0)
      LToDo -= HookIODoCrtDefaultPutnLocked(AHandle, LData + LDirect, LToDo);
  }
  return ASize - LToDo;
}

// One byte as glibc's putc / fputc writes it (_IO_putc_unlocked): into the
// put area while it has room, else __overflow (which turns a fresh stream
// byte-oriented and refuses nothing: on a wide stream the byte goes through
// the wide overflow as a wide character). Returns the byte (0..255) or EOF.
int HookIODoCrtPutLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const int AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  const unsigned char LByte = static_cast<unsigned char>(AChar);

  if (LModel.WritePtr >= LModel.WriteEnd)
  {
    if (LModel.Orientation == 0)
      LModel.Orientation = -1;
    return HookIODoCrtOverflowLocked(AHandle, LByte);
  }
  LModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.WritePtr)] = LByte;
  ++LModel.WritePtr;
  return LByte;
}

// __woverflow (wgenops.c): a fresh stream turns wide, then the stream's
// _IO_OVERFLOW, whichever table it holds: a byte-oriented stream's takes
// the character as a byte (its low 8 bits, as int)
wint_t HookIODoCrtWOverflowLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wint_t AChar)
{
  if (AHandle.Crt.Orientation == 0)
    HookIODoCrtFwideLocked(AHandle, 1);
  if (AHandle.Crt.Orientation > 0)
    return HookIODoCrtWideOverflowLocked(AHandle, AChar);
  return static_cast<wint_t>(HookIODoCrtOverflowLocked(AHandle, static_cast<int>(AChar)));
}

// One wide character as glibc's putwc writes it (_IO_putwc_unlocked, no
// orientation check): into the wide put area while it has room, else
// __woverflow. Returns the character or WEOF.
wint_t HookIODoCrtPutWideLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wchar_t AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (LModel.WideWritePtr >= LModel.WideWriteEnd)
    return HookIODoCrtWOverflowLocked(AHandle, static_cast<wint_t>(AChar));
  LModel.Wide[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.WideWritePtr)] = AChar;
  ++LModel.WideWritePtr;
  return static_cast<wint_t>(AChar);
}

// _IO_wdefault_xsputn (wgenops.c): the wide put area's room filled, each
// further character through __woverflow until all are taken or one fails.
// Returns the count taken.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtWideDefaultPutnLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wchar_t* AData,
  const std::int64_t ACount)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LMore = ACount;
  std::int64_t LCount;
  const wchar_t* LData = AData;

  if (LMore <= 0)
    return 0;
  for (;;)
  {
    LCount = LModel.WideWriteEnd - LModel.WideWritePtr;
    if (LCount > 0)
    {
      if (LCount > LMore)
        LCount = LMore;
      std::memcpy(LModel.Wide.data() + LModel.WideWritePtr, LData,
        static_cast<std::size_t>(LCount) * sizeof(wchar_t));
      LModel.WideWritePtr += LCount;
      LData += LCount;
      LMore -= LCount;
    }
    if (LMore == 0)
      break;
    if (HookIODoCrtWOverflowLocked(AHandle, static_cast<wint_t>(*LData)) == WEOF)
      break;
    ++LData;
    --LMore;
  }
  return ACount - LMore;
}

// glibc's _IO_wfile_xsputn: the room in the wide put area first (a
// line-buffered stream in put mode: the room to the wide buffer's end, and
// when it holds every character, only up to the last L'\n', which then
// forces a flush), the rest through _IO_wdefault_xsputn; the forced flush
// (_IO_wdo_write, its result not checked) when characters are pending.
// Returns the count taken (no whole-block path: a wide stream converts
// everything through its buffer).
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtWidePutnLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wchar_t* AData,
  const std::int64_t ACount)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  const wchar_t* LData = AData;
  std::int64_t LToDo = ACount;
  std::int64_t LCount;
  bool LMustFlush = false;

  if (ACount <= 0)
    return 0;
  LCount = LModel.WideWriteEnd - LModel.WideWritePtr;
  if (LModel.LineBuffered && LModel.Putting)
  {
    LCount = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LModel.Wide.size()) - LModel.WideWritePtr;
    if (LCount >= ACount)
    {
      for (std::int64_t LI = ACount; LI > 0; --LI)
      {
        if (AData[LI - 1] == L'\n')
        {
          LCount = LI;
          LMustFlush = true;
          break;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  if (LCount > 0)
  {
    if (LCount > LToDo)
      LCount = LToDo;
    std::memcpy(LModel.Wide.data() + LModel.WideWritePtr, LData,
      static_cast<std::size_t>(LCount) * sizeof(wchar_t));
    LModel.WideWritePtr += LCount;
    LData += LCount;
    LToDo -= LCount;
  }
  if (LToDo > 0)
    LToDo -= HookIODoCrtWideDefaultPutnLocked(AHandle, LData, LToDo);
  if (LMustFlush && (LModel.WideWritePtr != LModel.WideWriteBase))
    HookIODoCrtWideDoWriteLocked(AHandle);
  return ACount - LToDo;
}

// _IO_new_file_underflow: the next byte without taking it, refilling the
// main buffer (BufferSize bytes asked) when the get area is empty. EOF when
// AtEnd is already set (C99's sticky end), on a handle that cannot read
// (Failed, errno EBADF), at the end (AtEnd; the offset is no longer known)
// or after a failure (Failed).
int HookIODoCrtFillLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LGot;

  if (AHandle.AtEnd)
    return EOF;
  if (!HookIODoCanRead(AHandle))
  {
    AHandle.Failed = true;
    errno = EBADF;
    return EOF;
  }
  if (LModel.ReadPtr < LModel.ReadEnd)
    return static_cast<int>(HookIODoCrtArea(LModel)[LModel.ReadPtr]);
  if (!LModel.HasBuffer)
  {
    if (LModel.HaveBackup)
      HookIODoCrtDropBackup(LModel);
    HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
  }
  HookIODoCrtFlushStdout(LModel);
  // Unflushed bytes go first (glibc does not check the result here)
  HookIODoCrtSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle);
  LModel.ReadBase = 0;
  LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
  LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
  HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
  LGot = HookIODoCrtRawLocked(AHandle, LModel.Buffer.data(), LModel.Buffer.size());
  if (LGot <= 0)
  {
    if (LGot == 0)
      AHandle.AtEnd = true;
    else
    {
      AHandle.Failed = true;
      LGot = 0;
    }
  }
  LModel.ReadEnd += LGot;
  if (LGot == 0)
  {
    LModel.OffsetKnown = false;
    return EOF;
  }
  return static_cast<int>(LModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.ReadPtr)]);
}

// __underflow / __uflow (genops.c): a wide stream is refused (EOF, nothing
// flagged), a fresh one turns byte-oriented; in put mode it switches to get
// mode first (EOF when that fails); the get area's next byte, else the main
// area's (leaving the backup area), else a fill (the backup area dropped
// first). ATake: __uflow, the byte is taken.
int HookIODoCrtNextLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const bool ATake)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  int LByte;

  if (!HookIODoCrtNarrowLocked(AHandle))
    return EOF;
  if (LModel.Putting && (HookIODoCrtSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
    return EOF;
  if (LModel.ReadPtr < LModel.ReadEnd)
  {
    LByte = static_cast<int>(HookIODoCrtArea(LModel)[LModel.ReadPtr]);
    if (ATake)
      ++LModel.ReadPtr;
    return LByte;
  }
  if (LModel.InBackup)
  {
    HookIODoCrtToMain(LModel);
    if (LModel.ReadPtr < LModel.ReadEnd)
    {
      LByte = static_cast<int>(LModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.ReadPtr)]);
      if (ATake)
        ++LModel.ReadPtr;
      return LByte;
    }
  }
  if (LModel.HaveBackup)
    HookIODoCrtDropBackup(LModel);
  LByte = HookIODoCrtFillLocked(AHandle);
  if ((LByte != EOF) && ATake)
    ++LModel.ReadPtr;
  return LByte;
}

// One byte as glibc's getc reads it (_IO_getc_unlocked): the get area's
// next byte (no orientation change), else __uflow
int HookIODoCrtGetLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (LModel.ReadPtr < LModel.ReadEnd)
    return static_cast<int>(HookIODoCrtArea(LModel)[LModel.ReadPtr++]);
  return HookIODoCrtNextLocked(AHandle, true);
}

// ACount bytes read as that many getc calls read them (what a scan's
// reads do). Returns the count read; short only at the end or a failure.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtSkipLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t ACount)
{
  std::int64_t LDone = 0;

  while ((LDone < ACount) && (HookIODoCrtGetLocked(AHandle) != EOF))
    ++LDone;
  return LDone;
}

// A read of up to ASize bytes, as glibc's fread (_IO_file_xsgetn): the main
// buffer is made first (a backup area outside the get area dropped); the
// get area's bytes, then the main area's after the backup area; with the
// get area empty a request of less than a buffer underflows, a larger one
// reads the largest whole multiple of BufferSize straight from the IO,
// bypassing the buffer. A read of nothing sets AtEnd (the end) or Failed.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtReadLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LWant = ASize;
  std::int64_t LHave;
  std::int64_t LCount;

  if (!LModel.HasBuffer)
  {
    if ((!LModel.InBackup) && LModel.HaveBackup)
      HookIODoCrtDropBackup(LModel);
    HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
  }
  while (LWant > 0)
  {
    LHave = LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr;
    if (LWant <= LHave)
    {
      std::memcpy(ABuffer + (ASize - LWant), HookIODoCrtArea(LModel) + LModel.ReadPtr,
        static_cast<std::size_t>(LWant));
      LModel.ReadPtr += LWant;
      LWant = 0;
      break;
    }
    if (LHave > 0)
    {
      std::memcpy(ABuffer + (ASize - LWant), HookIODoCrtArea(LModel) + LModel.ReadPtr,
        static_cast<std::size_t>(LHave));
      LWant -= LHave;
      LModel.ReadPtr += LHave;
    }
    if (LModel.InBackup)
    {
      HookIODoCrtToMain(LModel);
      continue;
    }
    if (LWant < LModel.Buffer.size())
    {
      if (HookIODoCrtNextLocked(AHandle, false) == EOF)
        break;
      continue;
    }
    // glibc empties the put area here without flushing it (its bytes are
    // lost); the read takes the fflush C requires between a write and a
    // read first, so they land (on a wide stream that fflush is
    // _IO_wfile_sync's: the wide put area goes out first)
    if (LModel.Putting && (LModel.Orientation > 0) &&
      (LModel.WideWritePtr > LModel.WideWriteBase) && (HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(AHandle) != 0))
      break;
    if (LModel.Putting && (HookIODoCrtSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
      break;
    LModel.ReadBase = 0;
    LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
    LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
    HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
    // Whole blocks only, for a buffer of 128 bytes or more (measured: a
    // smaller one reads exactly what is wanted)
    LCount = LWant;
    if (LModel.Buffer.size() >= 128)
      LCount -= LWant % LModel.Buffer.size();
    LCount = HookIODoCrtRawLocked(AHandle, ABuffer + (ASize - LWant), LCount);
    if (LCount <= 0)
    {
      if (LCount == 0)
        AHandle.AtEnd = true;
      else
        AHandle.Failed = true;
      break;
    }
    LWant -= LCount;
  }
  return ASize - LWant;
}

// glibc's ungetc (_IO_sputbackc, then _IO_default_pbackfail, no markers):
// the same byte as the one before ReadPtr in the main area just steps back;
// any other goes in front of the get area's next byte through the backup
// area: entered (made at 128 bytes when there is none, the main area's
// unread part saved), or doubled when full. AtEnd is cleared. EOF is
// refused. Returns the byte (0..255) or EOF.
// In put mode glibc makes the backup area beside the put area, and the
// read after the ungot bytes mixes the two (its __uflow reads the main
// buffer up to the backup area's end); an fflush first does not help, as it
// leaves the stream in put mode. Here the stream switches to get mode first
// (HookIODoCrtSwitchToGetLocked: unflushed bytes land; EOF when that
// fails), so the ungot bytes are read and then the file at the caller's
// place.
// A wide-oriented stream: _IO_sputbackc's step back over the same byte
// before ReadPtr (byte get area), else the wide table's pbackfail
// (HookIODoCrtWidePbackfailLocked: AChar in front of the wide get area),
// since _IO_fwide turned the stream's table wide; measured on real glibc
// 2.39 (tests\probe\hookabi\wread4_real.c): ftell then -1 EINVAL and the
// next fgetwc reads AChar. In put mode the wide get mode first.
int HookIODoCrtWideSwitchToGetLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle);
wint_t HookIODoCrtWidePbackfailLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wint_t AChar);

int HookIODoCrtUngetLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const int AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  const unsigned char LByte = static_cast<unsigned char>(AChar);
  std::vector<unsigned char> LGrown;
  std::int64_t LOld;
  wint_t LWideResult;

  if (AChar == EOF)
    return EOF;
  if (LModel.Orientation > 0)
  {
    if (LModel.Putting && (HookIODoCrtWideSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
      return EOF;
    if ((LModel.ReadPtr > LModel.ReadBase)
      && (HookIODoCrtArea(LModel)[LModel.ReadPtr - 1] == LByte))
    {
      --LModel.ReadPtr;
      AHandle.AtEnd = false;
      return LByte;
    }
    LWideResult = HookIODoCrtWidePbackfailLocked(AHandle, static_cast<wint_t>(AChar));
    if (LWideResult == WEOF)
      return EOF;
    return static_cast<int>(LWideResult);
  }
  if (LModel.Putting && (HookIODoCrtSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
    return EOF;
  if ((LModel.ReadPtr > LModel.ReadBase) && (!LModel.InBackup)
    && (LModel.Buffer[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.ReadPtr - 1)] == LByte))
  {
    --LModel.ReadPtr;
    AHandle.AtEnd = false;
    return LByte;
  }
  if (!LModel.InBackup)
  {
    // An existing backup area is entered empty (save_for_backup keeps
    // nothing without markers); none is made
    if (!LModel.HaveBackup)
    {
      LModel.Backup.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(CHookIODoBackupSize), 0);
      LModel.SaveBase = 0;
      LModel.SaveEnd = CHookIODoBackupSize;
      LModel.HaveBackup = true;
    }
    LModel.ReadBase = LModel.ReadPtr;
    HookIODoCrtToBackup(LModel);
  }
  else if (LModel.ReadPtr <= LModel.ReadBase)
  {
    // Full: twice the size, the bytes kept at its end
    LOld = LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadBase;
    LGrown.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(2 * LOld), 0);
    std::memcpy(LGrown.data() + LOld, LModel.Backup.data() + LModel.ReadBase,
      static_cast<std::size_t>(LOld));
    LModel.Backup.swap(LGrown);
    LModel.ReadBase = 0;
    LModel.ReadPtr = LOld;
    LModel.ReadEnd = 2 * LOld;
  }
  --LModel.ReadPtr;
  LModel.Backup[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.ReadPtr)] = LByte;
  AHandle.AtEnd = false;
  return LByte;
}

// What glibc's wide seekoff returns for a failed flush: WEOF in an off64_t
// (4294967295, not -1), so fseek reports success there, as glibc's does
constexpr std::int64_t CHookIODoWideSeekWeof =
  static_cast<std::int64_t>(static_cast<std::uint32_t>(WEOF));

// _IO_switch_to_wget_mode (wgenops.c): pending wide characters are flushed
// first (the wide overflow, EOF on its failure); the wide get area starts
// at the wide buffer's start (the wide backup area's base while InBackup)
// and, outside it, ends no earlier than WideWritePtr; reading goes on at
// WideWritePtr, the wide put area is empty there and put mode ends. (Put
// mode never begins while ungot wide characters are pending: the overflow
// makes C's fseek first, so InBackup here comes only from the byte side.)
// 0 or EOF.
int HookIODoCrtWideSwitchToGetLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if ((LModel.WideWritePtr > LModel.WideWriteBase) &&
    (HookIODoCrtWideOverflowLocked(AHandle, WEOF) == WEOF))
    return EOF;
  if (LModel.InBackup && LModel.WideReadInBackup)
    LModel.WideReadBase = LModel.WideBackupBase;
  else
  {
    LModel.WideReadBase = 0;
    LModel.WideReadInBackup = false;
    if (LModel.WideWritePtr > LModel.WideReadEnd)
      LModel.WideReadEnd = LModel.WideWritePtr;
  }
  LModel.WideReadPtr = LModel.WideWritePtr;
  LModel.WideWriteBase = LModel.WideReadPtr;
  LModel.WideWritePtr = LModel.WideReadPtr;
  LModel.WideWriteEnd = LModel.WideReadPtr;
  LModel.Putting = false;
  return 0;
}

// _IO_wsetg / _IO_wsetp at the wide buffer's start: both wide areas empty
// there (glibc's null pointers while there is no wide buffer); the wide get
// area points into Wide again (the save area and the flag stay as they are)
void HookIODoCrtWideEmptyAreas(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel)
{
  AModel.WideReadInBackup = false;
  AModel.WideReadBase = 0;
  AModel.WideReadPtr = 0;
  AModel.WideReadEnd = 0;
  AModel.WideWriteBase = 0;
  AModel.WideWritePtr = 0;
  AModel.WideWriteEnd = 0;
  AModel.WideWriteArea = AModel.HasWide;
}

// glibc's adjust_wide_data (wfileops.c): the main get area's bytes
// [ReadBase, ReadPtr) become the wide get area, read to its end. A
// fixed-width charset that need not convert only counts them
// (AConvert false); otherwise they are converted into the wide buffer from
// its start. A conversion that fails sets Failed (false). glibc retries a
// partial conversion from the same start, forever when it cannot go on (a
// target inside a character, or no wide buffer): here what converted
// stands.
bool HookIODoCrtAdjustWideLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const bool AConvert)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::size_t LTaken = 0;
  std::size_t LMade = 0;
  std::int64_t LRoom;
  HookIODoCrtConvert LResult;

  if ((!AConvert) && (LModel.Converter->Clen > 0))
    LModel.WideReadEnd += (LModel.ReadPtr - LModel.ReadBase) / LModel.Converter->Clen;
  else if (LModel.ReadPtr > LModel.ReadBase)
  {
    LRoom = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LModel.Wide.size()) - LModel.WideReadBase;
    if (LRoom < 0)
      LRoom = 0;
    LResult = HookIODoCrtIconv(LModel.Converter->In, LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.ReadBase,
      static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.ReadPtr - LModel.ReadBase), LTaken,
      LModel.Wide.data() + LModel.WideReadBase, static_cast<std::size_t>(LRoom) * sizeof(wchar_t),
      LMade);
    if (LResult == HookIODoCrtConvert::Error)
    {
      AHandle.Failed = true;
      return false;
    }
    LModel.WideReadEnd = LModel.WideReadBase + static_cast<std::int64_t>(LMade / sizeof(wchar_t));
  }
  LModel.WideReadPtr = LModel.WideReadEnd;
  return true;
}

// glibc's _IO_wfile_underflow (wfileops.c): the next wide character without
// taking it, filling the wide get area when it is empty. The sticky end is
// WEOF (nothing else). A handle that cannot read fails (Failed, EBADF,
// WEOF). Leftover converted characters are returned straight. Otherwise
// bytes left in the main get area are converted into the wide buffer; with
// none, the main buffer is read (its own underflow is inlined here:
// ReadBase .. ReadEnd refilled from the IO) and converted, retried until a
// whole character comes out or the IO ends; a byte the charset rejects is
// EILSEQ (Failed). WEOF at the end (AtEnd, the offset lost). Returns the
// character (0 .. WCHAR) or WEOF.
wint_t HookIODoCrtWideUnderflowLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  // glibc's MB_LEN_MAX: the most bytes one wide character can take
  constexpr std::int64_t CMbLenMax = 16;

  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  unsigned char LAcc[CMbLenMax];
  std::int64_t LNAcc = 0;
  std::int64_t LCopied;
  std::int64_t LGot;
  std::int64_t LRoom;
  std::size_t LTaken;
  std::size_t LMade;
  HookIODoCrtConvert LResult;

  if (AHandle.AtEnd)
    return WEOF;
  if (!HookIODoCanRead(AHandle))
  {
    AHandle.Failed = true;
    errno = EBADF;
    return WEOF;
  }
  if (LModel.WideReadPtr < LModel.WideReadEnd)
    return static_cast<wint_t>(HookIODoCrtWideArea(LModel)[LModel.WideReadPtr]);
  // Convert what the main get area still holds, into the wide buffer from
  // its start
  if (LModel.ReadPtr < LModel.ReadEnd)
  {
    LModel.WideReadBase = 0;
    LModel.WideReadPtr = 0;
    LModel.WideReadInBackup = false;
    LRoom = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LModel.Wide.size());
    LResult = HookIODoCrtIconv(LModel.Converter->In, LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.ReadPtr,
      static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr), LTaken,
      LModel.Wide.data(), static_cast<std::size_t>(LRoom) * sizeof(wchar_t), LMade);
    LModel.ReadBase = LModel.ReadPtr;
    LModel.ReadPtr += static_cast<std::int64_t>(LTaken);
    LModel.WideReadEnd = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LMade / sizeof(wchar_t));
    if (LModel.WideReadPtr < LModel.WideReadEnd)
      return static_cast<wint_t>(LModel.Wide[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.WideReadPtr)]);
    if (LResult == HookIODoCrtConvert::Error)
    {
      errno = EILSEQ;
      AHandle.Failed = true;
      return WEOF;
    }
    // The leftover bytes slide to the main buffer's start, read on from there
    LGot = LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr;
    std::memmove(LModel.Buffer.data(), LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.ReadPtr,
      static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot));
    LModel.ReadBase = 0;
    LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
    LModel.ReadEnd = LGot;
  }
  else
  {
    LModel.ReadBase = 0;
    LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
    LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
  }
  LModel.ReadInBackup = false;
  if (!LModel.HasBuffer)
  {
    if (LModel.HaveBackup)
    {
      HookIODoCrtDropBackup(LModel);
      LModel.InBackup = false;
    }
    HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
  }
  LModel.WriteBase = 0;
  LModel.WritePtr = 0;
  LModel.WriteEnd = 0;
  LModel.WriteArea = true;
  if (!LModel.HasWide)
  {
    if (!LModel.WideBackup.empty())
    {
      HookIODoCrtWideDropBackup(LModel);
      LModel.InBackup = false;
    }
    HookIODoCrtWideAllocateLocked(AHandle);
  }
  HookIODoCrtFlushStdout(LModel);
  HookIODoCrtSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle);
  HookIODoCrtWideEmptyAreas(LModel);
  // Read bytes and convert until a whole character comes out or the IO ends
  for (;;)
  {
    LGot = HookIODoCrtRawLocked(AHandle, LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.ReadEnd,
      LModel.Buffer.size() - LModel.ReadEnd);
    if (LGot <= 0)
    {
      if ((LGot == 0) && (LNAcc == 0))
      {
        AHandle.AtEnd = true;
        LModel.OffsetKnown = false;
      }
      else
      {
        AHandle.Failed = true;
        LGot = 0;
      }
    }
    LModel.ReadEnd += LGot;
    if (LGot == 0)
    {
      if (LNAcc != 0)
        errno = EILSEQ;
      return WEOF;
    }
    // Normally convert straight from the main buffer; only when a previous
    // pass left a partial character (LNAcc) do a few bytes join it first
    if (LNAcc != 0)
    {
      LCopied = std::min<std::int64_t>(CMbLenMax - LNAcc, LGot);
      std::memcpy(LAcc + LNAcc, LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.ReadPtr,
        static_cast<std::size_t>(LCopied));
      LNAcc += LCopied;
      LModel.ReadBase = LModel.ReadPtr;
      LResult = HookIODoCrtIconv(LModel.Converter->In, LAcc, static_cast<std::size_t>(LNAcc),
        LTaken, LModel.Wide.data(), LModel.Wide.size() * sizeof(wchar_t), LMade);
      // Only the newly copied bytes the conversion used advance ReadPtr
      if (static_cast<std::int64_t>(LTaken) > (LNAcc - LCopied))
        LModel.ReadPtr += static_cast<std::int64_t>(LTaken) - (LNAcc - LCopied);
    }
    else
    {
      LModel.ReadBase = LModel.ReadPtr;
      LResult = HookIODoCrtIconv(LModel.Converter->In, LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.ReadPtr,
        static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr), LTaken,
        LModel.Wide.data(), LModel.Wide.size() * sizeof(wchar_t), LMade);
      LModel.ReadPtr += static_cast<std::int64_t>(LTaken);
    }
    LModel.WideReadEnd = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LMade / sizeof(wchar_t));
    if (LModel.WideReadEnd != 0)
      return static_cast<wint_t>(LModel.Wide[0]);
    if (LResult == HookIODoCrtConvert::Error)
    {
      errno = EILSEQ;
      AHandle.Failed = true;
      return WEOF;
    }
    // A partial character: read more. Bytes that made nothing slide to the
    // read's start; a partial character the buffer cannot extend is kept
    // aside (at most MB_LEN_MAX bytes, else EILSEQ)
    if (LNAcc == 0)
    {
      if (LModel.ReadBase < LModel.ReadPtr)
      {
        LGot = LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr;
        std::memmove(LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.ReadBase,
          LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.ReadPtr, static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot));
        LModel.ReadPtr = LModel.ReadBase;
        LModel.ReadEnd = LModel.ReadBase + LGot;
        continue;
      }
      LGot = LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr;
      if (LGot >= CMbLenMax)
      {
        errno = EILSEQ;
        AHandle.Failed = true;
        return WEOF;
      }
      std::memcpy(LAcc, LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.ReadPtr, static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot));
      LNAcc = LGot;
    }
    else
    {
      if (LTaken > 0)
      {
        std::memmove(LAcc, LAcc + LTaken, static_cast<std::size_t>(LNAcc) - LTaken);
        LNAcc -= static_cast<std::int64_t>(LTaken);
      }
      if (LNAcc == CMbLenMax)
      {
        errno = EILSEQ;
        AHandle.Failed = true;
        return WEOF;
      }
    }
    LModel.ReadBase = 0;
    LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
    LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
  }
}

// __wuflow / __wunderflow (wgenops.c): a wide stream read, the orientation
// made wide. In put mode it switches to the wide get mode first (WEOF when
// that fails). The wide get area's next character, else the main wide area's
// (leaving the wide backup area), else a fill (the wide backup area dropped
// first). ATake: __wuflow, the character is taken. On a byte-oriented
// stream turned the wrong way WEOF.
wint_t HookIODoCrtWideNextLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const bool ATake)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  wint_t LChar;

  if (LModel.Orientation == 0)
    HookIODoCrtFwideLocked(AHandle, 1);
  if (LModel.Orientation != 1)
    return WEOF;
  if (LModel.Putting && (HookIODoCrtWideSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
    return WEOF;
  if (LModel.WideReadPtr < LModel.WideReadEnd)
  {
    LChar = static_cast<wint_t>(HookIODoCrtWideArea(LModel)[LModel.WideReadPtr]);
    if (ATake)
      ++LModel.WideReadPtr;
    return LChar;
  }
  if (LModel.InBackup && LModel.WideReadInBackup)
  {
    HookIODoCrtWideToMain(LModel);
    if (LModel.WideReadPtr < LModel.WideReadEnd)
    {
      LChar = static_cast<wint_t>(LModel.Wide[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.WideReadPtr)]);
      if (ATake)
        ++LModel.WideReadPtr;
      return LChar;
    }
  }
  if (!LModel.WideBackup.empty())
    HookIODoCrtWideDropBackup(LModel);
  LChar = HookIODoCrtWideUnderflowLocked(AHandle);
  if ((LChar != WEOF) && ATake)
    ++LModel.WideReadPtr;
  return LChar;
}

// One wide character as glibc's getwc reads it (_IO_getwc_unlocked): the
// wide get area's next character (no orientation change), else __wuflow
wint_t HookIODoCrtWideGetLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (LModel.WideReadPtr < LModel.WideReadEnd)
    return static_cast<wint_t>(HookIODoCrtWideArea(LModel)[LModel.WideReadPtr++]);
  return HookIODoCrtWideNextLocked(AHandle, true);
}

// glibc's _IO_wdefault_pbackfail (wgenops.c, no markers): the pbackfail of
// a wide stream's table, reached by ungetwc after its fast path and by the
// byte ungetc after _IO_sputbackc's (the table turned wide with the
// orientation, iofwide.c). AChar goes in front of the wide get area through
// the wide backup area: entered (made at 128 wchar_t when there is none,
// the main area from WideReadPtr on its save area), or doubled when full.
// AtEnd is cleared. Returns AChar. The caller has refused WEOF and left put
// mode.
wint_t HookIODoCrtWidePbackfailLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wint_t AChar)
{
  constexpr std::int64_t CBackupSize = 128;

  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  const wchar_t LWide = static_cast<wchar_t>(AChar);
  std::vector<wchar_t> LGrown;
  std::int64_t LOld;

  // Its first test reads the BYTE get area (glibc's own code): a wide
  // character equal to the byte before ReadPtr, taken as a signed char,
  // steps ReadPtr back and pushes nothing
  if ((LModel.WideReadPtr > LModel.WideReadBase) && (!LModel.InBackup) &&
    (LModel.ReadPtr > 0) &&
    (static_cast<wint_t>(static_cast<signed char>(HookIODoCrtArea(LModel)[LModel.ReadPtr - 1]))
      == AChar))
  {
    --LModel.ReadPtr;
    AHandle.AtEnd = false;
    return AChar;
  }
  if (!LModel.WideReadInBackup)
  {
    if (LModel.WideBackup.empty())
    {
      LModel.WideBackup.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(CBackupSize), L'\0');
      LModel.WideSaveBase = 0;
      LModel.WideSaveEnd = CBackupSize;
      LModel.WideBackupBase = CBackupSize;
      LModel.WideSaveInBackup = true;
    }
    else if (LModel.WideReadPtr > LModel.WideReadBase)
      // save_for_wbackup with no markers keeps nothing: the area is empty
      LModel.WideBackupBase = LModel.WideSaveEnd;
    LModel.WideReadBase = LModel.WideReadPtr;
    HookIODoCrtWideToBackup(LModel);
  }
  else if (LModel.WideReadPtr <= LModel.WideReadBase)
  {
    LOld = LModel.WideReadEnd - LModel.WideReadBase;
    LGrown.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(2 * LOld), L'\0');
    std::memcpy(LGrown.data() + LOld, LModel.WideBackup.data() + LModel.WideReadBase,
      static_cast<std::size_t>(LOld) * sizeof(wchar_t));
    LModel.WideBackup.swap(LGrown);
    LModel.WideReadBase = 0;
    LModel.WideReadPtr = LOld;
    LModel.WideReadEnd = 2 * LOld;
    LModel.WideBackupBase = LModel.WideReadPtr;
  }
  --LModel.WideReadPtr;
  LModel.WideBackup[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.WideReadPtr)] = LWide;
  AHandle.AtEnd = false;
  return AChar;
}

// glibc's ungetwc on a wide stream (_IO_sputbackwc): the same character as
// the one before WideReadPtr in the main area just steps back; any other
// goes to the wide pbackfail. AtEnd is cleared. WEOF is refused. Returns
// the character or WEOF. In put mode the stream switches to the wide get
// mode first (unflushed wide characters land; WEOF when that fails).
wint_t HookIODoCrtWideUngetLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wint_t AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  const wchar_t LWide = static_cast<wchar_t>(AChar);

  if (AChar == WEOF)
    return WEOF;
  if (LModel.Putting && (HookIODoCrtWideSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
    return WEOF;
  if ((LModel.WideReadPtr > LModel.WideReadBase) && (!LModel.WideReadInBackup)
    && (LModel.Wide[static_cast<std::size_t>(LModel.WideReadPtr - 1)] == LWide))
  {
    --LModel.WideReadPtr;
    AHandle.AtEnd = false;
    return AChar;
  }
  return HookIODoCrtWidePbackfailLocked(AHandle, AChar);
}

// glibc's _IO_default_pbackfail (genops.c) with an int: what ungetwc reaches
// on a byte-oriented stream (its table's pbackfail). The byte before ReadPtr
// steps back only when it equals AChar whole (a character above 255 never
// does); otherwise the low byte goes in front through the backup area. In
// put mode the stream switches to get mode first. AtEnd cleared. Returns
// the low byte (0..255) or WEOF.
wint_t HookIODoCrtPbackfailLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wint_t AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::vector<unsigned char> LGrown;
  std::int64_t LOld;

  if (LModel.Putting && (HookIODoCrtSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
    return WEOF;
  if ((LModel.ReadPtr > LModel.ReadBase) && (!LModel.InBackup) &&
    (static_cast<wint_t>(HookIODoCrtArea(LModel)[LModel.ReadPtr - 1]) == AChar))
  {
    --LModel.ReadPtr;
    AHandle.AtEnd = false;
    return AChar;
  }
  if (!LModel.InBackup)
  {
    if (!LModel.HaveBackup)
    {
      LModel.Backup.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(CHookIODoBackupSize), 0);
      LModel.SaveBase = 0;
      LModel.SaveEnd = CHookIODoBackupSize;
      LModel.SaveInBackup = true;
      LModel.HaveBackup = true;
    }
    LModel.ReadBase = LModel.ReadPtr;
    HookIODoCrtToBackup(LModel);
  }
  else if (LModel.ReadPtr <= LModel.ReadBase)
  {
    LOld = LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadBase;
    LGrown.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(2 * LOld), 0);
    std::memcpy(LGrown.data() + LOld, LModel.Backup.data() + LModel.ReadBase,
      static_cast<std::size_t>(LOld));
    LModel.Backup.swap(LGrown);
    LModel.ReadBase = 0;
    LModel.ReadPtr = LOld;
    LModel.ReadEnd = 2 * LOld;
  }
  --LModel.ReadPtr;
  HookIODoCrtArea(LModel)[LModel.ReadPtr] = static_cast<unsigned char>(AChar);
  AHandle.AtEnd = false;
  return static_cast<wint_t>(static_cast<unsigned char>(AChar));
}

// glibc's ungetwc (ioungetwc.c): the stream turns wide when fresh, WEOF is
// refused, then _IO_sputbackwc: a wide stream through the wide backup
// area, a byte-oriented one (the wide get area is empty there) through the
// byte pbackfail
wint_t HookIODoCrtUngetWideLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const wint_t AChar)
{
  HookIODoCrtFwideLocked(AHandle, 1);
  if (AChar == WEOF)
    return WEOF;
  if (AHandle.Crt.Orientation > 0)
    return HookIODoCrtWideUngetLocked(AHandle, AChar);
  return HookIODoCrtPbackfailLocked(AHandle, AChar);
}

// glibc's fgetws line reader (_IO_getwline_info, extract the delimiter): up
// to ACount wide characters into AText, stopping after L'\n'; the stream
// turns wide when fresh (a byte-oriented one reads nothing). Returns the
// count stored.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtWideLineLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, wchar_t* AText,
  const std::int64_t ACount)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LLeft = ACount;
  std::int64_t LStored = 0;
  std::int64_t LHave;
  std::int64_t LI;
  wint_t LChar;
  const wchar_t* LArea;

  if (LModel.Orientation == 0)
    HookIODoCrtFwideLocked(AHandle, 1);
  while (LLeft != 0)
  {
    LHave = LModel.WideReadEnd - LModel.WideReadPtr;
    if (LHave <= 0)
    {
      LChar = HookIODoCrtWideNextLocked(AHandle, true);
      if (LChar == WEOF)
        break;
      AText[LStored++] = static_cast<wchar_t>(LChar);
      if (static_cast<wchar_t>(LChar) == L'\n')
        return LStored;
      --LLeft;
    }
    else
    {
      if (LHave > LLeft)
        LHave = LLeft;
      LArea = HookIODoCrtWideArea(LModel) + LModel.WideReadPtr;
      for (LI = 0; LI < LHave; ++LI)
      {
        if (LArea[LI] == L'\n')
        {
          std::memcpy(AText + LStored, LArea, static_cast<std::size_t>(LI + 1) * sizeof(wchar_t));
          LModel.WideReadPtr += LI + 1;
          return LStored + LI + 1;
        }
      }
      std::memcpy(AText + LStored, LArea, static_cast<std::size_t>(LHave) * sizeof(wchar_t));
      LModel.WideReadPtr += LHave;
      LStored += LHave;
      LLeft -= LHave;
    }
  }
  return LStored;
}

// The bytes the main get area's start holds for the first AChars wide
// characters of the wide get area: a fixed-width charset's count times
// Clen, else counted by converting them again (__libio_codecvt_length)
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtWideBytesLocked(HookIODoCrtModel& AModel, const std::int64_t AChars)
{
  return HookIODoCrtWideLength(*AModel.Converter, AModel.Buffer.data() + AModel.ReadBase,
    AModel.ReadEnd - AModel.ReadBase, AChars);
}

// glibc's _IO_wfile_sync: pending wide characters are flushed first (its
// failure is EOF, nothing else done). Then the descriptor steps back over
// the wide get area's unread characters: a fixed-width charset by their
// count times Clen (the main get area's own unread bytes are not counted,
// as glibc does not count them); otherwise the main get area is cut at the
// bytes its read characters came from and the descriptor steps back over
// the rest. Both get areas end at their pointers when the step succeeds; a
// failed step fails the sync unless errno is ESPIPE. Then the offset is no
// longer known. Returns 0 or EOF.
int HookIODoCrtWideSyncLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LDelta;
  std::int64_t LRead;

  if ((LModel.WideWritePtr > LModel.WideWriteBase) && (HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(AHandle) != 0))
    return EOF;
  LDelta = LModel.WideReadPtr - LModel.WideReadEnd;
  if (LDelta != 0)
  {
    if (LModel.Converter->Clen > 0)
      LDelta *= LModel.Converter->Clen;
    else
    {
      LRead = HookIODoCrtWideBytesLocked(LModel, LModel.WideReadPtr - LModel.WideReadBase);
      LModel.ReadPtr = LModel.ReadBase + LRead;
      LDelta = -(LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadBase - LRead);
    }
    if (HookIODoCrtSysSeekLocked(AHandle, LDelta, SEEK_CUR) >= 0)
    {
      LModel.WideReadEnd = LModel.WideReadPtr;
      LModel.ReadEnd = LModel.ReadPtr;
    }
    else if (errno != ESPIPE)
      return EOF;
  }
  LModel.OffsetKnown = false;
  return 0;
}

// glibc's do_ftell_wide (wfileops.c), once the wide buffer exists: pending
// wide characters on an appending stream first send the descriptor to the
// IO's end (the one change to the stream; a failed seek is -1). With none
// pending, the place is the descriptor's minus the unread characters'
// bytes (fixed width: their count times Clen plus the main get area's
// unread bytes; otherwise the main get area's bytes not yet read as
// characters). With some pending, their bytes are added (fixed width: the
// count times Clen; otherwise converted again to count them, from a scratch
// of their count times sizeof(wchar_t) bytes: a conversion that does not
// fit or fails gives WEOF in an off64_t, 4294967295, as glibc's), then the
// main put area's bytes (an appending stream from its base, any other from
// where the descriptor stands in the buffer). Below 0: EINVAL, -1.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtWideTellLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LOffset = 0;
  std::int64_t LPlace;
  std::int64_t LPending;
  std::int64_t LWideBase;
  std::int64_t LWidePtr;
  std::int64_t LWideEnd;
  std::vector<unsigned char> LScratch;
  std::size_t LTaken = 0;
  std::size_t LMade = 0;
  bool LUnflushed;
  const int LSaved = errno;

  if (LModel.HasWide)
  {
    LUnflushed = LModel.WideWritePtr > LModel.WideWriteBase;
    if (LUnflushed && AHandle.Appending)
    {
      if (HookIODoCrtSysSeekLocked(AHandle, 0, SEEK_END) < 0)
        return -1;
      LModel.OffsetKnown = true;
    }
    // glibc does not place a stream with ungot wide characters still to
    // read: -1 with EINVAL; with the backup area read up, the main area's
    // extent (the save area) counts, from its start
    if (LModel.InBackup)
    {
      if (LModel.WideReadPtr < LModel.WideReadEnd)
      {
        errno = EINVAL;
        return -1;
      }
      LWideBase = LModel.WideSaveBase;
      LWidePtr = LWideBase;
      LWideEnd = LModel.WideSaveEnd;
    }
    else
    {
      LWideBase = LModel.WideReadBase;
      LWidePtr = LModel.WideReadPtr;
      LWideEnd = LModel.WideReadEnd;
    }
    if (!LUnflushed)
    {
      if (LModel.Converter->Clen > 0)
      {
        LOffset -= (LWideEnd - LWidePtr) * LModel.Converter->Clen;
        LOffset -= LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr;
      }
      else
        LOffset -= LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadBase -
          HookIODoCrtWideBytesLocked(LModel, LWidePtr - LWideBase);
    }
    else
    {
      LPending = LModel.WideWritePtr - LModel.WideWriteBase;
      if (LModel.Converter->Clen > 0)
        LOffset += LPending * LModel.Converter->Clen;
      else
      {
        LScratch.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(LPending) * sizeof(wchar_t), 0);
        iconv(LModel.Converter->CountOut, nullptr, nullptr, nullptr, nullptr);
        errno = LSaved;
        if (HookIODoCrtIconv(LModel.Converter->CountOut, LModel.Wide.data() + LModel.WideWriteBase,
          static_cast<std::size_t>(LPending) * sizeof(wchar_t), LTaken, LScratch.data(),
          LScratch.size(), LMade) != HookIODoCrtConvert::Ok)
          return CHookIODoWideSeekWeof;
        LOffset += static_cast<std::int64_t>(LMade);
      }
      if (AHandle.Appending)
        LOffset += LModel.WritePtr - LModel.WriteBase;
      else
        LOffset += LModel.WritePtr - LModel.ReadEnd;
    }
  }
  LPlace = AHandle.Position + LOffset;
  if (LPlace < 0)
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  return LPlace;
}

// glibc's _IO_wfile_seekoff for fseek (the origin already checked): a
// stream that was writing (pending wide characters, or in put mode)
// switches to the wide get mode first (its failure: WEOF in an off64_t).
// With no wide buffer the main one is made (on a wide stream that makes
// the wide one too when the main was missing) and every area is emptied
// at its start. From the caller's place: the unread characters' bytes are
// counted back (fixed width: as ftell counts them; otherwise the main get
// area is cut where its read characters end); with the offset unknown the
// descriptor seeks itself. From the end: the IO's size, an IO with none
// seeks itself. With the offset known, a target inside the main buffer's
// bytes only moves ReadPtr there, and the bytes before it become the wide
// get area (counted, or converted); otherwise the descriptor goes to the
// target's block start, reads the block (only up to the target when the
// stream had nothing buffered), ReadPtr at the target, the bytes before it
// converted into the wide get area; a short read finishes by a plain seek.
// The plain seek and every success clear AtEnd and leave all areas empty
// or as just set; returns the new place or -1.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtWideSeekLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t AOffset,
  const int AOrigin)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LOffset = AOffset;
  int LOrigin = AOrigin;
  std::int64_t LSize;
  std::int64_t LStart;
  std::int64_t LBlock;
  std::int64_t LDelta;
  std::int64_t LCount;
  std::int64_t LRead;
  std::int64_t LResult;
  bool LExact;
  bool LWasWriting;
  bool LInBuffer;

  LExact = (LModel.WideReadBase == LModel.WideReadEnd) &&
    (LModel.WideWriteBase == LModel.WideWritePtr);
  LWasWriting = (LModel.WideWritePtr > LModel.WideWriteBase) || LModel.Putting;
  if (LWasWriting && (HookIODoCrtWideSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle) != 0))
    return CHookIODoWideSeekWeof;
  if (!LModel.HasWide)
  {
    // A wide get area with no wide buffer is the backup area ungetwc made:
    // glibc frees it and clears the flag
    if (LModel.WideReadInBackup)
    {
      HookIODoCrtWideDropBackup(LModel);
      LModel.InBackup = false;
    }
    HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
    HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
    LModel.ReadBase = 0;
    LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
    LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
    LModel.ReadInBackup = false;
    HookIODoCrtWideEmptyAreas(LModel);
  }
  // SEEK_CUR / SEEK_END make the target absolute when they can; otherwise
  // (and after a failed conversion) the descriptor seeks itself: glibc's
  // "dumb" path at the end
  if (LOrigin == SEEK_CUR)
  {
    if (LModel.Converter->Clen > 0)
    {
      LOffset -= (LModel.WideReadEnd - LModel.WideReadPtr) * LModel.Converter->Clen;
      LOffset -= LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr;
    }
    else
    {
      LRead = HookIODoCrtWideBytesLocked(LModel, LModel.WideReadPtr - LModel.WideReadBase);
      LModel.ReadPtr = LModel.ReadBase + LRead;
      LModel.WideReadEnd = LModel.WideReadPtr;
      LOffset -= LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadBase - LRead;
    }
    if (LModel.OffsetKnown)
    {
      if ((LOffset > 0) && (AHandle.Position > (INT64_MAX - LOffset)))
      {
        errno = EINVAL;
        return -1;
      }
      LOffset += AHandle.Position;
      LOrigin = SEEK_SET;
    }
  }
  else if (LOrigin == SEEK_END)
  {
    LSize = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSize(AHandle.Stream);
    if (LSize >= 0)
    {
      if ((LOffset > 0) && (LSize > (INT64_MAX - LOffset)))
      {
        errno = EINVAL;
        return -1;
      }
      LOffset += LSize;
      LOrigin = SEEK_SET;
    }
  }
  if (LOrigin == SEEK_SET)
  {
    // A target made absolute drops the wide backup area (ungot wide
    // characters are lost, as C says); the "dumb" path from an unknown
    // offset keeps it, as glibc's does
    HookIODoCrtWideDropBackup(LModel);
    LInBuffer = false;
    // A target inside the main buffer's bytes
    if (LModel.OffsetKnown && LModel.HasBuffer && (!LModel.InBackup))
    {
      LStart = AHandle.Position - LModel.ReadEnd;
      if ((LOffset >= LStart) && (LOffset < AHandle.Position))
      {
        LInBuffer = true;
        LModel.ReadBase = 0;
        LModel.ReadPtr = LOffset - LStart;
        HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
        HookIODoCrtWideEmptyAreas(LModel);
        if (HookIODoCrtAdjustWideLocked(AHandle, false))
        {
          AHandle.AtEnd = false;
          return LOffset;
        }
      }
    }
    // A negative target fails at the block's seek, as glibc's
    if ((!LInBuffer) && HookIODoCanRead(AHandle))
    {
      // The target's block start (glibc's mask, as the byte stream's)
      LBlock = LOffset & ~(LModel.Buffer.size() - 1);
      LDelta = LOffset - LBlock;
      if (LDelta > LModel.Buffer.size())
      {
        LBlock = LOffset;
        LDelta = 0;
      }
      if (HookIODoCrtSysSeekLocked(AHandle, LBlock, SEEK_SET) < 0)
        return -1;
      LCount = 0;
      if (LDelta != 0)
        LCount = HookIODoCrtRawLocked(AHandle, LModel.Buffer.data(),
          LExact ? LDelta : LModel.Buffer.size());
      if (LCount < LDelta)
      {
        LOffset = (LCount < 0) ? LDelta : (LDelta - LCount);
        LOrigin = SEEK_CUR;
      }
      else
      {
        LModel.ReadBase = 0;
        LModel.ReadPtr = LDelta;
        LModel.ReadEnd = LCount;
        HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
        HookIODoCrtWideEmptyAreas(LModel);
        if (HookIODoCrtAdjustWideLocked(AHandle, true))
        {
          LModel.OffsetKnown = true;
          AHandle.AtEnd = false;
          return LOffset;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // glibc's "dumb" path: the descriptor seeks itself
  LResult = HookIODoCrtSysSeekLocked(AHandle, LOffset, LOrigin);
  if (LResult >= 0)
  {
    AHandle.AtEnd = false;
    LModel.OffsetKnown = true;
    LModel.ReadBase = 0;
    LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
    LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
    HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
    HookIODoCrtWideEmptyAreas(LModel);
  }
  return LResult;
}

// glibc's ftello / ftell (do_ftell, then ftello.c): the descriptor's place
// minus the get area's unread bytes (only once the main buffer exists: a
// fresh stream's ungot bytes are not counted), refused below 0 with EINVAL;
// then, in the backup area, minus the main area's unread part (that result
// is not checked: it can be negative). -1 itself is a failure (errno EIO
// when none is set).
// With unflushed bytes in the put area the place counts them instead: an
// appending stream's descriptor first goes to the IO's end (do_ftell's one
// change to the stream; a failed seek is -1) and its bytes are added there;
// any other stream adds WritePtr - ReadEnd (ReadEnd is where the
// descriptor stands in the buffer).
// A wide stream's place is do_ftell_wide's (HookIODoCrtWideTellLocked),
// with no backup area's adjustment.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtTellLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LPlace;
  std::int64_t LOffset = 0;
  bool LUnflushed;

  if (LModel.Orientation > 0)
  {
    LPlace = HookIODoCrtWideTellLocked(AHandle);
    if ((LPlace == -1) && (errno == 0))
      errno = EIO;
    return LPlace;
  }
  if (LModel.HasBuffer)
  {
    LUnflushed = LModel.WritePtr > LModel.WriteBase;
    if (LUnflushed && AHandle.Appending)
    {
      if (HookIODoCrtSysSeekLocked(AHandle, 0, SEEK_END) < 0)
        return -1;
      LModel.OffsetKnown = true;
      LOffset = LModel.WritePtr - LModel.WriteBase;
    }
    else if (LUnflushed)
      LOffset = LModel.WritePtr - LModel.ReadEnd;
    else
      LOffset = -(LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr);
  }
  LPlace = AHandle.Position + LOffset;
  if (LPlace < 0)
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  if (LModel.InBackup)
    LPlace -= LModel.SaveEnd - LModel.SaveBase;
  if ((LPlace == -1) && (errno == 0))
    errno = EIO;
  return LPlace;
}

// _IO_new_file_seekoff's plain seek (its "dumb" path): the backup area
// dropped, the descriptor seeks AOffset from AOrigin itself; on success the
// get area empties, AtEnd is cleared and the offset is known. Returns the
// new place or -1.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtSeekPlainLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t AOffset,
  const int AOrigin)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LResult;

  if (LModel.HaveBackup)
    HookIODoCrtDropBackup(LModel);
  LResult = HookIODoCrtSysSeekLocked(AHandle, AOffset, AOrigin);
  if (LResult >= 0)
  {
    AHandle.AtEnd = false;
    LModel.OffsetKnown = true;
    LModel.ReadBase = 0;
    LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
    LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
    HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
  }
  return LResult;
}

// glibc's fseek / fseeko / rewind core (_IO_seekoff_unlocked, then
// _IO_new_file_seekoff, mode in + out): a byte-oriented stream drops its
// backup area first (from the caller's place, the backup area's unread bytes
// counted). The main buffer is made (a backup area in use dropped). From
// the caller's place: the get area's unread bytes counted back, then with
// the offset unknown the descriptor seeks itself; from the end: the IO's
// size. With the offset known, a target inside the main buffer only moves
// ReadPtr; otherwise the descriptor goes to the target's block start and
// reads the block (only up to the target when the get area was empty),
// ReadPtr at the target; a short read finishes by a plain seek. Success
// clears AtEnd and makes the offset known; a failure keeps AtEnd. Returns
// the new place or -1.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtSeekLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t AOffset,
  const int AOrigin)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LOffset = AOffset;
  int LOrigin = AOrigin;
  std::int64_t LSize;
  std::int64_t LStart;
  std::int64_t LBlock;
  std::int64_t LDelta;
  std::int64_t LCount;
  bool LExact;

  if ((LOrigin != SEEK_SET) && (LOrigin != SEEK_CUR) && (LOrigin != SEEK_END))
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  if ((LModel.Orientation < 0) && LModel.HaveBackup)
  {
    if ((LOrigin == SEEK_CUR) && LModel.InBackup)
      LOffset -= LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr;
    HookIODoCrtDropBackup(LModel);
  }
  // A wide stream drops its wide backup area first. From the caller's place
  // while reading in it, glibc aborts the process (ioseekoff.c: a pushed-back
  // wide character has no byte place to count back from); a real FILE dies
  // the same way.
  if ((LModel.Orientation > 0) && (!LModel.WideBackup.empty()))
  {
    if ((LOrigin == SEEK_CUR) && LModel.InBackup)
      std::abort();
    HookIODoCrtWideDropBackup(LModel);
  }
  // A wide stream's seek is _IO_wfile_seekoff's
  if (LModel.Orientation > 0)
    return HookIODoCrtWideSeekLocked(AHandle, LOffset, LOrigin);
  // POSIX: after an fflush the descriptor's place must be exact (both
  // areas empty). A stream that was writing flushes and switches to get
  // mode first (its failure fails the seek).
  LExact = (LModel.ReadBase == LModel.ReadEnd) && (LModel.WriteBase == LModel.WritePtr);
  if (((LModel.WritePtr > LModel.WriteBase) || LModel.Putting)
    && (HookIODoCrtSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
    return -1;
  if (!LModel.HasBuffer)
  {
    if (LModel.InBackup)
    {
      LModel.InBackup = false;
      LModel.Backup.clear();
      LModel.HaveBackup = false;
      LModel.SaveBase = 0;
      LModel.SaveEnd = 0;
      LModel.ReadInBackup = false;
      LModel.SaveInBackup = true;
    }
    HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
    HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
    LModel.ReadBase = 0;
    LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
    LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
  }
  if (LOrigin == SEEK_CUR)
  {
    LOffset -= LModel.ReadEnd - LModel.ReadPtr;
    if (!LModel.OffsetKnown)
      return HookIODoCrtSeekPlainLocked(AHandle, LOffset, SEEK_CUR);
    if ((LOffset > 0) && (AHandle.Position > (INT64_MAX - LOffset)))
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return -1;
    }
    LOffset += AHandle.Position;
    if (LOffset < 0)
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return -1;
    }
  }
  else if (LOrigin == SEEK_END)
  {
    // A regular file's size; an IO with none seeks itself
    LSize = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSize(AHandle.Stream);
    if (LSize < 0)
      return HookIODoCrtSeekPlainLocked(AHandle, LOffset, SEEK_END);
    if ((LOffset > 0) && (LSize > (INT64_MAX - LOffset)))
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return -1;
    }
    LOffset += LSize;
  }
  HookIODoCrtDropBackup(LModel);
  // A target inside the main buffer's bytes
  if (LModel.OffsetKnown)
  {
    LStart = AHandle.Position - LModel.ReadEnd;
    if ((LOffset >= LStart) && (LOffset < AHandle.Position))
    {
      LModel.ReadBase = 0;
      LModel.ReadPtr = LOffset - LStart;
      HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
      AHandle.AtEnd = false;
      return LOffset;
    }
  }
  if (!HookIODoCanRead(AHandle))
    return HookIODoCrtSeekPlainLocked(AHandle, LOffset, SEEK_SET);
  // The target's "block start": glibc masks with the buffer's size - 1
  // whatever that size is (measured with odd sizes), and goes to the target
  // itself when that leaves more than a buffer to read (a negative target
  // fails at the seek)
  LBlock = LOffset & ~(LModel.Buffer.size() - 1);
  LDelta = LOffset - LBlock;
  if (LDelta > LModel.Buffer.size())
  {
    LBlock = LOffset;
    LDelta = 0;
  }
  if (HookIODoCrtSysSeekLocked(AHandle, LBlock, SEEK_SET) < 0)
    return -1;
  LCount = 0;
  if (LDelta != 0)
  {
    LCount = HookIODoCrtRawLocked(AHandle, LModel.Buffer.data(),
      LExact ? LDelta : LModel.Buffer.size());
    if (LCount < LDelta)
    {
      LModel.ReadBase = 0;
      LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
      LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
      return HookIODoCrtSeekPlainLocked(AHandle, (LCount < 0) ? LDelta : (LDelta - LCount),
        SEEK_CUR);
    }
  }
  LModel.ReadBase = 0;
  LModel.ReadPtr = LDelta;
  LModel.ReadEnd = LCount;
  HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
  LModel.OffsetKnown = true;
  AHandle.AtEnd = false;
  return LOffset;
}

// _IO_new_file_sync: unflushed bytes in the put area are flushed first
// (_IO_do_flush; its failure is EOF, nothing else done). Then the
// descriptor steps back over the get area's unread bytes (ReadPtr -
// ReadEnd; in the backup area those of the backup area only) and the get
// area ends at ReadPtr; a failed step fails the sync unless errno is
// ESPIPE. Then the offset is no longer known. Returns 0 or EOF.
// A wide stream's sync is _IO_wfile_sync's (HookIODoCrtWideSyncLocked).
int HookIODoCrtSyncLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  std::int64_t LDelta;

  if (LModel.Orientation > 0)
    return HookIODoCrtWideSyncLocked(AHandle);
  if ((LModel.WritePtr > LModel.WriteBase) && (HookIODoCrtDoFlushLocked(AHandle) != 0))
    return EOF;
  LDelta = LModel.ReadPtr - LModel.ReadEnd;
  if (LDelta != 0)
  {
    if (HookIODoCrtSysSeekLocked(AHandle, LDelta, SEEK_CUR) >= 0)
      LModel.ReadEnd = LModel.ReadPtr;
    else if (errno != ESPIPE)
      return EOF;
  }
  LModel.OffsetKnown = false;
  return 0;
}

// For setvbuf while the get area is the backup area: the descriptor goes
// back to the caller's place behind the ungot bytes (over the main area's
// unread bytes, which the save area holds) and the save area is the new
// main buffer's empty start: the ungot bytes stay unread in the backup
// area, the next fill starts at the caller's place. EOF when the
// descriptor cannot step back. The offset is no longer known.
int HookIODoCrtKeepUngotLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  const std::int64_t LMainUnread = LModel.SaveEnd - LModel.SaveBase;

  if ((LMainUnread != 0) && (HookIODoCrtSysSeekLocked(AHandle, -LMainUnread, SEEK_CUR) < 0))
    return EOF;
  LModel.SaveBase = 0;
  LModel.SaveEnd = 0;
  LModel.OffsetKnown = false;
  return 0;
}

// _IO_new_file_setbuf (_IO_default_setbuf): after a sync (its failure is
// the result), no array or a size of 0 makes the stream unbuffered on the
// 1-byte _shortbuf, otherwise the caller's array of ASize bytes is the
// buffer; the get area is empty at its start. Returns 0 or EOF.
//
// A backup area not in use stays as it is (glibc does not touch it). While
// reading from it, glibc's sync drops the ungot bytes and its save area
// keeps pointing into the main buffer it then frees (measured on a real
// FILE: the next reads return freed memory and fclose aborts in free()).
// No defined bytes exist to copy there, so the model keeps the stream as
// the caller stands in it (HookIODoCrtKeepUngotLocked): the ungot bytes
// are read first, then the file from the caller's place.
int HookIODoCrtSetBufferLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, char* ABuffer, const std::size_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  const bool LUngot = LModel.InBackup;

  if (LUngot)
  {
    if (HookIODoCrtKeepUngotLocked(AHandle) == EOF)
      return EOF;
  }
  else if (HookIODoCrtSyncLocked(AHandle) == EOF)
    return EOF;
  if ((ABuffer == nullptr) || (ASize == 0))
  {
    LModel.Unbuffered = true;
    LModel.Buffer.assign(1, 0);
  }
  else
  {
    LModel.Unbuffered = false;
    LModel.Buffer.adopt(reinterpret_cast<unsigned char*>(ABuffer),
      static_cast<std::int64_t>(ASize));
  }
  LModel.HasBuffer = true;
  // _IO_new_file_setbuf: the put area is the new buffer's empty start
  // (the sync above flushed it)
  HookIODoCrtEmptyPutArea(LModel);
  // The get area is the new buffer's empty start, unless it is still the
  // backup area holding the ungot bytes (the empty main area then waits in
  // the save area)
  if (!LUngot)
  {
    LModel.ReadBase = 0;
    LModel.ReadPtr = 0;
    LModel.ReadEnd = 0;
  }
  return 0;
}

// glibc's setvbuf (iosetvbuf.c _IO_setvbuf): _IOFBF clears the line and
// unbuffered flags and, with no array, only makes the buffer when there is
// none (its own size: ASize is ignored, measured); _IOLBF sets the line
// flag and, with no array, does nothing else; _IONBF is unbuffered. An
// array goes through HookIODoCrtSetBufferLocked. Any other mode is EOF with
// errno untouched (measured). Returns 0 or EOF.
int HookIODoCrtSetvbufLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, char* ABuffer, const int AMode,
  const std::size_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;

  if (AMode == _IOFBF)
  {
    LModel.LineBuffered = false;
    LModel.Unbuffered = false;
    if (ABuffer == nullptr)
    {
      HookIODoCrtAllocateLocked(AHandle);
      return 0;
    }
  }
  else if (AMode == _IOLBF)
  {
    LModel.Unbuffered = false;
    LModel.LineBuffered = true;
    if (ABuffer == nullptr)
      return 0;
  }
  else if (AMode == _IONBF)
  {
    LModel.LineBuffered = false;
    LModel.Unbuffered = true;
    return HookIODoCrtSetBufferLocked(AHandle, nullptr, 0);
  }
  else
    return EOF;
  return HookIODoCrtSetBufferLocked(AHandle, ABuffer, ASize);
}

// glibc's setbuf (_IO_setbuffer at BUFSIZ): the line flag cleared, then
// the array (or none: unbuffered) as the buffer; its result is dropped
void HookIODoCrtSetbufLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, char* ABuffer)
{
  AHandle.Crt.LineBuffered = false;
  HookIODoCrtSetBufferLocked(AHandle, ABuffer, (ABuffer == nullptr) ? 0 : BUFSIZ);
}
#endif

// fread's read of up to ASize bytes, through the target CRT's FILE model
// (HookIODoCrtReadLocked: ungot bytes first, Windows text mode
// translated). A handle that cannot read fails where the target CRT fails
// it: its stdio refusal, or the descriptor's read (EBADF).
std::int64_t HookIODoReadLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
  return HookIODoCrtReadLocked(AHandle, ABuffer, ASize);
}

// One byte as the target CRT's fgetc / getc reads it: the byte (0..255) or
// EOF. A handle that cannot read fails where the target CRT fails it (see
// HookIODoCrtGetLocked: ucrt's _filbuf, glibc's underflow).
int HookIODoGetLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  return HookIODoCrtGetLocked(AHandle);
}

// fwrite's write of ASize bytes through the target CRT's FILE model: ucrt's
// _fwrite_nolock (HookIODoCrtWriteLocked: the bytes written), glibc's
// _IO_sputn (HookIODoCrtPutnLocked: the bytes written, or -1 for its EOF)
std::int64_t HookIODoWriteLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* ABuffer,
  const std::int64_t ASize)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  return HookIODoCrtWriteLocked(AHandle, ABuffer, ASize);
#else
  return HookIODoCrtPutnLocked(AHandle, ABuffer, ASize);
#endif
}

// fseek's rule: AOffset from the start (SEEK_SET), the caller's place
// (SEEK_CUR) or the end (SEEK_END); an unknown origin fails with EINVAL.
// Linux: glibc's (HookIODoCrtSeekLocked). Windows, as ucrt's fseek: past a
// valid origin AtEnd is cleared whether or not the seek then succeeds; a
// read-only binary stream whose target lies in its buffer only moves in it
// (HookIODoCrtSeekInBufferLocked); otherwise SEEK_CUR's place is ucrt's
// ftell, the buffer is dropped (a read-only stream's next fill asks for the
// small size) and the descriptor moves: the target must be reachable in the
// IO (past the end when the IO allows it), before the start or out of
// reach fails with EINVAL; success clears the Ctrl-Z end. Returns 0 or -1.
int HookIODoSeekLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t AOffset, const int AOrigin)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  std::int64_t LBase = 0;
  std::int64_t LTarget;

  if ((AOrigin != SEEK_SET) && (AOrigin != SEEK_CUR) && (AOrigin != SEEK_END))
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  AHandle.AtEnd = false;
  if (HookIODoCrtSeekInBufferLocked(AHandle, AOffset, AOrigin))
    return 0;
  // SEEK_CUR's place is taken before the buffer is flushed and dropped (the
  // flush's result is not checked: ucrt's fseek does not)
  if (AOrigin == SEEK_CUR)
    LBase = HookIODoPlaceLocked(AHandle);
  HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(AHandle);
  HookIODoCrtResetLocked(AHandle, true);
  if (AOrigin == SEEK_END)
  {
    LBase = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSize(AHandle.Stream);
    // An IO with no size may still know its end
    if (LBase < 0)
      LBase = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, 0, ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromEnd);
    if (LBase < 0)
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return -1;
    }
  }
  // LBase is never negative here except a place before the start (ungetc at
  // 0); the sum is checked before it is formed
  if ((AOffset > 0) && (LBase > (INT64_MAX - AOffset)))
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  LTarget = LBase + AOffset;
  if (LTarget < 0)
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, LTarget, ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromStart) != LTarget)
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return -1;
  }
  AHandle.Position = LTarget;
  // lowio's lseek clears the Ctrl-Z end
  AHandle.Crt.LowEof = false;
  return 0;
#else
  return (HookIODoCrtSeekLocked(AHandle, AOffset, AOrigin) < 0) ? -1 : 0;
#endif
}

// Runs AWork(handle) under AFile's stream lock. False: AFile is not a HookIO
// handle. A handle closed by a call that raced this one fails with EBADF
// (AWork does not run); out of memory inside AWork is ENOMEM. The caller
// sets its result to the failure value before the call. Every call that
// can move the handle's end / error state runs here, so the glibc head's
// flags are mirrored here once AWork is done (still under the lock).
template <typename TWork>
bool HookIODoWith(std::FILE* AFile, TWork&& AWork)
{
  const HookIODoHandleRef LHandle = HookIODoFindHandle(AFile);

  if (!LHandle)
    return false;
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(*LHandle->StreamLock);
    if (LHandle->Closed)
    {
      errno = EBADF;
      return true;
    }
    try
    {
      AWork(*LHandle);
    }
    catch (...)
    {
      HookIODoMirrorFlags(*LHandle);
      throw;
    }
    HookIODoMirrorFlags(*LHandle);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
  }
  return true;
}

// The bytes fread / fwrite move for ACount elements of ASize, by the target
// CRT's rule: ucrt refuses a product past SIZE_MAX (its parameter check:
// EINVAL, 0, no ferror); glibc takes the product as size_t arithmetic gives
// it (wrapped, no check), and a product of 0 moves nothing. A count past
// INT64_MAX (never a real buffer) is clamped there. False: nothing moves.
bool HookIODoByteCount(const std::size_t ASize, const std::size_t ACount, std::int64_t& ABytes)
{
  std::size_t LBytes;

  ABytes = 0;
  if ((ASize == 0) || (ACount == 0))
    return false;
#if defined(_WIN32)
  if (ACount > (SIZE_MAX / ASize))
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return false;
  }
#endif
  LBytes = ASize * ACount;
  if (LBytes == 0)
    return false;
  if (LBytes > static_cast<std::size_t>(INT64_MAX))
    ABytes = INT64_MAX;
  else
    ABytes = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LBytes);
  return true;
}

// fread: whole elements; a partial one is read and not counted. Linux, as
// glibc's _IO_fread: every element counts when the whole (wrapped) product
// was read.
bool HookIODoRead(void* ABuffer, const std::size_t ASize, const std::size_t ACount,
  std::FILE* AFile, std::size_t& AResult)
{
  AResult = 0;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    std::int64_t LBytes;
    std::int64_t LGot;
    if (!HookIODoByteCount(ASize, ACount, LBytes))
      return;
    LGot = HookIODoReadLocked(AHandle, static_cast<unsigned char*>(ABuffer), LBytes);
#if defined(_WIN32)
    AResult = static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot) / ASize;
#else
    if (static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot) == (ASize * ACount))
      AResult = ACount;
    else
      AResult = static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot) / ASize;
#endif
  });
}

// fwrite: whole elements written through the target CRT's FILE model.
// Linux, as glibc's _IO_fwrite: a wide stream writes nothing (0), a fresh
// one turns byte-oriented, and every element counts when _IO_sputn took
// every byte or gave EOF (an overflow that failed after the last byte was
// taken).
bool HookIODoWrite(const void* ABuffer, const std::size_t ASize, const std::size_t ACount,
  std::FILE* AFile, std::size_t& AResult)
{
  AResult = 0;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    std::int64_t LGot;
    std::int64_t LTotal;
    if (!HookIODoByteCount(ASize, ACount, LTotal))
      return;
#if defined(_WIN32)
    LGot = HookIODoWriteLocked(AHandle, static_cast<const unsigned char*>(ABuffer), LTotal);
    AResult = static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot) / ASize;
#else
    if (!HookIODoCrtNarrowLocked(AHandle))
      return;
    LGot = HookIODoWriteLocked(AHandle, static_cast<const unsigned char*>(ABuffer), LTotal);
    if ((static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot) == (ASize * ACount)) || (LGot < 0))
      AResult = ACount;
    else
      AResult = static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot) / ASize;
#endif
  });
}

// fseek / _fseeki64 / fseeko64: 0 or -1
bool HookIODoSeek(std::FILE* AFile, const std::int64_t AOffset, const int AOrigin, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = -1;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    AResult = HookIODoSeekLocked(AHandle, AOffset, AOrigin);
  });
}

// _ftelli64 / ftello / ftello64: the target CRT's ftell on its FILE model
// (HookIODoCrtTellLocked), its value as it is: its own refusals set errno
// themselves, and neither CRT checks every sign (ucrt none: an ungot '\n'
// at the front of a text buffer can make it negative; glibc not after its
// backup area's adjustment).
bool HookIODoTell(std::FILE* AFile, std::int64_t& AResult)
{
  AResult = -1;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    AResult = HookIODoCrtTellLocked(AHandle);
  });
}

// ftell: as HookIODoTell, and a place past what a long holds is -1 with
// EINVAL, as ucrt's ftell gives (measured on a real file seeked past 2 GiB).
// Only Windows can reach it: on x86_64 Linux a long is 64 bits and holds any
// place, as glibc's ftell does.
bool HookIODoTellLong(std::FILE* AFile, long& AResult)
{
  std::int64_t LPlace = -1;
  bool LOurs;

  AResult = -1;
  LOurs = HookIODoTell(AFile, LPlace);
  if (!LOurs)
    return false;
  // A negative place goes back as it is (a failure is -1 already)
  if (LPlace > static_cast<std::int64_t>(LONG_MAX))
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return true;
  }
  AResult = static_cast<long>(LPlace);
  return true;
}

// rewind: to the start. Windows, as ucrt's rewind (rewind.cpp): written
// bytes are flushed, the buffer is dropped without the small-size rule of
// fseek (and never by fseek's fast track), both flags and the Ctrl-Z end
// are cleared, then the descriptor goes to 0; a failed seek sets Failed
// again. Linux, as glibc's: its fseek to 0, then clearerr (both flags
// cleared even when the seek fails).
bool HookIODoRewind(std::FILE* AFile)
{
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
#if defined(_WIN32)
    HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(AHandle);
    HookIODoCrtResetLocked(AHandle, false);
    AHandle.AtEnd = false;
    AHandle.Failed = false;
    AHandle.Crt.LowEof = false;
    if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSeek(AHandle.Stream, 0, ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::SeekOrigin::FromStart) == 0)
      AHandle.Position = 0;
    else
      AHandle.Failed = true;
#else
    HookIODoSeekLocked(AHandle, 0, SEEK_SET);
    AHandle.AtEnd = false;
    AHandle.Failed = false;
#endif
  });
}

// feof
bool HookIODoEof(std::FILE* AFile, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = 0;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    AResult = AHandle.AtEnd ? 1 : 0;
  });
}

// ferror
bool HookIODoError(std::FILE* AFile, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = 0;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    AResult = AHandle.Failed ? 1 : 0;
  });
}

// clearerr (Windows text mode: also the Ctrl-Z end, as ucrt's)
bool HookIODoClearError(std::FILE* AFile)
{
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    AHandle.AtEnd = false;
    AHandle.Failed = false;
#if defined(_WIN32)
    AHandle.Crt.LowEof = false;
#endif
  });
}

// The IO's IOFlush for a handle that writes; 0 or EOF (Failed, errno EIO)
int HookIODoFlushLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  if (!HookIODoCanWrite(AHandle))
    return 0;
  if (::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOFlush(AHandle.Stream))
    return 0;
  AHandle.Failed = true;
  errno = EIO;
  return EOF;
}

// The target CRT's flush of a handle's unflushed written bytes, as fflush
// and fclose run it: ucrt's __acrt_stdio_flush_nolock
// (HookIODoCrtFlushLocked), glibc's _IO_SYNC (HookIODoCrtSyncLocked, which
// also steps a reading handle's descriptor back over its unread bytes:
// measured on a real FILE, tests\probe\hookabi\fflush_read.c). 0 or EOF.
int HookIODoCrtFlushHandleLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  return HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(AHandle);
#else
  return HookIODoCrtSyncLocked(AHandle);
#endif
}

// What fflush(NULL) and the exit flush do to one handle: only a handle
// holding written bytes flushes them (ucrt's common_flush_all: a stream
// that writes and does not read; glibc's _IO_flush_all: unflushed bytes in
// the put area, a wide stream's in its wide put area, through
// overflow(EOF)). A reading handle is left alone. 0 or EOF.
int HookIODoCrtFlushWrittenLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  if (AHandle.Crt.StreamRead || (!AHandle.Crt.StreamWrite))
    return 0;
  return HookIODoCrtFlushLocked(AHandle);
#else
  if ((AHandle.Crt.Orientation <= 0) && (AHandle.Crt.WritePtr <= AHandle.Crt.WriteBase))
    return 0;
  if ((AHandle.Crt.Orientation > 0) && (AHandle.Crt.WideWritePtr <= AHandle.Crt.WideWriteBase))
    return 0;
  return (HookIODoCrtOverflowLocked(AHandle, EOF) == EOF) ? EOF : 0;
#endif
}

// fflush of one handle (nil is HookIODoFlushAll's): the target CRT's flush
// (HookIODoCrtFlushHandleLocked), then the IO's own IOFlush
// (HookIODoFlushLocked). ucrt's flush leaves a reading stream alone.
bool HookIODoFlush(std::FILE* AFile, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = EOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    if (HookIODoCrtFlushHandleLocked(AHandle) == EOF)
      return;
    AResult = HookIODoFlushLocked(AHandle);
  });
}

// Every open handle, copied out under the registry lock (each is then
// worked on under its own stream lock only); empty when none is open
std::vector<HookIODoHandleRef> HookIODoOpenHandles()
{
  std::vector<HookIODoHandleRef> LOpen;

  if (HookIODoOpenCount.load() == 0)
    return LOpen;
  std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
  LOpen.reserve(HookIODoHandles().size());
  for (const auto& LEntry : HookIODoHandles())
    LOpen.push_back(LEntry.second);
  return LOpen;
}

// fflush(nil)'s half for HookIO: every open handle's written bytes
// (HookIODoCrtFlushWrittenLocked), then the IO's IOFlush; 0 or EOF when
// any failed.
int HookIODoFlushAll()
{
  std::vector<HookIODoHandleRef> LOpen;
  int LResult = 0;

  try
  {
    LOpen = HookIODoOpenHandles();
    for (const HookIODoHandleRef& LHandle : LOpen)
    {
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(*LHandle->StreamLock);
      if (LHandle->Closed)
        continue;
      if (HookIODoCrtFlushWrittenLocked(*LHandle) != 0)
        LResult = EOF;
      if (HookIODoFlushLocked(*LHandle) != 0)
        LResult = EOF;
    }
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return EOF;
  }
  return LResult;
}

// Both CRTs flush every open stream's written bytes at exit (ucrt's stdio
// termination, glibc's _IO_cleanup); an open handle's do the same. Only
// bytes still unflushed go to the IO (a handle with none never touches
// it). Armed on the first open (HookIODoAddHandle): a function-local static
// made then is destroyed before every static made earlier, so an IO
// registered before that open is still alive here (the registry is never
// destroyed). A Windows D handle still open is then closed and its entry
// removed: the OS deletes a D file when the ending process's handle closes.
// That handle stays known, so a later call on it fails as on a closed one
// (EBADF) instead of reaching the C runtime.
struct HookIODoExitFlush
{
  ~HookIODoExitFlush()
  {
    std::vector<HookIODoHandleRef> LGoing;

    try
    {
      for (const HookIODoHandleRef& LHandle : HookIODoOpenHandles())
      {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(*LHandle->StreamLock);
        if (LHandle->Closed)
          continue;
        HookIODoCrtFlushWrittenLocked(*LHandle);
        if (LHandle->Temporary)
        {
          LHandle->Closed = true;
          if (LHandle->Owned)
            ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOClose(LHandle->Stream);
          LHandle->Stream = nullptr;
          LGoing.push_back(LHandle);
        }
      }
      // Outside the stream locks: the removal runs the source
      for (const HookIODoHandleRef& LHandle : LGoing)
        HookIODoGiveBackEntry(*LHandle, true);
    }
    catch (...)
    {
      // Nothing can report a failure at exit
    }
  }
};

void HookIODoArmExitFlush()
{
  static HookIODoExitFlush LExitFlush;
}

// fgetc / getc: the byte as unsigned char, or EOF
bool HookIODoGetc(std::FILE* AFile, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = EOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    if (!HookIODoAnsiStream(AHandle))
      return;
    AResult = HookIODoGetLocked(AHandle);
  });
}

// fgets: up to ACount - 1 bytes, stopping after a newline, then a 0. nil when
// nothing was read before the end, on an error, or for ACount <= 0 (EINVAL).
bool HookIODoGets(char* AText, const int ACount, std::FILE* AFile, char*& AResult)
{
  AResult = nullptr;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    int LCount = 0;
    int LByte;
    // The error flag is sticky: only an error of this call fails it
    const bool LFailedBefore = AHandle.Failed;
    if ((AText == nullptr) || (ACount <= 0))
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return;
    }
    if (!HookIODoAnsiStream(AHandle))
      return;
    // One getc at a time: what ucrt's fgets does, and where glibc's line
    // reader leaves its FILE
    while (LCount < (ACount - 1))
    {
      LByte = HookIODoGetLocked(AHandle);
      if (LByte == EOF)
        break;
      AText[LCount] = static_cast<char>(LByte);
      ++LCount;
      if (LByte == '\n')
        break;
    }
    // Nothing read at the end, or an error on the way: C's fgets gives nil
    if ((AHandle.Failed && (!LFailedBefore)) || ((LCount == 0) && (ACount > 1)))
      return;
    AText[LCount] = '\0';
    AResult = AText;
  });
}

#if !defined(_WIN32)
// glibc's fortified names (declared by its headers only under
// _FORTIFY_SOURCE): the formatter the _chk printf hooks use for a handle, and
// what a failed size check calls, as glibc's own _chk functions do
extern "C" int __vsnprintf_chk(char* AText, std::size_t AMaxLength, int AFlag,
  std::size_t ATextLength, const char* AFormat, va_list AArgs) noexcept;
extern "C" [[noreturn]] void __chk_fail() noexcept;

// glibc's __fgets_chk / __fgets_unlocked_chk on a handle (AText holds
// ASize bytes): up to min(ACount - 1, ASize) bytes, the newline kept; nil for
// ACount <= 0, when nothing was read, or on an error of this call; a read
// that reached ASize bytes leaves no room for the NUL and fails the check
// (__chk_fail, called once the stream lock is released), as glibc's own does
bool HookIODoGetsChecked(char* AText, const std::size_t ASize, const int ACount,
  std::FILE* AFile, char*& AResult)
{
  bool LOverflow = false;
  bool LHandled;

  AResult = nullptr;
  LHandled = HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    std::size_t LLimit;
    std::size_t LCount = 0;
    int LByte;
    // The error flag is sticky: only an error of this call fails it
    const bool LFailedBefore = AHandle.Failed;
    if (ACount <= 0)
      return;
    LLimit = std::min(static_cast<std::size_t>(ACount) - 1, ASize);
    while (LCount < LLimit)
    {
      LByte = HookIODoGetLocked(AHandle);
      if (LByte == EOF)
        break;
      AText[LCount] = static_cast<char>(LByte);
      ++LCount;
      if (LByte == '\n')
        break;
    }
    if ((AHandle.Failed && (!LFailedBefore)) || (LCount == 0))
      return;
    if (LCount >= ASize)
    {
      LOverflow = true;
      return;
    }
    AText[LCount] = '\0';
    AResult = AText;
  });
  if (LOverflow)
    __chk_fail();
  return LHandled;
}

// glibc's __fread_chk / __fread_unlocked_chk checks, on the arguments alone
// (so they are the same for a real FILE): the byte count must fit a size_t
// and the caller's buffer of ABufferSize bytes, else __chk_fail
void HookIODoCheckRead(const std::size_t ABufferSize, const std::size_t ASize,
  const std::size_t ACount)
{
  const std::size_t LHalf = static_cast<std::size_t>(1) << (4 * sizeof(std::size_t));
  const std::size_t LBytes = ASize * ACount;

  // Only when either factor is large can the product wrap
  if (((ASize | ACount) >= LHalf) && (ASize != 0) && ((LBytes / ASize) != ACount))
    __chk_fail();
  if (LBytes > ABufferSize)
    __chk_fail();
}
#endif

// fputc / putc: the target CRT's byte write on its FILE model
// (HookIODoCrtPutLocked); the byte written as unsigned char, or EOF
bool HookIODoPutc(const int AChar, std::FILE* AFile, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = EOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    if (!HookIODoAnsiStream(AHandle))
      return;
    AResult = HookIODoCrtPutLocked(AHandle, AChar);
  });
}

#if !defined(_WIN32)
// The 128-byte stage of glibc's printf to a FILE
// (printf_buffer.h PRINTF_BUFFER_SIZE_TO_FILE_STAGE)
constexpr std::int64_t CHookIODoPrintStageSize = 128;

// How glibc's printf hands its text to a FILE (stdio-common
// printf_buffer_to_file.c), the stream byte-oriented already (HookIODoPrint
// checks that before it formats, as vfprintf's ORIENT): while the put area
// has room the text goes straight into it; once it is full, the next byte
// waits in a 1-byte stage and goes through __overflow when one more byte
// comes (or at the end); with no room at the start, the text gathers in a
// 128-byte stage that goes through _IO_sputn each time it is full (and at
// the end). After each hand-over the put area's room decides again. The
// text's length, or -1 when a hand-over failed.
std::int64_t HookIODoCrtPrintLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const unsigned char* AText,
  const std::int64_t ALength)
{
  enum class TStage
  {
    Direct,
    Stage,
    One
  };

  HookIODoCrtModel& LModel = AHandle.Crt;
  unsigned char LStage[CHookIODoPrintStageSize];
  std::int64_t LStageUsed = 0;
  std::int64_t LDone = 0;
  std::int64_t LTake;
  TStage LMode;

  // __printf_buffer_to_file_switch
  auto LSwitch = [&]()
  {
    LStageUsed = 0;
    LMode = (LModel.WritePtr < LModel.WriteEnd) ? TStage::Direct : TStage::Stage;
  };
  // __printf_buffer_flush_to_file: false when the hand-over failed
  auto LFlush = [&]() -> bool
  {
    if (LMode == TStage::Stage)
    {
      if (HookIODoCrtPutnLocked(AHandle, LStage, LStageUsed) != LStageUsed)
        return false;
      LSwitch();
      return true;
    }
    if (LMode == TStage::One)
    {
      if (LStageUsed == 1)
      {
        if (HookIODoCrtOverflowLocked(AHandle, LStage[0]) == EOF)
          return false;
        LSwitch();
      }
      return true;
    }
    // Direct: the bytes are in the put area already; a full one turns to
    // the 1-byte stage
    if (LModel.WritePtr == LModel.WriteEnd)
    {
      LMode = TStage::One;
      LStageUsed = 0;
    }
    return true;
  };

  LSwitch();
  while (LDone < ALength)
  {
    if ((LMode == TStage::Direct) && (LModel.WritePtr < LModel.WriteEnd))
    {
      LTake = LModel.WriteEnd - LModel.WritePtr;
      if (LTake > (ALength - LDone))
        LTake = ALength - LDone;
      std::memcpy(LModel.Buffer.data() + LModel.WritePtr, AText + LDone,
        static_cast<std::size_t>(LTake));
      LModel.WritePtr += LTake;
      LDone += LTake;
    }
    else if ((LMode == TStage::Stage) && (LStageUsed < CHookIODoPrintStageSize))
    {
      LTake = CHookIODoPrintStageSize - LStageUsed;
      if (LTake > (ALength - LDone))
        LTake = ALength - LDone;
      std::memcpy(LStage + LStageUsed, AText + LDone, static_cast<std::size_t>(LTake));
      LStageUsed += LTake;
      LDone += LTake;
    }
    else if ((LMode == TStage::One) && (LStageUsed == 0))
    {
      LStage[0] = AText[LDone];
      LStageUsed = 1;
      ++LDone;
    }
    else if (!LFlush())
      return -1;
  }
  if (!LFlush())
    return -1;
  return ALength;
}
#endif

// ALength bytes of formatted text, as the target CRT's printf hands them
// to a FILE: ucrt (and mingw's printf, through fputc) one byte at a time
// (HookIODoCrtPutLocked), stopping at the first that fails; glibc through
// HookIODoCrtPrintLocked. ALength or -1. The formatted writes end here.
bool HookIODoWriteText(std::FILE* AFile, const char* AText, const std::size_t ALength, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = -1;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    const unsigned char* LText = reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char*>(AText);
    if (ALength > static_cast<std::size_t>(INT_MAX))
    {
      AHandle.Failed = true;
      errno = EOVERFLOW;
      return;
    }
#if defined(_WIN32)
    for (std::size_t LI = 0; LI < ALength; ++LI)
    {
      if (HookIODoCrtPutLocked(AHandle, LText[LI]) == EOF)
        return;
    }
    AResult = static_cast<int>(ALength);
#else
    if (HookIODoCrtPrintLocked(AHandle, LText, static_cast<std::int64_t>(ALength)) >= 0)
      AResult = static_cast<int>(ALength);
#endif
  });
}

// The value fputs gives on success: the target CRT's own (ucrt 0, glibc 1),
// measured against the CRT on a real file by std_hookio's "text write" rows
#ifdef _WIN32
constexpr int HOOKIO_DO_PUTS_OK = 0;
#else
constexpr int HOOKIO_DO_PUTS_OK = 1;
#endif

// fputs: HOOKIO_DO_PUTS_OK, or EOF. ucrt's is an fwrite of the text
// (HookIODoCrtWriteLocked); glibc's orients the stream and is an
// _IO_sputn of it (HookIODoCrtPutnLocked).
bool HookIODoPuts(const char* AText, std::FILE* AFile, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = EOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    std::int64_t LLength;
    if (AText == nullptr)
    {
      // nil text on our handle: refused like the CRT's invalid parameter
      errno = EINVAL;
      return;
    }
    if (!HookIODoAnsiStream(AHandle))
      return;
    LLength = static_cast<std::int64_t>(std::strlen(AText));
#if !defined(_WIN32)
    // glibc's fputs on a wide stream writes nothing: EOF
    if (!HookIODoCrtNarrowLocked(AHandle))
      return;
#endif
    if (HookIODoWriteLocked(AHandle, reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char*>(AText), LLength)
      == LLength)
      AResult = HOOKIO_DO_PUTS_OK;
  });
}

// fputwc / putwc: one wide character through the target CRT's FILE model.
// Windows: ucrt's _fputwc_nolock (HookIODoCrtPutWideLocked; putwc is
// fputwc there). Linux: fputwc refuses a byte-oriented stream (WEOF; a
// fresh one turns wide), putwc checks nothing (_IO_putwc_unlocked, so on a
// byte-oriented stream the character goes through the byte overflow as its
// low byte), then HookIODoCrtPutWideLocked. The character, or WEOF.
bool HookIODoPutwc(const wchar_t AChar, std::FILE* AFile, const bool ACheck, wint_t& AResult)
{
  AResult = WEOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
#if !defined(_WIN32)
    if (ACheck && (HookIODoCrtFwideLocked(AHandle, 1) < 0))
      return;
#else
    (void)ACheck;
#endif
    AResult = HookIODoCrtPutWideLocked(AHandle, AChar);
  });
}

// fputws: Windows as ucrt's (fputws.cpp: each character through
// _fputwc_nolock, the first WEOF is EOF; 0 on success; nil text EINVAL).
// Linux as glibc's (iofputws.c): the stream must be (or turn) wide, then
// _IO_sputn of the text (HookIODoCrtWidePutnLocked) must take every
// character: 1, else EOF.
bool HookIODoPutws(const wchar_t* AText, std::FILE* AFile, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = EOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    if (AText == nullptr)
    {
      // nil text on our handle: refused like the CRT's invalid parameter
      errno = EINVAL;
      return;
    }
#if defined(_WIN32)
    for (const wchar_t* LCursor = AText; *LCursor != L'\0'; ++LCursor)
    {
      if (HookIODoCrtPutWideLocked(AHandle, *LCursor) == WEOF)
        return;
    }
    AResult = 0;
#else
    const std::int64_t LLength = static_cast<std::int64_t>(std::wcslen(AText));
    if (HookIODoCrtFwideLocked(AHandle, 1) != 1)
      return;
    if (HookIODoCrtWidePutnLocked(AHandle, AText, LLength) == LLength)
      AResult = 1;
#endif
  });
}

#if !defined(_WIN32)
// fwide: glibc's (fwide.c: _IO_fwide on the handle's model)
bool HookIODoFwide(std::FILE* AFile, const int AMode, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = 0;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    AResult = HookIODoCrtFwideLocked(AHandle, AMode);
  });
}
#endif

// ungetc: AChar put back by the target CRT's rules on its FILE model
// (HookIODoCrtUngetLocked: ucrt's buffer, glibc's get / backup area);
// AtEnd cleared on success; EOF is refused.
bool HookIODoUngetc(const int AChar, std::FILE* AFile, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = EOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    if (!HookIODoAnsiStream(AHandle))
      return;
    AResult = HookIODoCrtUngetLocked(AHandle, AChar);
  });
}

// fgetwc / getwc: one wide character through the target CRT's FILE model.
// Windows: ucrt's _fgetwc_nolock (getwc is fgetwc there). Linux: glibc's
// _IO_getwc_unlocked (__wuflow turns a fresh stream wide and refuses a
// byte-oriented one: WEOF, nothing flagged).
bool HookIODoGetwc(std::FILE* AFile, wint_t& AResult)
{
  AResult = WEOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
#if defined(_WIN32)
    AResult = HookIODoCrtGetWideLocked(AHandle);
#else
    AResult = HookIODoCrtWideGetLocked(AHandle);
#endif
  });
}

// fgetws: up to ACount - 1 wide characters, stopping after L'\n', then a 0.
// Windows as ucrt's (fgets.cpp common_fgets<wchar_t>): nil text with a
// count, or a negative count, EINVAL; 0 nil; each character by
// _fgetwc_nolock; nil only when nothing was read. Linux as glibc's
// (iofgetws.c): ACount <= 0 nil, 1 an empty string without reading; the
// line reader; nil when nothing was read or on an error of this call (the
// earlier error flag kept); nil text refused EINVAL.
bool HookIODoGetws(wchar_t* AText, const int ACount, std::FILE* AFile, wchar_t*& AResult)
{
  AResult = nullptr;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
#if defined(_WIN32)
    int LI;
    wint_t LChar;
    wchar_t* LCursor = AText;
    if (((AText == nullptr) && (ACount != 0)) || (ACount < 0))
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return;
    }
    if (ACount == 0)
      return;
    for (LI = 1; LI != ACount; ++LI)
    {
      LChar = HookIODoCrtGetWideLocked(AHandle);
      if (LChar == WEOF)
      {
        if (LCursor == AText)
          return;
        break;
      }
      *LCursor++ = static_cast<wchar_t>(LChar);
      if (static_cast<wchar_t>(LChar) == L'\n')
        break;
    }
    *LCursor = L'\0';
    AResult = AText;
#else
    std::int64_t LCount;
    bool LOldError;
    if (ACount <= 0)
      return;
    if (AText == nullptr)
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return;
    }
    if (ACount == 1)
    {
      AText[0] = L'\0';
      AResult = AText;
      return;
    }
    LOldError = AHandle.Failed;
    AHandle.Failed = false;
    LCount = HookIODoCrtWideLineLocked(AHandle, AText, ACount - 1);
    if ((LCount == 0) || (AHandle.Failed && (errno != EAGAIN)))
      AResult = nullptr;
    else
    {
      AText[LCount] = L'\0';
      AResult = AText;
    }
    AHandle.Failed = AHandle.Failed || LOldError;
#endif
  });
}

// ungetwc: AChar put back by the target CRT's rules (HookIODoCrtUngetWideLocked)
bool HookIODoUngetwc(const wint_t AChar, std::FILE* AFile, wint_t& AResult)
{
  AResult = WEOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    AResult = HookIODoCrtUngetWideLocked(AHandle, AChar);
  });
}

// setvbuf: the target CRT's own (HookIODoCrtSetvbufLocked): 0, or -1 / EOF
bool HookIODoSetvbuf(std::FILE* AFile, char* ABuffer, const int AMode, const std::size_t ASize,
  int& AResult)
{
  AResult = -1;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    AResult = HookIODoCrtSetvbufLocked(AHandle, ABuffer, AMode, ASize);
  });
}

// setbuf: the target CRT's own (HookIODoCrtSetbufLocked)
bool HookIODoSetbuf(std::FILE* AFile, char* ABuffer)
{
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    HookIODoCrtSetbufLocked(AHandle, ABuffer);
  });
}

// fileno / _fileno: a handle has no descriptor; -1 with EBADF
bool HookIODoFileno(std::FILE* AFile, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = -1;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle&)
  {
    errno = EBADF;
  });
}

// True for a HookIO handle: _lock_file and _unlock_file do nothing
// on one (each call takes the stream lock itself)
bool HookIODoOwns(std::FILE* AFile)
{
  return static_cast<bool>(HookIODoFindHandle(AFile));
}

// AFormat with AArgs as text; false on a format error (errno kept) or out of
// memory. AArgs is read through a copy, so the caller's list stays unread.
// Linux AFlag: -1 = a plain printf; otherwise the flag a fortified caller
// passed to __fprintf_chk / __vfprintf_chk, and the text is formatted by
// glibc's __vsnprintf_chk with it, so its format checks (%n in writable
// memory, ...) are exactly glibc's own.
#if defined(_WIN32)
bool HookIODoFormat(std::string& AResult, const unsigned __int64 AOptions,
  const char* AFormat, _locale_t ALocale, va_list AArgs)
#else
bool HookIODoFormat(std::string& AResult, const int AFlag, const char* AFormat, va_list AArgs)
#endif
{
  va_list LCopy;
  int LLength;

  // The length first, then the text into a buffer of that size
  va_copy(LCopy, AArgs);
#if defined(_WIN32)
  LLength = __stdio_common_vsprintf(AOptions | _CRT_INTERNAL_PRINTF_STANDARD_SNPRINTF_BEHAVIOR,
    nullptr, 0, AFormat, ALocale, LCopy);
#else
  if (AFlag < 0)
    LLength = std::vsnprintf(nullptr, 0, AFormat, LCopy);
  else
    LLength = __vsnprintf_chk(nullptr, 0, AFlag, 0, AFormat, LCopy);
#endif
  va_end(LCopy);
  if (LLength < 0)
    return false;
  try
  {
    AResult.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(LLength) + 1, '\0');
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
  va_copy(LCopy, AArgs);
#if defined(_WIN32)
  LLength = __stdio_common_vsprintf(AOptions | _CRT_INTERNAL_PRINTF_STANDARD_SNPRINTF_BEHAVIOR,
    AResult.data(), AResult.size(), AFormat, ALocale, LCopy);
#else
  if (AFlag < 0)
    LLength = std::vsnprintf(AResult.data(), AResult.size(), AFormat, LCopy);
  else
    LLength = __vsnprintf_chk(AResult.data(), AResult.size(), AFlag, AResult.size(), AFormat,
      LCopy);
#endif
  va_end(LCopy);
  if (LLength < 0)
    return false;
  AResult.resize(static_cast<std::size_t>(LLength));
  return true;
}

// A formatted write to a handle: the count, or -1 (format error, short write).
// Linux AFlag as HookIODoFormat's; glibc's vfprintf orients the stream
// before anything else (ORIENT): a wide stream is -1, nothing formatted or
// flagged.
#if defined(_WIN32)
bool HookIODoPrint(std::FILE* AFile, const unsigned __int64 AOptions, const char* AFormat,
  _locale_t ALocale, va_list AArgs, int& AResult)
#else
bool HookIODoPrint(std::FILE* AFile, const int AFlag, const char* AFormat, va_list AArgs,
  int& AResult)
#endif
{
  std::string LText;
#if !defined(_WIN32)
  bool LNarrow = false;
#endif

  AResult = -1;
  if (!HookIODoOwns(AFile))
    return false;
#if !defined(_WIN32)
  if (!HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle) { LNarrow = HookIODoCrtNarrowLocked(AHandle); }))
    return false;
  if (!LNarrow)
    return true;
#else
  // ucrt's output processor validates first (corecrt_internal_stdio_output.h
  // validate: _VALIDATE_STREAM_ANSI): -1, EINVAL, nothing formatted
  bool LAnsi = true;
  if (!HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle) { LAnsi = HookIODoAnsiStream(AHandle); }))
    return false;
  if (!LAnsi)
    return true;
#endif
#if defined(_WIN32)
  if (!HookIODoFormat(LText, AOptions, AFormat, ALocale, AArgs))
#else
  if (!HookIODoFormat(LText, AFlag, AFormat, AArgs))
#endif
  {
    // The handle still learns of the failure, as ferror would show it
    HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle) { AHandle.Failed = true; });
    return true;
  }
  return HookIODoWriteText(AFile, LText.data(), LText.size(), AResult);
}

// What a read can change on a handle: the scan's start, put back before the
// handle moves on (the re-read then leaves the FILE model exactly as the
// scan's own reads would have)
// CallerBytes: the caller's setvbuf array as it was (the model's copy holds
// only the view of it, and the stand-in's reads may refill it).
struct HookIODoReadState
{
  std::int64_t Position = 0;
  bool AtEnd = false;
  bool Failed = false;
  HookIODoCrtModel Crt;
  std::vector<unsigned char> CallerBytes;
};

HookIODoReadState HookIODoSaveReadState(const HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
  HookIODoReadState LState;
  const HookIODoCrtBuffer& LBuffer = AHandle.Crt.Buffer;

  LState.Position = AHandle.Position;
  LState.AtEnd = AHandle.AtEnd;
  LState.Failed = AHandle.Failed;
  LState.Crt = AHandle.Crt;
  if (LBuffer.External != nullptr)
    LState.CallerBytes.assign(LBuffer.External, LBuffer.External + LBuffer.Size);
  return LState;
}

// AStart put back on the handle, the caller's array bytes included
void HookIODoRestoreReadState(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const HookIODoReadState& AStart)
{
  AHandle.Position = AStart.Position;
  AHandle.AtEnd = AStart.AtEnd;
  AHandle.Failed = AStart.Failed;
  AHandle.Crt = AStart.Crt;
  if (AHandle.Crt.Buffer.External != nullptr)
    std::memcpy(AHandle.Crt.Buffer.External, AStart.CallerBytes.data(), AStart.CallerBytes.size());
}

// A scan on a handle runs the real scan over a stand-in FILE that holds the
// handle's next bytes, and the stand-in reads ahead of what the scan uses:
// its reads alone would leave the handle past the scan and its end flag set
// where a real FILE has none. Afterwards the handle goes back to where the
// scan started, with the end / error flags it had then, and moves on by
// exactly AUsed bytes (HookIODoScanReplay), then takes what the scan's last
// reads did (HookIODoScanFinish).
//
// The replay reads the bytes as the scan's own getc calls would
// (HookIODoCrtSkipLocked), so the FILE model ends as a real FILE's.
void HookIODoScanReplay(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const HookIODoReadState& AStart,
  const std::int64_t AUsed)
{
  HookIODoRestoreReadState(AHandle, AStart);
  HookIODoCrtSkipLocked(AHandle, AUsed);
}

// After the replay: ALookAhead, the scan read one byte past the ones it
// used and put it back (or met the end there); that read is made again and
// the byte put back by the model's ungetc, as the scan's getc / ungetc left
// a real FILE (a read that refilled the buffer or left glibc's backup area,
// an end met through a refill, AtEnd cleared by the ungetc). Linux: the
// stream is byte-oriented (glibc's scan orients it before anything else).
// Then the flags the stand-in showed: AEnd, the scan read past the last
// byte; AFailed, a read failed.
void HookIODoScanFinish(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const bool ALookAhead, const bool AEnd,
  const bool AFailed)
{
  int LByte;

#if !defined(_WIN32)
  AHandle.Crt.Orientation = -1;
#endif
  if (ALookAhead)
  {
    LByte = HookIODoCrtGetLocked(AHandle);
    if (LByte != EOF)
      HookIODoCrtUngetLocked(AHandle, LByte);
  }
  if (AEnd)
    AHandle.AtEnd = true;
  if (AFailed)
    AHandle.Failed = true;
}

// Whether the look-ahead decides anything: a byte taken from the get area
// and put back leaves the model as it was, unless the get area is empty
// (the get refills, or leaves glibc's backup area) or AtEnd is set (the
// ungetc clears it)
bool HookIODoScanLookAheadMatters(const HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  return (AHandle.Crt.Count == 0) || AHandle.AtEnd;
#else
  return (AHandle.Crt.ReadPtr == AHandle.Crt.ReadEnd) || AHandle.AtEnd;
#endif
}

// Replay and finish in one, for a caller that knows ALookAhead up front
void HookIODoScanSettle(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const HookIODoReadState& AStart,
  const std::int64_t AUsed, const bool ALookAhead, const bool AEnd, const bool AFailed)
{
  HookIODoScanReplay(AHandle, AStart, AUsed);
  HookIODoScanFinish(AHandle, ALookAhead, AEnd, AFailed);
}

#if !defined(_WIN32)

// fscanf on a handle (Linux): the stand-in is a fopencookie FILE that reads
// the handle; what the scan used is ftell of the cookie FILE, which counts its
// own read-ahead back. Bytes keeps what the cookie was given, for the
// look-ahead rerun (HookIODoScanLookedAhead).
struct HookIODoScan
{
  HookIODoHandle* Handle = nullptr;
  std::int64_t Delivered = 0;
  std::string Bytes;
  bool Failed = false;
};

// The cookie's read: the handle's next bytes through the model. A read that
// fails in this call (its own failure, not one the handle had before) is a
// failure when it delivered nothing; when it delivered bytes first (ungot
// ones ahead of a refused fill), those go now and the next call meets the
// failure again, as glibc's next __uflow would.
ssize_t HookIODoScanRead(void* ACookie, char* ABuffer, std::size_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoScan* LScan = static_cast<HookIODoScan*>(ACookie);
  const bool LFailedBefore = LScan->Handle->Failed;
  bool LFailedNow;
  std::int64_t LGot;

  LScan->Handle->Failed = false;
  LGot = HookIODoReadLocked(*LScan->Handle, reinterpret_cast<unsigned char*>(ABuffer),
    static_cast<std::int64_t>(ASize));
  LFailedNow = LScan->Handle->Failed;
  LScan->Handle->Failed = LFailedBefore || LFailedNow;
  LScan->Delivered += LGot;
  try
  {
    LScan->Bytes.append(ABuffer, static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot));
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    // Without them the rerun cannot run: the scan fails as a read did
    errno = ENOMEM;
    LScan->Failed = true;
    return -1;
  }
  if ((LGot == 0) && LFailedNow)
  {
    LScan->Failed = true;
    return -1;
  }
  return static_cast<ssize_t>(LGot);
}

// A cookie over fixed bytes: the look-ahead rerun's stand-in
struct HookIODoScanCut
{
  const char* Data = nullptr;
  std::int64_t Size = 0;
  std::int64_t Place = 0;
};

ssize_t HookIODoScanCutRead(void* ACookie, char* ABuffer, std::size_t ASize)
{
  HookIODoScanCut* LCut = static_cast<HookIODoScanCut*>(ACookie);
  std::int64_t LTake = LCut->Size - LCut->Place;

  if (LTake > static_cast<std::int64_t>(ASize))
    LTake = static_cast<std::int64_t>(ASize);
  std::memcpy(ABuffer, LCut->Data + LCut->Place, static_cast<std::size_t>(LTake));
  LCut->Place += LTake;
  return static_cast<ssize_t>(LTake);
}

// Only ftell's question: where the scan stands in what it was given
int HookIODoScanSeek(void* ACookie, off64_t* AOffset, int AOrigin)
{
  HookIODoScan* LScan = static_cast<HookIODoScan*>(ACookie);

  if ((AOrigin == SEEK_CUR) && (*AOffset == 0))
  {
    *AOffset = static_cast<off64_t>(LScan->Delivered);
    return 0;
  }
  errno = EINVAL;
  return -1;
}

using HookIODoScanFn = int (*)(std::FILE*, const char*, va_list);

// Whether a scan that used the first AUsed of ABytes read one more and put
// it back (its look-ahead): rerun over those bytes alone, it reads past
// them, and meets the end there, exactly when it read one more before (the
// scan's reads are a pure function of the bytes; glibc's conversions take
// the end and a byte they put back alike, so the arguments end as the
// first run wrote them). errno is kept. False when the cookie could not be
// made (the caller handles it as a failed read).
bool HookIODoScanLookedAhead(const std::string& ABytes, const std::int64_t AUsed,
  const HookIODoScanFn AScan, const char* AFormat, va_list AArgs, bool& ALooked)
{
  const int LErrno = errno;
  HookIODoScanCut LCut;
  cookie_io_functions_t LFunctions = {};
  std::FILE* LFile;
  va_list LArgs;

  ALooked = false;
  LCut.Data = ABytes.data();
  LCut.Size = AUsed;
  LFunctions.read = HookIODoScanCutRead;
  LFile = fopencookie(&LCut, "r", LFunctions);
  if (LFile == nullptr)
    return false;
  va_copy(LArgs, AArgs);
  AScan(LFile, AFormat, LArgs);
  va_end(LArgs);
  // These calls go through this unit's hooks: the cookie FILE is real
  ALooked = std::feof(LFile) != 0;
  std::fclose(LFile);
  errno = LErrno;
  return true;
}

// AScan (the real vfscanf) over AFile's handle; false: not a handle. The
// look-ahead (HookIODoScanFinish): a scan that met the cookie's end met the
// handle's; one that used every byte it was given read no further;
// otherwise it is found by the rerun, when it matters
// (HookIODoScanLookAheadMatters).
// A stream in put mode switches to get mode first, as the scan's first
// read would (__uflow): the snapshot then holds no unflushed bytes, which
// the replay would otherwise write a second time.
bool HookIODoScanHandle(std::FILE* AFile, const HookIODoScanFn AScan, const char* AFormat,
  va_list AArgs, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = EOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    // glibc's scan orients the stream before anything else (ORIENT: a wide
    // stream is EOF, nothing flagged), then refuses a write-only stream
    // (vfscanf-internal.c ARGCHECK: EBADF, EOF, no ferror, nothing
    // flushed, ungot bytes left alone)
    if (!HookIODoCrtNarrowLocked(AHandle))
      return;
    if (!HookIODoCanRead(AHandle))
    {
      errno = EBADF;
      return;
    }
    if (AHandle.Crt.Putting && (HookIODoCrtSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
      return;
    const HookIODoReadState LStart = HookIODoSaveReadState(AHandle);
    HookIODoScan LScan;
    cookie_io_functions_t LFunctions = {};
    std::FILE* LCookie;
    long LUsed;
    bool LEnd;
    bool LLookAhead;
    bool LFailed;
    va_list LArgs;

    LScan.Handle = &AHandle;
    LFunctions.read = HookIODoScanRead;
    LFunctions.seek = HookIODoScanSeek;
    LCookie = fopencookie(&LScan, "r", LFunctions);
    if (LCookie == nullptr)
    {
      errno = ENOMEM;
      return;
    }
    va_copy(LArgs, AArgs);
    AResult = AScan(LCookie, AFormat, LArgs);
    va_end(LArgs);
    // These calls go through this unit's hooks: the cookie FILE is real
    LUsed = std::ftell(LCookie);
    LEnd = std::feof(LCookie) != 0;
    std::fclose(LCookie);
    if (LUsed < 0)
      LUsed = static_cast<long>(LScan.Delivered);
    LFailed = LScan.Failed;
    HookIODoScanReplay(AHandle, LStart, static_cast<std::int64_t>(LUsed));
    LLookAhead = LEnd;
    if ((!LEnd) && (!LFailed) && (LUsed < LScan.Delivered)
      && HookIODoScanLookAheadMatters(AHandle))
    {
      if (!HookIODoScanLookedAhead(LScan.Bytes, static_cast<std::int64_t>(LUsed), AScan,
        AFormat, AArgs, LLookAhead))
        LFailed = true;
    }
    HookIODoScanFinish(AHandle, LLookAhead, LEnd, LFailed);
  });
}

#else

// The real scan: ucrt's __stdio_common_vfscanf
using HookIODoScanFn = int (*)(unsigned __int64, std::FILE*, const char*, _locale_t, va_list);

// Bytes copied into the stand-in before the first scan
constexpr std::int64_t CHookIODoScanWindow = 4096;

// Copies the handle's next bytes into AStandIn (at its end) until it holds
// AWindow of them or the handle has no more (AHandleEnd; AReadFailed when a
// read failed rather than reached the end). False when the stand-in refused
// a write (errno is the CRT's).
bool HookIODoScanFill(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, std::FILE* AStandIn, const std::int64_t AWindow,
  std::int64_t& ACopied, bool& AHandleEnd, bool& AReadFailed)
{
  unsigned char LScratch[512];
  std::int64_t LWant;
  std::int64_t LGot;
  bool LFailedBefore;

  if (std::fseek(AStandIn, 0, SEEK_END) != 0)
    return false;
  while ((ACopied < AWindow) && (!AHandleEnd))
  {
    LWant = AWindow - ACopied;
    if (LWant > static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(LScratch)))
      LWant = static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(LScratch));
    LFailedBefore = AHandle.Failed;
    LGot = HookIODoReadLocked(AHandle, LScratch, LWant);
    if ((LGot > 0) && (std::fwrite(LScratch, 1, static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot), AStandIn)
      != static_cast<std::size_t>(LGot)))
      return false;
    ACopied += LGot;
    if (LGot < LWant)
    {
      AHandleEnd = true;
      if (AHandle.Failed && (!LFailedBefore))
        AReadFailed = true;
    }
  }
  return true;
}

// Whether a scan that used AUsed of AStandIn's bytes read one more and put it
// back (its look-ahead). The scan's reads are a pure function of the bytes:
// over the same first AUsed bytes alone it makes the same reads, so it reads
// past them, and meets the end there, exactly when it read one more before.
// ucrt's conversions take the end and a byte they put back alike (neither
// is part of the field), so the arguments end as the first run wrote them.
// The rerun gets a stand-in of its own holding those bytes (AStandIn is
// left at an unknown place); errno is kept. False when a stand-in refused
// (errno is the refusing call's; the caller handles it as a failed read).
bool HookIODoScanLookedAhead(std::FILE* AStandIn, const std::int64_t AUsed,
  const HookIODoScanFn AScan, const unsigned __int64 AOptions, const char* AFormat,
  _locale_t ALocale, va_list AArgs, bool& ALooked)
{
  unsigned char LScratch[512];
  const int LErrno = errno;
  std::FILE* LCut;
  std::int64_t LLeft = AUsed;
  std::size_t LStep;
  bool LOk = true;
  va_list LArgs;

  ALooked = false;
  // These calls go through this unit's hooks: both stand-ins are real
  LCut = std::tmpfile();
  if (LCut == nullptr)
    return false;
  std::rewind(AStandIn);
  while (LOk && (LLeft > 0))
  {
    LStep = (LLeft < static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(LScratch)))
      ? static_cast<std::size_t>(LLeft) : sizeof(LScratch);
    LOk = (std::fread(LScratch, 1, LStep, AStandIn) == LStep)
      && (std::fwrite(LScratch, 1, LStep, LCut) == LStep);
    LLeft -= static_cast<std::int64_t>(LStep);
  }
  if (LOk)
  {
    std::rewind(LCut);
    va_copy(LArgs, AArgs);
    AScan(AOptions, LCut, AFormat, ALocale, LArgs);
    va_end(LArgs);
    ALooked = std::feof(LCut) != 0;
  }
  std::fclose(LCut);
  if (LOk)
    errno = LErrno;
  return LOk;
}

// fscanf on a handle (Windows): ucrt has no fopencookie, so the stand-in is a
// temporary FILE (std::tmpfile, deleted on close) holding the handle's next
// bytes. When the scan reads past the copied bytes while the handle has more,
// twice as many are copied and the scan runs again from the same start over
// the same arguments (va_copy): it never sees an end the handle does not
// have, and each argument ends as the last run wrote it (every run reads the
// same bytes up to where the earlier one stopped). What the scan used is
// _ftelli64 of the stand-in, which counts the scan's read-ahead back.
// false: not a handle.
// Written bytes the scan's first read would flush (HookIODoCrtLeaveWriteLocked,
// as fgetc's) are flushed first: the snapshot then holds none, which the
// replay would otherwise write a second time.
bool HookIODoScanHandle(std::FILE* AFile, const HookIODoScanFn AScan,
  const unsigned __int64 AOptions, const char* AFormat, _locale_t ALocale, va_list AArgs,
  int& AResult)
{
  AResult = EOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    // ucrt's input processor validates first (corecrt_internal_stdio_input.h
    // validate: _VALIDATE_STREAM_ANSI): EOF, EINVAL, nothing read
    if (!HookIODoAnsiStream(AHandle))
      return;
    if (!HookIODoCrtLeaveWriteLocked(AHandle, false))
      return;
    const HookIODoReadState LStart = HookIODoSaveReadState(AHandle);
    std::FILE* LStandIn;
    std::int64_t LWindow = CHookIODoScanWindow;
    std::int64_t LCopied = 0;
    std::int64_t LUsed = 0;
    bool LHandleEnd = false;
    bool LReadFailed = false;
    bool LEnd = false;
    bool LLookAhead;
    va_list LArgs;

    // ucrt's scan reads through _filbuf, which refuses a write-only stream
    // (it writes from its open) with ferror only, errno untouched
    if (!HookIODoCanRead(AHandle))
    {
      AHandle.Failed = true;
      return;
    }
    // These calls go through this unit's hooks: the stand-in FILE is real
    LStandIn = std::tmpfile();
    if (LStandIn == nullptr)
    {
      // errno is tmpfile's; the scan cannot run, as a read that failed
      AHandle.Failed = true;
      return;
    }
    for (;;)
    {
      if (!HookIODoScanFill(AHandle, LStandIn, LWindow, LCopied, LHandleEnd, LReadFailed))
      {
        // The stand-in refused the bytes: nothing was scanned, the handle
        // is back where it was with its error flag set
        std::fclose(LStandIn);
        AResult = EOF;
        HookIODoScanSettle(AHandle, LStart,
          0, false, false, true);
        return;
      }
      std::rewind(LStandIn);
      va_copy(LArgs, AArgs);
      AResult = AScan(AOptions, LStandIn, AFormat, ALocale, LArgs);
      va_end(LArgs);
      LEnd = std::feof(LStandIn) != 0;
      LUsed = _ftelli64(LStandIn);
      // Done unless the scan reached the copied bytes' end while the handle
      // has more
      if ((!LEnd) || LHandleEnd)
        break;
      LWindow *= 2;
    }
    if (LUsed < 0)
    {
      // Where the scan stopped is unknown: the handle stays at its start,
      // with its error flag set
      std::fclose(LStandIn);
      HookIODoScanSettle(AHandle, LStart,
        0, false, LEnd, true);
      return;
    }
    HookIODoScanReplay(AHandle, LStart, LUsed);
    // The look-ahead (HookIODoScanFinish): a scan that met the stand-in's end
    // met the handle's (the loop above); one that stopped at the copied
    // bytes' end read no further; otherwise it is found by the rerun, when
    // it matters (HookIODoScanLookAheadMatters).
    LLookAhead = LEnd;
    if ((!LEnd) && (LUsed < LCopied) && HookIODoScanLookAheadMatters(AHandle))
    {
      if (!HookIODoScanLookedAhead(LStandIn, LUsed, AScan, AOptions, AFormat, ALocale, AArgs,
        LLookAhead))
        LReadFailed = true;
    }
    std::fclose(LStandIn);
    HookIODoScanFinish(AHandle, LLookAhead, LEnd, LReadFailed);
  });
}

#endif

// One wide character through the target CRT's read on a handle
wint_t HookIODoWideGetAnyLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
{
#if defined(_WIN32)
  return HookIODoCrtGetWideLocked(AHandle);
#else
  return HookIODoCrtWideGetLocked(AHandle);
#endif
}

// AFormat with AArgs as wide text; false on a format error (errno kept) or
// out of memory. Windows: ucrt's own __stdio_common_vswprintf with the
// caller's options (so every conversion is ucrt's); Linux: vswprintf, its
// buffer doubled while the text does not fit. AArgs is read through copies.
#if defined(_WIN32)
bool HookIODoWideFormat(std::wstring& AResult, const unsigned __int64 AOptions,
  const wchar_t* AFormat, _locale_t ALocale, va_list AArgs)
#else
bool HookIODoWideFormat(std::wstring& AResult, const wchar_t* AFormat, va_list AArgs)
#endif
{
  va_list LCopy;
  int LLength;

#if defined(_WIN32)
  va_copy(LCopy, AArgs);
  LLength = __stdio_common_vswprintf(AOptions | _CRT_INTERNAL_PRINTF_STANDARD_SNPRINTF_BEHAVIOR,
    nullptr, 0, AFormat, ALocale, LCopy);
  va_end(LCopy);
  if (LLength < 0)
    return false;
  try
  {
    AResult.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(LLength) + 1, L'\0');
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return false;
  }
  va_copy(LCopy, AArgs);
  LLength = __stdio_common_vswprintf(AOptions | _CRT_INTERNAL_PRINTF_STANDARD_SNPRINTF_BEHAVIOR,
    AResult.data(), AResult.size(), AFormat, ALocale, LCopy);
  va_end(LCopy);
  if (LLength < 0)
    return false;
  AResult.resize(static_cast<std::size_t>(LLength));
  return true;
#else
  // glibc's vswprintf gives -1 both for a text that does not fit and for a
  // format error; the buffer grows to a large bound, past it the format is
  // the failure
  constexpr std::size_t CMax = static_cast<std::size_t>(1) << 26;
  std::size_t LSize = 256;
  const int LErrno = errno;

  for (;;)
  {
    try
    {
      AResult.assign(LSize, L'\0');
    }
    catch (...)
    {
      errno = ENOMEM;
      return false;
    }
    errno = 0;
    va_copy(LCopy, AArgs);
    LLength = std::vswprintf(AResult.data(), AResult.size(), AFormat, LCopy);
    va_end(LCopy);
    if (LLength >= 0)
    {
      errno = LErrno;
      AResult.resize(static_cast<std::size_t>(LLength));
      return true;
    }
    if ((errno == EILSEQ) || (LSize >= CMax))
      return false;
    LSize *= 2;
  }
#endif
}

// A wide formatted write to a handle: the count of wide characters, or -1.
// Windows as ucrt's vfwprintf: each character through _fputwc_nolock, the
// first failure -1. Linux as glibc's vfwprintf: the stream must be (or turn)
// wide (ORIENT: else -1, nothing formatted), then _IO_sputn of the text
// must take every character.
#if defined(_WIN32)
bool HookIODoWidePrint(std::FILE* AFile, const unsigned __int64 AOptions, const wchar_t* AFormat,
  _locale_t ALocale, va_list AArgs, int& AResult)
#else
bool HookIODoWidePrint(std::FILE* AFile, const wchar_t* AFormat, va_list AArgs, int& AResult)
#endif
{
  std::wstring LText;
  bool LWide = true;

  AResult = -1;
  if (!HookIODoOwns(AFile))
    return false;
#if !defined(_WIN32)
  if (!HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    LWide = HookIODoCrtFwideLocked(AHandle, 1) == 1;
  }))
    return false;
  if (!LWide)
    return true;
#endif
#if defined(_WIN32)
  if (!HookIODoWideFormat(LText, AOptions, AFormat, ALocale, AArgs))
#else
  if (!HookIODoWideFormat(LText, AFormat, AArgs))
#endif
  {
    HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle) { AHandle.Failed = true; });
    return true;
  }
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
#if defined(_WIN32)
    for (const wchar_t LChar : LText)
    {
      if (HookIODoCrtPutWideLocked(AHandle, LChar) == WEOF)
        return;
    }
    AResult = static_cast<int>(LText.size());
#else
    const std::int64_t LLength = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LText.size());
    if (HookIODoCrtWidePutnLocked(AHandle, LText.data(), LLength) == LLength)
      AResult = static_cast<int>(LLength);
#endif
  });
}

#if defined(_WIN32)
using HookIODoWideScanFn = int (*)(unsigned __int64, std::FILE*, const wchar_t*, _locale_t,
  va_list);
#else
using HookIODoWideScanFn = int (*)(std::FILE*, const wchar_t*, va_list);
#endif

// A wide scan's stand-in bytes: the handle's next wide characters as the
// real wide scan reads them back (Windows: each its 2 raw UTF-16 bytes,
// which ucrt's fgetwc reads from a binary stream; Linux: the current
// locale's bytes, which glibc's wide stream converts back), appended to
// AData. AOffsets[i] is the byte place of character i (one past the last at
// the end), so the scan's byte place maps back to a character count. False
// when out of memory.
bool HookIODoWideScanFill(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, std::string& AData, const std::int64_t AWindow,
  std::vector<std::int64_t>& AOffsets, bool& AHandleEnd, bool& AReadFailed)
{
  wint_t LChar;
  bool LFailedBefore;
#if !defined(_WIN32)
  char LBytes[MB_LEN_MAX];
  std::mbstate_t LState = {};
  std::size_t LSize;
#endif

  if (AOffsets.empty())
    AOffsets.push_back(0);
  while ((static_cast<std::int64_t>(AOffsets.size()) - 1 < AWindow) && (!AHandleEnd))
  {
    LFailedBefore = AHandle.Failed;
    LChar = HookIODoWideGetAnyLocked(AHandle);
    if (LChar == WEOF)
    {
      AHandleEnd = true;
      if (AHandle.Failed && (!LFailedBefore))
        AReadFailed = true;
      break;
    }
    try
    {
#if defined(_WIN32)
      const wchar_t LWide = static_cast<wchar_t>(LChar);
      AData.append(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&LWide), sizeof(LWide));
      AOffsets.push_back(AOffsets.back() + static_cast<std::int64_t>(sizeof(LWide)));
#else
      LSize = std::wcrtomb(LBytes, static_cast<wchar_t>(LChar), &LState);
      if (LSize == static_cast<std::size_t>(-1))
      {
        // A character the locale cannot write back cannot be scanned: the
        // window ends before it (the replay stops there too)
        AHandleEnd = true;
        break;
      }
      AData.append(LBytes, LSize);
      AOffsets.push_back(AOffsets.back() + static_cast<std::int64_t>(LSize));
#endif
    }
    catch (...)
    {
      return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}

// A fresh stand-in FILE holding ASize bytes of AData, at its start and not
// yet oriented: the real wide scan runs on it. Windows: a binary tmpfile
// (ucrt has no orientation). Linux: the bytes go to the descriptor, never
// through the FILE, because glibc's fwrite orients a stream byte-wise and
// fwide then cannot turn it wide (a byte stand-in fails every wide scan
// with EOF); the stream is then made wide. nullptr when it cannot be made.
std::FILE* HookIODoWideStandIn(const std::string& AData, const std::size_t ASize)
{
  std::FILE* LFile;

  // These calls go through this unit's hooks: the stand-in FILE is real
  LFile = std::tmpfile();
  if (LFile == nullptr)
    return nullptr;
#if defined(_WIN32)
  if ((ASize != 0) && (std::fwrite(AData.data(), 1, ASize, LFile) != ASize))
  {
    std::fclose(LFile);
    return nullptr;
  }
  std::fflush(LFile);
  std::rewind(LFile);
#else
  const int LDescriptor = ::fileno(LFile);
  std::size_t LDone = 0;
  while (LDone < ASize)
  {
    const ssize_t LWritten = ::write(LDescriptor, AData.data() + LDone, ASize - LDone);
    if (LWritten <= 0)
    {
      std::fclose(LFile);
      return nullptr;
    }
    LDone += static_cast<std::size_t>(LWritten);
  }
  if (::lseek(LDescriptor, 0, SEEK_SET) != 0)
  {
    std::fclose(LFile);
    return nullptr;
  }
  std::fwide(LFile, 1);
#endif
  return LFile;
}

// The character count a stand-in byte place stands for: the largest i with
// AOffsets[i] <= APlace
std::int64_t HookIODoWideScanChars(const std::vector<std::int64_t>& AOffsets,
  const std::int64_t APlace)
{
  std::int64_t LCount = 0;

  while ((LCount + 1 < static_cast<std::int64_t>(AOffsets.size())) &&
    (AOffsets[static_cast<std::size_t>(LCount + 1)] <= APlace))
    ++LCount;
  return LCount;
}

// ACount wide characters read as the scan's own getwc calls read them
void HookIODoWideSkipLocked(HookIODoHandle& AHandle, const std::int64_t ACount)
{
  std::int64_t LDone = 0;

  while ((LDone < ACount) && (HookIODoWideGetAnyLocked(AHandle) != WEOF))
    ++LDone;
}

// A wide scan on a handle (fwscanf / vfwscanf): the real wide scan over a
// stand-in holding the handle's next wide characters (HookIODoWideScanFill),
// the window doubled and the scan rerun while it reads past the copied
// characters and the handle has more. Afterwards the handle goes back to the
// scan's start and reads exactly the characters the scan used; one more
// read and put back when the scan looked past them (its last getwc /
// ungetwc), found by a rerun over exactly the used characters. Linux: the
// stream turns wide (a byte-oriented one: EOF, nothing flagged); a
// write-only stream is refused EBADF. false: not a handle.
bool HookIODoWideScanHandle(std::FILE* AFile, const HookIODoWideScanFn AScan,
#if defined(_WIN32)
  const unsigned __int64 AOptions, _locale_t ALocale,
#endif
  const wchar_t* AFormat, va_list AArgs, int& AResult)
{
  AResult = EOF;
  return HookIODoWith(AFile, [&](HookIODoHandle& AHandle)
  {
    constexpr std::int64_t CWindow = 2048;
    std::FILE* LStandIn;
    std::FILE* LCut;
    std::vector<std::int64_t> LOffsets;
    std::int64_t LWindow = CWindow;
    std::int64_t LPlace;
    std::int64_t LUsed;
    std::int64_t LCopied;
    bool LHandleEnd = false;
    bool LReadFailed = false;
    bool LEnd = false;
    bool LLookAhead;
    wint_t LChar;
    va_list LArgs;
    std::string LData;
    int LScanErrno = 0;

#if !defined(_WIN32)
    if (HookIODoCrtFwideLocked(AHandle, 1) != 1)
      return;
    if (!HookIODoCanRead(AHandle))
    {
      errno = EBADF;
      return;
    }
    if (AHandle.Crt.Putting && (HookIODoCrtWideSwitchToGetLocked(AHandle) == EOF))
      return;
#else
    if (!HookIODoCrtLeaveWriteLocked(AHandle, false))
      return;
    if (!HookIODoCanRead(AHandle))
    {
      AHandle.Failed = true;
      return;
    }
#endif
    const HookIODoReadState LStart = HookIODoSaveReadState(AHandle);
    for (;;)
    {
      if (!HookIODoWideScanFill(AHandle, LData, LWindow, LOffsets, LHandleEnd, LReadFailed))
      {
        HookIODoRestoreReadState(AHandle, LStart);
        AHandle.Failed = true;
        return;
      }
      // A fresh stand-in each run: a scan leaves its stream read and
      // oriented, and a rerun must start as the first one did
      LStandIn = HookIODoWideStandIn(LData, LData.size());
      if (LStandIn == nullptr)
      {
        HookIODoRestoreReadState(AHandle, LStart);
        AHandle.Failed = true;
        return;
      }
      va_copy(LArgs, AArgs);
#if defined(_WIN32)
      AResult = AScan(AOptions, LStandIn, AFormat, ALocale, LArgs);
#else
      AResult = AScan(LStandIn, AFormat, LArgs);
#endif
      va_end(LArgs);
      LEnd = std::feof(LStandIn) != 0;
      LPlace = std::ftell(LStandIn);
      LScanErrno = errno;
      std::fclose(LStandIn);
      errno = LScanErrno;
      if ((!LEnd) || LHandleEnd)
        break;
      LWindow *= 2;
    }
    LCopied = static_cast<std::int64_t>(LOffsets.size()) - 1;
    LUsed = (LPlace < 0) ? LCopied : HookIODoWideScanChars(LOffsets, LPlace);
    HookIODoRestoreReadState(AHandle, LStart);
    HookIODoWideSkipLocked(AHandle, LUsed);
    // The look-ahead: a rerun over exactly the used characters meets their
    // end exactly when the scan read one more and put it back
    LLookAhead = LEnd;
    if ((!LEnd) && (LUsed < LCopied))
    {
      LCut = HookIODoWideStandIn(LData,
        static_cast<std::size_t>(LOffsets[static_cast<std::size_t>(LUsed)]));
      if (LCut == nullptr)
        LReadFailed = true;
      else
      {
        va_copy(LArgs, AArgs);
#if defined(_WIN32)
        AScan(AOptions, LCut, AFormat, ALocale, LArgs);
#else
        AScan(LCut, AFormat, LArgs);
#endif
        va_end(LArgs);
        LLookAhead = std::feof(LCut) != 0;
        std::fclose(LCut);
      }
      errno = LScanErrno;
    }
    if (LLookAhead)
    {
      LChar = HookIODoWideGetAnyLocked(AHandle);
      if (LChar != WEOF)
        HookIODoCrtUngetWideLocked(AHandle, LChar);
    }
    if (LEnd)
      AHandle.AtEnd = true;
    if (LReadFailed)
      AHandle.Failed = true;
  });
}

// Registers one stream under the next prefix number; "" when both are nil or
// out of memory. The prefix text is built before the entry is added, so a
// failure registers nothing.
std::string HookIODoRegister(const HookIODoIO AStream, const HookIODoSource ASource)
{
  try
  {
    HookIODoEntry LEntry;
    if ((AStream == nullptr) && (ASource == nullptr))
      return std::string();
    LEntry.Stream = AStream;
    LEntry.Source = ASource;
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
    if (AStream != nullptr)
      LEntry.StreamLock = HookIODoStreamLockOf(AStream);
    const std::uint64_t LId = HookIODoLastId + 1;
    std::string LPrefix = std::string(CHookIODoScheme) + std::to_string(LId);
    HookIODoEntries().emplace(LId, LEntry);
    HookIODoLastId = LId;
    return LPrefix;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    return std::string();
  }
}

// Removes a registered prefix (exactly `io://<n>`); false when it is not one
bool HookIODoUnregister(const std::string& APrefix)
{
  std::uint64_t LId;
  const char* LRest;

  if (!HookIODoParse(APrefix.c_str(), LId, LRest))
    return false;
  if ((LId == 0) || (*LRest != '\0'))
    return false;
  try
  {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
    return HookIODoEntries().erase(LId) == 1;
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    return false;
  }
}

// Makes ASource the path source (nil: none). The source is registered under
// a prefix of its own first (false, nothing changed, when that fails); the
// one it replaces is unregistered after the swap, so a lookup meanwhile sees
// either source, never neither by mistake.
bool HookIODoSetPathSource(const HookIODoSource ASource)
{
  std::uint64_t LNewId = 0;
  std::uint64_t LOldId;

  if (ASource != nullptr)
  {
    const std::string LPrefix(HookIODoRegister(nullptr, ASource));
    const char* LRest;
    if (LPrefix.empty() || (!HookIODoParse(LPrefix.c_str(), LNewId, LRest)) || (LNewId == 0))
      return false;
  }
  LOldId = HookIODoPathSourceId.exchange(LNewId);
  if (LOldId != 0)
  {
    try
    {
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
      HookIODoEntries().erase(LOldId);
    }
    catch (...)
    {
      // Only the lock can throw; the old entry stays unreachable
    }
  }
  return true;
}

// Unsets the path source only while it is still ASource (another set since
// is left as it is); true when it was unset. A compare-and-swap on the
// prefix number, so a concurrent set is never lost.
bool HookIODoResetPathSourceIf(const HookIODoSource ASource)
{
  for (;;)
  {
    std::uint64_t LId = HookIODoPathSourceId.load();
    HookIODoEntry LEntry;
    if ((LId == 0) || (ASource == nullptr))
      return false;
    if ((!HookIODoFind(LId, LEntry)) || (LEntry.Source != ASource))
      return false;
    if (HookIODoPathSourceId.compare_exchange_strong(LId, 0))
    {
      try
      {
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
        HookIODoEntries().erase(LId);
      }
      catch (...)
      {
        // Only the lock can throw; the old entry stays unreachable
      }
      return true;
    }
  }
}

// Makes ASource this thread's own path source (nil: none, the program's
// applies again). Registered under a prefix of its own first (false, nothing
// changed, when that fails); the one it replaces is unregistered after. Only
// this thread reads HookIODoThreadPathSourceId, so the swap needs no atomic.
bool HookIODoSetThreadPathSource(const HookIODoSource ASource)
{
  std::uint64_t LNewId = 0;
  std::uint64_t LOldId;

  if (ASource != nullptr)
  {
    const std::string LPrefix(HookIODoRegister(nullptr, ASource));
    const char* LRest;
    if (LPrefix.empty() || (!HookIODoParse(LPrefix.c_str(), LNewId, LRest)) || (LNewId == 0))
      return false;
  }
  LOldId = HookIODoThreadPathSourceId;
  HookIODoThreadPathSourceId = LNewId;
  if (LOldId != 0)
  {
    try
    {
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(HookIODoLock());
      HookIODoEntries().erase(LOldId);
    }
    catch (...)
    {
      // Only the lock can throw; the old entry stays unreachable
    }
  }
  return true;
}

// The source this thread's own path source was set from (nil: none set)
HookIODoSource HookIODoThreadPathSource()
{
  HookIODoEntry LEntry;

  if (HookIODoThreadPathSourceId == 0)
    return nullptr;
  if (!HookIODoFind(HookIODoThreadPathSourceId, LEntry))
    return nullptr;
  return LEntry.Source;
}

}

// For raylib_ext (a unit above HookIO): SetRaylibIOSource(nil) unsets only
// the path source it set itself, never one the program set directly
namespace pcpp_hookio_internal {

bool ResetPathSourceIf(const ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSource ASource) noexcept
{
  return HookIODoResetPathSourceIf(ASource);
}

}

namespace {

#if defined(_WIN32)

constexpr wchar_t CHookIODoWideScheme[] = L"io://";

// True when APath is an io:// path, after every leading "./" or ".\" (as
// HookIODoSkipCurrentFolder for a narrow path)
bool HookIODoWideIsVirtual(const wchar_t* APath)
{
  const wchar_t* LCursor = APath;

  if (APath == nullptr)
    return false;
  while ((LCursor[0] == L'.') && ((LCursor[1] == L'/') || (LCursor[1] == L'\\')))
    LCursor += 2;
  return std::wcsncmp(LCursor, CHookIODoWideScheme, CHookIODoSchemeLength) == 0;
}

// AText (UTF-16) as UTF-8 into AResult; false when it does not convert
bool HookIODoNarrow(const wchar_t* AText, std::string& AResult)
{
  int LCount;

  if (AText == nullptr)
    return false;
  LCount = WideCharToMultiByte(CP_UTF8, WC_ERR_INVALID_CHARS, AText, -1,
    nullptr, 0, nullptr, nullptr);
  if (LCount <= 0)
    return false;
  AResult.resize(static_cast<std::size_t>(LCount));
  LCount = WideCharToMultiByte(CP_UTF8, WC_ERR_INVALID_CHARS, AText, -1,
    AResult.data(), LCount, nullptr, nullptr);
  if (LCount <= 0)
    return false;
  // Drop the terminator the conversion wrote
  AResult.resize(static_cast<std::size_t>(LCount - 1));
  return true;
}

// A hooked _wfopen: as HookIODoOpen after converting to UTF-8. Only a path
// that starts with io:// (after any leading "./" or ".\") is converted, or
// any path while the path source is active (else a real path costs no
// allocation); an io:// path that does not convert is a missing file
// (ENOENT), such a mode is refused (EINVAL). A plain path or mode that does
// not convert goes to the C runtime.
bool HookIODoOpenWide(const wchar_t* APath, const wchar_t* AMode, std::FILE*& AResult)
{
  AResult = nullptr;
  if (APath == nullptr)
    return false;
  if (!HookIODoWideIsVirtual(APath))
  {
    if (!HookIODoPathSourceActive())
      return false;
    try
    {
      std::string LPath;
      std::string LMode;
      if ((!HookIODoNarrow(APath, LPath)) || (!HookIODoNarrow(AMode, LMode)))
        return false;
      return HookIODoOpen(LPath.c_str(), LMode.c_str(), AResult);
    }
    catch (...)
    {
      return false;
    }
  }
  try
  {
    std::string LPath;
    std::string LMode;
    if (!HookIODoNarrow(APath, LPath))
    {
      errno = ENOENT;
      return true;
    }
    if (!HookIODoNarrow(AMode, LMode))
    {
      errno = EINVAL;
      return true;
    }
    return HookIODoOpen(LPath.c_str(), LMode.c_str(), AResult);
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return true;
  }
}

#endif

// The query family (access, stat, GetFileAttributesA) answers a virtual path
// as fopen would find it. False: not a virtual path, the caller passes it to
// the C runtime. True: answered; AFound = the file exists (else errno
// ENOENT, or ENOMEM), ASize = its size (0 when the IO cannot tell), and
// AWritable = a write open that empties nothing ("r+") would succeed: always
// on a registered IO (HookIODoOpenShared opens it in every mode), on a source entry
// when IOSourceOpen gives it in ReadWrite (opened and closed at once). Under
// a registered IO's prefix every name is that IO; a source entry exists when
// IOSourceExists says so. Directories are not answered: CustomIO has no
// directory query, and a source's root is a missing file, as opendir finds
// it. The registry lock is never held while CustomIO runs.
bool HookIODoQuery(const char* APath, bool& AFound, std::int64_t& ASize, bool& AWritable)
{
  std::uint64_t LId;
  const char* LRest;
  HookIODoEntry LEntry;
  HookIODoIO LStream;
  std::string LMapped;

  AFound = false;
  ASize = 0;
  AWritable = false;
  if (!HookIODoResolve(APath, LId, LRest, LMapped))
    return false;
  // The query's own work (the source's real files) never maps a plain path
  HookIODoPathGuard LPathGuard;
  if ((LId == 0) || (!HookIODoFind(LId, LEntry)))
  {
    errno = ENOENT;
    return true;
  }
  try
  {
    if (LEntry.Stream != nullptr)
    {
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> LGuard(*LEntry.StreamLock);
      ASize = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSize(LEntry.Stream);
      AWritable = true;
    }
    else
    {
      const std::string LName(HookIODoEntryName(LRest));
      if (!::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceExists(LEntry.Source, LName))
      {
        errno = ENOENT;
        return true;
      }
      ASize = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceSize(LEntry.Source, LName);
      LStream = ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOSourceOpen(LEntry.Source, LName, HookIODoMode::ReadWrite);
      if (LStream != nullptr)
      {
        AWritable = true;
        ::pcpp_m_CustomIO::IOClose(LStream);
      }
    }
  }
  catch (...)
  {
    errno = ENOMEM;
    return true;
  }
  if (ASize < 0)
    ASize = 0;
  AFound = true;
  return true;
}

// access (Linux, Windows' oldnames access) / _access on a virtual path: 0, or
// -1 with errno. AMode: Linux F_OK or R_OK / W_OK / X_OK bits, Windows 0, 2,
// 4 or 6; any other bit is EINVAL, checked before the path as the C runtime
// does. An IO is never executable (X_OK: EACCES); W_OK needs AWritable.
bool HookIODoAccess(const char* APath, const int AMode, int& AResult)
{
  std::uint64_t LId;
  const char* LRest;
  bool LFound;
  std::int64_t LSize;
  bool LWritable;
#if defined(_WIN32)
  const int LValid = 6;
  const int LWriteBit = 2;
  const int LExecuteBit = 0;
#else
  const int LValid = R_OK | W_OK | X_OK;
  const int LWriteBit = W_OK;
  const int LExecuteBit = X_OK;
#endif
  std::string LMapped;

  AResult = -1;
  if (!HookIODoResolve(APath, LId, LRest, LMapped))
    return false;
  if ((AMode & (~LValid)) != 0)
  {
    errno = EINVAL;
    return true;
  }
  // A path source entry removed between the two lookups: missing, as above
  if (!HookIODoQuery(APath, LFound, LSize, LWritable))
    errno = ENOENT;
  if (!LFound)
    return true;
  if (((AMode & LExecuteBit) != 0) || (((AMode & LWriteBit) != 0) && (!LWritable)))
  {
    errno = EACCES;
    return true;
  }
  AResult = 0;
  return true;
}

// stat (Linux) / stat64i32 (Windows) on a virtual path: 0 with ABuf filled,
// or -1 with errno. A regular file, read for everyone, write as AWritable
// (Windows: the owner bits copied to group and other, as ucrt's stat does),
// one link, its size, no times (an IO has none: 0). Linux: owned by this
// process's user and group. Windows: a size past what the 32-bit st_size
// holds is -1 with EOVERFLOW, as ucrt's _stat64i32 gives. Linux TStat:
// struct stat or struct stat64 (the plain stat symbol and stat64).
#if defined(_WIN32)
bool HookIODoStat(const char* APath, struct _stat64i32* ABuf, int& AResult)
#else
template <typename TStat>
bool HookIODoStat(const char* APath, TStat* ABuf, int& AResult)
#endif
{
  bool LFound;
  std::int64_t LSize;
  bool LWritable;

  AResult = -1;
  if (!HookIODoQuery(APath, LFound, LSize, LWritable))
    return false;
  if (!LFound)
    return true;
  if (ABuf == nullptr)
  {
#if defined(_WIN32)
    errno = EINVAL;
#else
    errno = EFAULT;
#endif
    return true;
  }
#if defined(_WIN32)
  if (LSize > static_cast<std::int64_t>(LONG_MAX))
  {
    errno = EOVERFLOW;
    return true;
  }
  std::memset(ABuf, 0, sizeof(*ABuf));
  ABuf->st_mode = static_cast<unsigned short>(_S_IFREG | _S_IREAD);
  if (LWritable)
    ABuf->st_mode = static_cast<unsigned short>(ABuf->st_mode | _S_IWRITE);
  // ucrt's stat: the owner's bits (0x01C0, octal 700) copied to group and
  // other
  ABuf->st_mode = static_cast<unsigned short>(ABuf->st_mode | ((ABuf->st_mode & 0x01C0) >> 3) |
    ((ABuf->st_mode & 0x01C0) >> 6));
  ABuf->st_nlink = 1;
  ABuf->st_size = static_cast<_off_t>(LSize);
#else
  std::memset(ABuf, 0, sizeof(*ABuf));
  ABuf->st_mode = S_IFREG | S_IRUSR | S_IRGRP | S_IROTH;
  if (LWritable)
    ABuf->st_mode = ABuf->st_mode | S_IWUSR;
  ABuf->st_nlink = 1;
  ABuf->st_uid = getuid();
  ABuf->st_gid = getgid();
  ABuf->st_size = static_cast<decltype(ABuf->st_size)>(LSize);
  ABuf->st_blksize = CHookIODoBlockSize;
  ABuf->st_blocks = static_cast<decltype(ABuf->st_blocks)>((LSize + 511) / 512);
#endif
  AResult = 0;
  return true;
}

#if defined(_WIN32)
// GetFileAttributesA on a virtual path: FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL, or
// FILE_ATTRIBUTE_READONLY when not AWritable; a missing one gives
// INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES with ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND. errno is left as it was
// (the Win32 call reports through GetLastError only).
bool HookIODoAttributes(const char* APath, DWORD& AResult)
{
  const int LSavedErrno = errno;
  bool LFound;
  std::int64_t LSize;
  bool LWritable;

  AResult = INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES;
  if (!HookIODoQuery(APath, LFound, LSize, LWritable))
    return false;
  errno = LSavedErrno;
  if (!LFound)
  {
    SetLastError(ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND);
    return true;
  }
  if (LWritable)
    AResult = FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL;
  else
    AResult = FILE_ATTRIBUTE_READONLY;
  return true;
}
#endif

// Each C++ hook's slot for its real function (HookReal fills it once)
void* GHookIODoRealVfprintf = nullptr;
void* GHookIODoRealVfscanf = nullptr;
void* GHookIODoRealIsoVfscanf = nullptr;
void* GHookIODoRealVfprintfChk = nullptr;
void* GHookIODoRealFgetsChk = nullptr;
void* GHookIODoRealFgetsUnlockedChk = nullptr;
void* GHookIODoRealFreadChk = nullptr;
void* GHookIODoRealFreadUnlockedChk = nullptr;
void* GHookIODoRealXstat = nullptr;
void* GHookIODoRealXstat64 = nullptr;

} // namespace

// The variadic and va_list hooks, in C++: a clink variadic routine has no
// va_list to pass on (BNF sec 6). Same contract as the PaskalCPP hooks below:
// a HookIO handle is answered here, anything else goes to the real function,
// and with no real function the call fails as the function fails (errno
// ENOSYS). Outside the unnamed namespace: C linkage needs external linkage.
#pragma clang diagnostic push
#pragma clang diagnostic ignored "-Winconsistent-dllimport"

#if defined(_WIN32)

// What ucrt's fprintf and the headers' inline vfprintf / printf family call
extern "C" int __stdio_common_vfprintf(unsigned __int64 AOptions, FILE* AFile,
  const char* AFormat, _locale_t ALocale, va_list AArgs)
{
  using TReal = int (*)(unsigned __int64, FILE*, const char*, _locale_t, va_list);
  TReal LReal;
  int LResult;

  if (HookIODoPrint(AFile, AOptions, AFormat, ALocale, AArgs, LResult))
    return LResult;
  LReal = reinterpret_cast<TReal>(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookReal(GHookIODoRealVfprintf,
    "__stdio_common_vfprintf"));
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return -1;
  }
  return LReal(AOptions, AFile, AFormat, ALocale, AArgs);
}
HOOKABI_IMPORT_SLOT(__stdio_common_vfprintf);

// What ucrt's fscanf / vfscanf and the headers' inline scan forms (fscanf_s,
// _fscanf_l, ...) call: a handle is scanned by the real function over a
// stand-in FILE, a real FILE by the real function directly
extern "C" int __stdio_common_vfscanf(unsigned __int64 AOptions, FILE* AFile,
  const char* AFormat, _locale_t ALocale, va_list AArgs)
{
  HookIODoScanFn LReal;
  int LResult;

  LReal = reinterpret_cast<HookIODoScanFn>(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookReal(GHookIODoRealVfscanf,
    "__stdio_common_vfscanf"));
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return EOF;
  }
  if (HookIODoScanHandle(AFile, LReal, AOptions, AFormat, ALocale, AArgs, LResult))
    return LResult;
  return LReal(AOptions, AFile, AFormat, ALocale, AArgs);
}
HOOKABI_IMPORT_SLOT(__stdio_common_vfscanf);

// mingw's own printf (libmingw32's mingw_fprintf.obj holds only this name, so
// this replaces that object whole). A real FILE goes to __mingw_vfprintf.
extern "C" int __mingw_fprintf(FILE* AFile, const char* AFormat, ...)
{
  va_list LArgs;
  va_list LCopy;
  int LLength;
  int LResult = -1;
  std::string LText;

  va_start(LArgs, AFormat);
  if (HookIODoOwns(AFile))
  {
    va_copy(LCopy, LArgs);
    LLength = __mingw_vsnprintf(nullptr, 0, AFormat, LCopy);
    va_end(LCopy);
    if (LLength >= 0)
    {
      try
      {
        LText.assign(static_cast<std::size_t>(LLength) + 1, '\0');
        va_copy(LCopy, LArgs);
        LLength = __mingw_vsnprintf(LText.data(), LText.size(), AFormat, LCopy);
        va_end(LCopy);
      }
      catch (...)
      {
        errno = ENOMEM;
        LLength = -1;
      }
    }
    if (LLength >= 0)
      HookIODoWriteText(AFile, LText.data(), static_cast<std::size_t>(LLength), LResult);
  }
  else
    LResult = __mingw_vfprintf(AFile, AFormat, LArgs);
  va_end(LArgs);
  return LResult;
}

#else

extern "C" int vfprintf(FILE* AFile, const char* AFormat, va_list AArgs)
{
  using TReal = int (*)(FILE*, const char*, va_list);
  TReal LReal;
  int LResult;

  if (HookIODoPrint(AFile, -1, AFormat, AArgs, LResult))
    return LResult;
  LReal = reinterpret_cast<TReal>(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookReal(GHookIODoRealVfprintf, "vfprintf"));
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return -1;
  }
  return LReal(AFile, AFormat, AArgs);
}

// glibc's fortified names, what C built with -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE calls in
// place of fprintf / vfprintf / fgets / fread and their _unlocked forms. On a
// handle each applies glibc's own check, then the handle's plain path (a
// handle has no CRT lock, so the _unlocked forms are the same); a real FILE
// goes to glibc's own _chk function.
extern "C" int __vfprintf_chk(FILE* AFile, int AFlag, const char* AFormat, va_list AArgs)
{
  using TReal = int (*)(FILE*, int, const char*, va_list);
  TReal LReal;
  int LResult;

  if (HookIODoPrint(AFile, AFlag, AFormat, AArgs, LResult))
    return LResult;
  LReal = reinterpret_cast<TReal>(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookReal(GHookIODoRealVfprintfChk,
    "__vfprintf_chk"));
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return -1;
  }
  return LReal(AFile, AFlag, AFormat, AArgs);
}

extern "C" int __fprintf_chk(FILE* AFile, int AFlag, const char* AFormat, ...)
{
  va_list LArgs;
  int LResult;

  va_start(LArgs, AFormat);
  LResult = __vfprintf_chk(AFile, AFlag, AFormat, LArgs);
  va_end(LArgs);
  return LResult;
}

// __fgets_chk and __fgets_unlocked_chk: AName / ASlot = the real one
static char* HookIODoGetsChk(char* AText, std::size_t ASize, int ACount, FILE* AFile,
  void*& ASlot, const char* AName)
{
  using TReal = char* (*)(char*, std::size_t, int, FILE*);
  TReal LReal;
  char* LResult;

  if (HookIODoGetsChecked(AText, ASize, ACount, AFile, LResult))
    return LResult;
  LReal = reinterpret_cast<TReal>(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookReal(ASlot, AName));
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return nullptr;
  }
  return LReal(AText, ASize, ACount, AFile);
}

extern "C" char* __fgets_chk(char* AText, std::size_t ASize, int ACount, FILE* AFile)
{
  return HookIODoGetsChk(AText, ASize, ACount, AFile, GHookIODoRealFgetsChk, "__fgets_chk");
}

extern "C" char* __fgets_unlocked_chk(char* AText, std::size_t ASize, int ACount, FILE* AFile)
{
  return HookIODoGetsChk(AText, ASize, ACount, AFile, GHookIODoRealFgetsUnlockedChk,
    "__fgets_unlocked_chk");
}

// __fread_chk and __fread_unlocked_chk: glibc's checks first (they read the
// arguments only), then the handle's fread or the real one
static std::size_t HookIODoReadChk(void* ABuffer, std::size_t ABufferSize, std::size_t ASize,
  std::size_t ACount, FILE* AFile, void*& ASlot, const char* AName)
{
  using TReal = std::size_t (*)(void*, std::size_t, std::size_t, std::size_t, FILE*);
  TReal LReal;
  std::size_t LResult;

  HookIODoCheckRead(ABufferSize, ASize, ACount);
  if (HookIODoRead(ABuffer, ASize, ACount, AFile, LResult))
    return LResult;
  LReal = reinterpret_cast<TReal>(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookReal(ASlot, AName));
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return 0;
  }
  return LReal(ABuffer, ABufferSize, ASize, ACount, AFile);
}

extern "C" std::size_t __fread_chk(void* ABuffer, std::size_t ABufferSize, std::size_t ASize,
  std::size_t ACount, FILE* AFile)
{
  return HookIODoReadChk(ABuffer, ABufferSize, ASize, ACount, AFile, GHookIODoRealFreadChk,
    "__fread_chk");
}

extern "C" std::size_t __fread_unlocked_chk(void* ABuffer, std::size_t ABufferSize,
  std::size_t ASize, std::size_t ACount, FILE* AFile)
{
  return HookIODoReadChk(ABuffer, ABufferSize, ASize, ACount, AFile,
    GHookIODoRealFreadUnlockedChk, "__fread_unlocked_chk");
}

// fscanf and the C99 name C callers bind to: a handle is scanned by the real
// vfscanf (ASlot / AName) over a cookie FILE, a real FILE by the same
// function directly. static: a helper, not a C runtime name.
static int HookIODoVscan(FILE* AFile, void*& ASlot, const char* AName, const char* AFormat,
  va_list AArgs)
{
  HookIODoScanFn LReal;
  int LResult;

  LReal = reinterpret_cast<HookIODoScanFn>(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookReal(ASlot, AName));
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return EOF;
  }
  if (HookIODoScanHandle(AFile, LReal, AFormat, AArgs, LResult))
    return LResult;
  return LReal(AFile, AFormat, AArgs);
}

// The plain symbol fscanf, for callers built without the headers' redirect.
// glibc's headers name the C++ fscanf __isoc99_fscanf (asm label), so this
// definition takes the symbol by an asm label of its own.
extern "C" int HookIODoPlainFscanf(FILE* AFile, const char* AFormat, ...) __asm__("fscanf");

extern "C" int HookIODoPlainFscanf(FILE* AFile, const char* AFormat, ...)
{
  va_list LArgs;
  int LResult;

  va_start(LArgs, AFormat);
  LResult = HookIODoVscan(AFile, GHookIODoRealVfscanf, "vfscanf", AFormat, LArgs);
  va_end(LArgs);
  return LResult;
}

// The C99 name, what the headers make of fscanf
extern "C" int __isoc99_fscanf(FILE* AFile, const char* AFormat, ...)
{
  va_list LArgs;
  int LResult;

  va_start(LArgs, AFormat);
  LResult = HookIODoVscan(AFile, GHookIODoRealIsoVfscanf, "__isoc99_vfscanf", AFormat, LArgs);
  va_end(LArgs);
  return LResult;
}

// vfscanf by its plain symbol (asm label, as fscanf above) and by the C99
// name the headers make of it: the same scans over the caller's va_list
extern "C" int HookIODoPlainVfscanf(FILE* AFile, const char* AFormat, va_list AArgs)
  __asm__("vfscanf");

extern "C" int HookIODoPlainVfscanf(FILE* AFile, const char* AFormat, va_list AArgs)
{
  return HookIODoVscan(AFile, GHookIODoRealVfscanf, "vfscanf", AFormat, AArgs);
}

extern "C" int __isoc99_vfscanf(FILE* AFile, const char* AFormat, va_list AArgs)
{
  return HookIODoVscan(AFile, GHookIODoRealIsoVfscanf, "__isoc99_vfscanf", AFormat, AArgs);
}

// stat by its plain symbol and stat64 (measured 2026-10-21: minizip's
// ioapi.h, read through CustomIO's header, defines glibc's
// __USE_FILE_OFFSET64 itself, so <sys/stat.h> here declares stat with the asm
// name stat64, while C objects such as raylib's call the plain stat; both
// symbols are defined, whatever the macro state). zig's glibc stub defines
// each in a static object of its own (libc_nonshared stat-2.32.o /
// stat64-2.32.o, one name each), so these replace them whole and, for a real
// path, call what they call: __xstat / __xstat64 with HookStatVersion.
static_assert(sizeof(struct stat) == sizeof(struct stat64), "x86_64: one stat layout");

extern "C" int HookIODoPlainStat(const char* APath, struct stat* ABuf) __asm__("stat");

extern "C" int HookIODoPlainStat(const char* APath, struct stat* ABuf)
{
  using TReal = int (*)(int, const char*, struct stat*);
  TReal LReal;
  int LResult;

  if (HookIODoStat(APath, ABuf, LResult))
    return LResult;
  LReal = reinterpret_cast<TReal>(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookReal(GHookIODoRealXstat, "__xstat"));
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return -1;
  }
  return LReal(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookStatVersion, APath, ABuf);
}

extern "C" int HookIODoStat64(const char* APath, struct stat64* ABuf) __asm__("stat64");

extern "C" int HookIODoStat64(const char* APath, struct stat64* ABuf)
{
  using TReal = int (*)(int, const char*, struct stat64*);
  TReal LReal;
  int LResult;

  if (HookIODoStat(APath, ABuf, LResult))
    return LResult;
  LReal = reinterpret_cast<TReal>(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookReal(GHookIODoRealXstat64,
    "__xstat64"));
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return -1;
  }
  return LReal(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookStatVersion, APath, ABuf);
}

#endif

// The CRTs' lock-free forms (glibc *_unlocked, ucrt *_nolock): a handle
// has no CRT lock (each call takes its stream lock), so each is its plain
// name on a handle; a real FILE goes to the CRT's own lock-free function.
// AName is the real function's name, ASlot its slot (HookReal fills it).
#define HOOKIO_DO_REAL(AType, AName) \
  static void* LSlot = nullptr; \
  AType LReal = reinterpret_cast<AType>(::pcpp_m_HookABI::HookReal(LSlot, AName))

#if defined(_WIN32)
#undef _getc_nolock
#undef _putc_nolock
#undef _getwc_nolock
#undef _putwc_nolock
#undef _fgetc_nolock
#undef _fputc_nolock
#undef _fgetwc_nolock
#undef _fputwc_nolock
#endif

#if defined(_WIN32)
extern "C" int _fgetc_nolock(FILE* AFile)
#else
extern "C" int fgetc_unlocked(FILE* AFile)
#endif
{
  using TReal = int (*)(FILE*);
  int LResult;

  if (HookIODoGetc(AFile, LResult))
    return LResult;
#if defined(_WIN32)
  HOOKIO_DO_REAL(TReal, "_fgetc_nolock");
#else
  HOOKIO_DO_REAL(TReal, "fgetc_unlocked");
#endif
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return EOF;
  }
  return LReal(AFile);
}

#if defined(_WIN32)
extern "C" int _getc_nolock(FILE* AFile)
#else
extern "C" int getc_unlocked(FILE* AFile)
#endif
{
  using TReal = int (*)(FILE*);
  int LResult;

  if (HookIODoGetc(AFile, LResult))
    return LResult;
#if defined(_WIN32)
  HOOKIO_DO_REAL(TReal, "_getc_nolock");
#else
  HOOKIO_DO_REAL(TReal, "getc_unlocked");
#endif
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return EOF;
  }
  return LReal(AFile);
}

#if defined(_WIN32)
extern "C" int _fputc_nolock(int AChar, FILE* AFile)
#else
extern "C" int fputc_unlocked(int AChar, FILE* AFile)
#endif
{
  using TReal = int (*)(int, FILE*);
  int LResult;

  if (HookIODoPutc(AChar, AFile, LResult))
    return LResult;
#if defined(_WIN32)
  HOOKIO_DO_REAL(TReal, "_fputc_nolock");
#else
  HOOKIO_DO_REAL(TReal, "fputc_unlocked");
#endif
  if (LReal == nullptr)
  {
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return EOF;
  }
  return LReal(AChar, AFile);
}

#if defined(_WIN32)
extern "C" int _putc_nolock(int AChar, FILE* AFile)
#else
extern "C" int putc_unlocked(int AChar, FILE* AFile)
#endif
{
  using TReal = int (*)(int, FILE*);
  int LResult;

  if (HookIODoPutc(AChar, AFile, LResult))
    return LResult;
#if defined(_WIN32)
